"end": 117.41999999999999, "text": " The lighting is perfect, the textures are totally photorealistic.", "tokens": [50717, 440, 9577, 307, 2176, 11, 264, 24501, 366, 3879, 2409, 418, 304, 3142, 13, 50888], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.106185896056039, "compression_ratio": 1.6537102473498233, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609850872496222e-12}, {"id": 39, "seek": 10696, "start": 117.5, "end": 118.86, "text": " You'd never know anything was wrong.", "tokens": [50892, 509, 1116, 1128, 458, 1340, 390, 2085, 13, 50960], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.106185896056039, "compression_ratio": 1.6537102473498233, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609850872496222e-12}, {"id": 40, "seek": 10696, "start": 118.91999999999999, "end": 122.36, "text": " Right, because the failure is completely invisible in a static moment.", "tokens": [50963, 1779, 11, 570, 264, 7763, 307, 2584, 14603, 294, 257, 13437, 1623, 13, 51135], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.106185896056039, "compression_ratio": 1.6537102473498233, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609850872496222e-12}, {"id": 41, "seek": 10696, "start": 123.0, "end": 128.38, "text": " The failure only exists in the temporal relationship, you know, the connection between the frames over time.", "tokens": [51167, 440, 7763, 787, 8198, 294, 264, 30881, 2480, 11, 291, 458, 11, 264, 4984, 1296, 264, 12083, 670, 565, 13, 51436], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.106185896056039, "compression_ratio": 1.6537102473498233, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609850872496222e-12}, {"id": 42, "seek": 10696, "start": 128.6, "end": 131.64, "text": " Because it's essentially a new universe every time you look away.", "tokens": [51447, 1436, 309, 311, 4476, 257, 777, 6445, 633, 565, 291, 574, 1314, 13, 51599], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.106185896056039, "compression_ratio": 1.6537102473498233, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609850872496222e-12}, {"id": 43, "seek": 13164, "start": 131.64, "end": 138.94, "text": " Exactly. You are interacting with a universe that is constantly forgetting and reinventing itself every single time you blink.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 509, 366, 18017, 365, 257, 6445, 300, 307, 6460, 25428, 293, 33477, 278, 2564, 633, 2167, 565, 291, 24667, 13, 50730], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1303601783254872, "compression_ratio": 1.5780590717299579, "no_speech_prob": 1.6743962986953687e-12}, {"id": 44, "seek": 13164, "start": 139.05999999999997, "end": 142.35999999999999, "text": " It's like a glitch in the matrix, but, you know, the deeply structural one.", "tokens": [50736, 467, 311, 411, 257, 23552, 294, 264, 8141, 11, 457, 11, 291, 458, 11, 264, 8760, 15067, 472, 13, 50901], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1303601783254872, "compression_ratio": 1.5780590717299579, "no_speech_prob": 1.6743962986953687e-12}, {"id": 45, "seek": 13164, "start": 142.42, "end": 142.61999999999998, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50904, 865, 13, 50914], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1303601783254872, "compression_ratio": 1.5780590717299579, "no_speech_prob": 1.6743962986953687e-12}, {"id": 46, "seek": 13164, "start": 142.95999999999998, "end": 145.83999999999997, "text": " We're literally looking at a landscape that shifts under our feet.", "tokens": [50931, 492, 434, 3736, 1237, 412, 257, 9661, 300, 19201, 833, 527, 3521, 13, 51075], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1303601783254872, "compression_ratio": 1.5780590717299579, "no_speech_prob": 1.6743962986953687e-12}, {"id": 47, "seek": 13164, "start": 146.67999999999998, "end": 149.82, "text": " And that is exactly what today's deep dive is all about.", "tokens": [51117, 400, 300, 307, 2293, 437, 965, 311, 2452, 9192, 307, 439, 466, 13, 51274], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1303601783254872, "compression_ratio": 1.5780590717299579, "no_speech_prob": 1.6743962986953687e-12}, {"id": 48, "seek": 13164, "start": 150.06, "end": 152.26, "text": " We're trying to solve this exact problem.", "tokens": [51286, 492, 434, 1382, 281, 5039, 341, 1900, 1154, 13, 51396], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1303601783254872, "compression_ratio": 1.5780590717299579, "no_speech_prob": 1.6743962986953687e-12}, {"id": 49, "seek": 15226, "start": 152.26, "end": 156.01999999999998, "text": " And we have some pretty heavy theoretical material to help us do that.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 321, 362, 512, 1238, 4676, 20864, 2527, 281, 854, 505, 360, 300, 13, 50553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14908977917262486, "compression_ratio": 1.4588744588744589, "no_speech_prob": 1.263917898293443e-12}, {"id": 50, "seek": 15226, "start": 156.1, "end": 156.42, "text": " We do.", "tokens": [50557, 492, 360, 13, 50573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14908977917262486, "compression_ratio": 1.4588744588744589, "no_speech_prob": 1.263917898293443e-12}, {"id": 51, "seek": 15226, "start": 156.66, "end": 164.54, "text": " We are exploring this really dense, highly mathematical, 2026 theoretical text by an independent researcher known as Fliction.", "tokens": [50585, 492, 366, 12736, 341, 534, 18011, 11, 5405, 18894, 11, 945, 10880, 20864, 2487, 538, 364, 6695, 21751, 2570, 382, 3235, 4105, 13, 50979], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14908977917262486, "compression_ratio": 1.4588744588744589, "no_speech_prob": 1.263917898293443e-12}, {"id": 52, "seek": 15226, "start": 165.04, "end": 165.26, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51004, 1779, 13, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14908977917262486, "compression_ratio": 1.4588744588744589, "no_speech_prob": 1.263917898293443e-12}, {"id": 53, "seek": 15226, "start": 165.34, "end": 170.32, "text": " The paper is titled Persistent Generative Worlds, a Field Theory of Semantic Simulation.", "tokens": [51019, 440, 3035, 307, 19841, 14006, 25367, 15409, 1166, 43003, 11, 257, 17952, 29009, 295, 14421, 7128, 3998, 2776, 13, 51268], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14908977917262486, "compression_ratio": 1.4588744588744589, "no_speech_prob": 1.263917898293443e-12}, {"id": 54, "seek": 15226, "start": 170.89999999999998, "end": 173.18, "text": " Such a mouthful, but so fascinating.", "tokens": [51297, 9653, 257, 4525, 906, 11, 457, 370, 10343, 13, 51411], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14908977917262486, "compression_ratio": 1.4588744588744589, "no_speech_prob": 1.263917898293443e-12}, {"id": 55, "seek": 17318, "start": 173.18, "end": 178.26000000000002, "text": " So our mission for you listening to this right now is to explore this radical blueprint.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 527, 4447, 337, 291, 4764, 281, 341, 558, 586, 307, 281, 6839, 341, 12001, 35868, 13, 50619], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11334073439888333, "compression_ratio": 1.6539682539682539, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482827251863453e-12}, {"id": 56, "seek": 17318, "start": 178.82, "end": 185.22, "text": " We want to understand how artificial intelligence can finally stop forgetting and start building persistent living realities.", "tokens": [50647, 492, 528, 281, 1223, 577, 11677, 7599, 393, 2721, 1590, 25428, 293, 722, 2390, 24315, 2647, 27785, 13, 50967], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11334073439888333, "compression_ratio": 1.6539682539682539, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482827251863453e-12}, {"id": 57, "seek": 17318, "start": 185.4, "end": 188.8, "text": " Because, frankly, the stakes here go way, way beyond just video games.", "tokens": [50976, 1436, 11, 11939, 11, 264, 28429, 510, 352, 636, 11, 636, 4399, 445, 960, 2813, 13, 51146], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11334073439888333, "compression_ratio": 1.6539682539682539, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482827251863453e-12}, {"id": 58, "seek": 17318, "start": 188.8, "end": 189.28, "text": " Oh, absolutely.", "tokens": [51146, 876, 11, 3122, 13, 51170], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11334073439888333, "compression_ratio": 1.6539682539682539, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482827251863453e-12}, {"id": 59, "seek": 17318, "start": 189.4, "end": 191.74, "text": " The video game wall is just an easy way to visualize it.", "tokens": [51176, 440, 960, 1216, 2929, 307, 445, 364, 1858, 636, 281, 23273, 309, 13, 51293], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11334073439888333, "compression_ratio": 1.6539682539682539, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482827251863453e-12}, {"id": 60, "seek": 17318, "start": 191.96, "end": 192.24, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51304, 1779, 13, 51318], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11334073439888333, "compression_ratio": 1.6539682539682539, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482827251863453e-12}, {"id": 61, "seek": 17318, "start": 192.9, "end": 202.9, "text": " That shifting wall in the courtyard is just a visual manifestation of a much deeper, like an ontological flaw in how current AI understands reality itself.", "tokens": [51351, 663, 17573, 2929, 294, 264, 41364, 307, 445, 257, 5056, 29550, 295, 257, 709, 7731, 11, 411, 364, 6592, 4383, 13717, 294, 577, 2190, 7318, 15146, 4103, 2564, 13, 51851], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11334073439888333, "compression_ratio": 1.6539682539682539, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482827251863453e-12}, {"id": 62, "seek": 20290, "start": 202.9, "end": 204.18, "text": " Yeah, you see it everywhere.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 11, 291, 536, 309, 5315, 13, 50429], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10945826656413528, "compression_ratio": 1.5703971119133573, "no_speech_prob": 2.2273335519712445e-12}, {"id": 63, "seek": 20290, "start": 204.4, "end": 205.14000000000001, "text": " You really do.", "tokens": [50440, 509, 534, 360, 13, 50477], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10945826656413528, "compression_ratio": 1.5703971119133573, "no_speech_prob": 2.2273335519712445e-12}, {"id": 64, "seek": 20290, "start": 205.3, "end": 208.8, "text": " You see this exact same architectural gap across the board.", "tokens": [50485, 509, 536, 341, 1900, 912, 26621, 7417, 2108, 264, 3150, 13, 50660], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10945826656413528, "compression_ratio": 1.5703971119133573, "no_speech_prob": 2.2273335519712445e-12}, {"id": 65, "seek": 20290, "start": 209.06, "end": 217.38, "text": " If you use a video generation model, it will subtly alter a person's facial structure across a camera cut.", "tokens": [50673, 759, 291, 764, 257, 960, 5125, 2316, 11, 309, 486, 7257, 356, 11337, 257, 954, 311, 15642, 3877, 2108, 257, 2799, 1723, 13, 51089], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10945826656413528, "compression_ratio": 1.5703971119133573, "no_speech_prob": 2.2273335519712445e-12}, {"id": 66, "seek": 20290, "start": 217.46, "end": 220.78, "text": " Like their nose gets slightly wider or their eye color shifts.", "tokens": [51093, 1743, 641, 6690, 2170, 4748, 11842, 420, 641, 3313, 2017, 19201, 13, 51259], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10945826656413528, "compression_ratio": 1.5703971119133573, "no_speech_prob": 2.2273335519712445e-12}, {"id": 67, "seek": 20290, "start": 220.86, "end": 221.38, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51263, 7587, 13, 51289], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10945826656413528, "compression_ratio": 1.5703971119133573, "no_speech_prob": 2.2273335519712445e-12}, {"id": 68, "seek": 20290, "start": 221.64000000000001, "end": 229.66, "text": " Or if you're interacting with a language model, it might confidently contradict a plot point that it established, you know, 30 pages earlier in a story.", "tokens": [51302, 1610, 498, 291, 434, 18017, 365, 257, 2856, 2316, 11, 309, 1062, 41956, 28900, 257, 7542, 935, 300, 309, 7545, 11, 291, 458, 11, 2217, 7183, 3071, 294, 257, 1657, 13, 51703], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10945826656413528, "compression_ratio": 1.5703971119133573, "no_speech_prob": 2.2273335519712445e-12}, {"id": 69, "seek": 22966, "start": 229.66, "end": 234.78, "text": " Or a chatbot acts like it's meeting you for the absolute first time, even though you've been talking for weeks.", "tokens": [50365, 1610, 257, 5081, 18870, 10672, 411, 309, 311, 3440, 291, 337, 264, 8236, 700, 565, 11, 754, 1673, 291, 600, 668, 1417, 337, 3259, 13, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11556561096854832, "compression_ratio": 1.5515873015873016, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484400650051967e-12}, {"id": 70, "seek": 22966, "start": 234.9, "end": 235.26, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50627, 1779, 13, 50645], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11556561096854832, "compression_ratio": 1.5515873015873016, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484400650051967e-12}, {"id": 71, "seek": 22966, "start": 235.42, "end": 241.76, "text": " The entire system is designed to produce an output that looks or sounds highly plausible right in that exact moment.", "tokens": [50653, 440, 2302, 1185, 307, 4761, 281, 5258, 364, 5598, 300, 1542, 420, 3263, 5405, 39925, 558, 294, 300, 1900, 1623, 13, 50970], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11556561096854832, "compression_ratio": 1.5515873015873016, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484400650051967e-12}, {"id": 72, "seek": 22966, "start": 242.07999999999998, "end": 243.14, "text": " But it has no memory.", "tokens": [50986, 583, 309, 575, 572, 4675, 13, 51039], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11556561096854832, "compression_ratio": 1.5515873015873016, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484400650051967e-12}, {"id": 73, "seek": 22966, "start": 243.51999999999998, "end": 243.76, "text": " None.", "tokens": [51058, 14492, 13, 51070], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11556561096854832, "compression_ratio": 1.5515873015873016, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484400650051967e-12}, {"id": 74, "seek": 22966, "start": 244.06, "end": 251.12, "text": " It possesses absolutely no mechanism to ensure that its output remains faithful to a continuous, persistent identity over time.", "tokens": [51085, 467, 17490, 279, 3122, 572, 7513, 281, 5586, 300, 1080, 5598, 7023, 17808, 281, 257, 10957, 11, 24315, 6575, 670, 565, 13, 51438], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11556561096854832, "compression_ratio": 1.5515873015873016, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484400650051967e-12}, {"id": 75, "seek": 25112, "start": 251.12, "end": 258.16, "text": " So to figure out how to build a true AI world, we basically have to look under the hood and kind of diagnose the disease first.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 281, 2573, 484, 577, 281, 1322, 257, 2074, 7318, 1002, 11, 321, 1936, 362, 281, 574, 833, 264, 13376, 293, 733, 295, 36238, 264, 4752, 700, 13, 50717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10759943911903783, "compression_ratio": 1.504201680672269, "no_speech_prob": 2.226885776474008e-12}, {"id": 76, "seek": 25112, "start": 258.34000000000003, "end": 258.76, "text": " We do.", "tokens": [50726, 492, 360, 13, 50747], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10759943911903783, "compression_ratio": 1.504201680672269, "no_speech_prob": 2.226885776474008e-12}, {"id": 77, "seek": 25112, "start": 259.08, "end": 265.88, "text": " Because why do these models, which are honestly so smart, they pass bar exams, they write complex code.", "tokens": [50763, 1436, 983, 360, 613, 5245, 11, 597, 366, 6095, 370, 4069, 11, 436, 1320, 2159, 20514, 11, 436, 2464, 3997, 3089, 13, 51103], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10759943911903783, "compression_ratio": 1.504201680672269, "no_speech_prob": 2.226885776474008e-12}, {"id": 78, "seek": 25112, "start": 266.04, "end": 266.26, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51111, 865, 13, 51122], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10759943911903783, "compression_ratio": 1.504201680672269, "no_speech_prob": 2.226885776474008e-12}, {"id": 79, "seek": 25112, "start": 266.76, "end": 271.3, "text": " Why do they fail so spectacularly at remembering a mossy rock?", "tokens": [51147, 1545, 360, 436, 3061, 370, 18149, 356, 412, 20719, 257, 36193, 88, 3727, 30, 51374], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10759943911903783, "compression_ratio": 1.504201680672269, "no_speech_prob": 2.226885776474008e-12}, {"id": 80, "seek": 25112, "start": 271.88, "end": 275.4, "text": " Like what is the actual mechanism of this amnesia?", "tokens": [51403, 1743, 437, 307, 264, 3539, 7513, 295, 341, 669, 4081, 654, 30, 51579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10759943911903783, "compression_ratio": 1.504201680672269, "no_speech_prob": 2.226885776474008e-12}, {"id": 81, "seek": 27540, "start": 275.4, "end": 280.0, "text": " Well, to answer that, we have to look at what these models are actually using in place of a world.", "tokens": [50365, 1042, 11, 281, 1867, 300, 11, 321, 362, 281, 574, 412, 437, 613, 5245, 366, 767, 1228, 294, 1081, 295, 257, 1002, 13, 50595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12708002543277877, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.399329762306889e-12}, {"id": 82, "seek": 27540, "start": 280.09999999999997, "end": 280.23999999999995, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50600, 1033, 13, 50607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12708002543277877, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.399329762306889e-12}, {"id": 83, "seek": 27540, "start": 280.32, "end": 280.79999999999995, "text": " What do they use?", "tokens": [50611, 708, 360, 436, 764, 30, 50635], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12708002543277877, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.399329762306889e-12}, {"id": 84, "seek": 27540, "start": 281.08, "end": 289.23999999999995, "text": " If you examine the underlying architecture of large language models or even diffusion models, you don't find a persistent environment anywhere in the code.", "tokens": [50649, 759, 291, 17496, 264, 14217, 9482, 295, 2416, 2856, 5245, 420, 754, 25242, 5245, 11, 291, 500, 380, 915, 257, 24315, 2823, 4992, 294, 264, 3089, 13, 51057], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12708002543277877, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.399329762306889e-12}, {"id": 85, "seek": 27540, "start": 289.35999999999996, "end": 289.58, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51063, 1779, 13, 51074], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12708002543277877, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.399329762306889e-12}, {"id": 86, "seek": 27540, "start": 289.73999999999995, "end": 291.82, "text": " What you find are context windows.", "tokens": [51082, 708, 291, 915, 366, 4319, 9309, 13, 51186], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12708002543277877, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.399329762306889e-12}, {"id": 87, "seek": 27540, "start": 292.02, "end": 293.15999999999997, "text": " You find hidden states.", "tokens": [51196, 509, 915, 7633, 4368, 13, 51253], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12708002543277877, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.399329762306889e-12}, {"id": 88, "seek": 27540, "start": 293.65999999999997, "end": 294.53999999999996, "text": " You find pashes.", "tokens": [51278, 509, 915, 280, 12808, 13, 51322], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12708002543277877, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.399329762306889e-12}, {"id": 89, "seek": 27540, "start": 294.79999999999995, "end": 297.62, "text": " But wait, aren't those just, you know, different forms of memory?", "tokens": [51335, 583, 1699, 11, 3212, 380, 729, 445, 11, 291, 458, 11, 819, 6422, 295, 4675, 30, 51476], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12708002543277877, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.399329762306889e-12}, {"id": 90, "seek": 27540, "start": 297.71999999999997, "end": 298.47999999999996, "text": " They're buffers.", "tokens": [51481, 814, 434, 9204, 433, 13, 51519], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12708002543277877, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.399329762306889e-12}, {"id": 91, "seek": 27540, "start": 298.78, "end": 302.56, "text": " And a buffer is fundamentally a completely different thing from a world.", "tokens": [51534, 400, 257, 21762, 307, 17879, 257, 2584, 819, 551, 490, 257, 1002, 13, 51723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12708002543277877, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.399329762306889e-12}, {"id": 92, "seek": 27540, "start": 302.88, "end": 303.32, "text": " How so?", "tokens": [51739, 1012, 370, 30, 51761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12708002543277877, "compression_ratio": 1.6666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.399329762306889e-12}, {"id": 93, "seek": 30332, "start": 303.32, "end": 306.88, "text": " A buffer only holds whatever happens to be near at hand, right?", "tokens": [50365, 316, 21762, 787, 9190, 2035, 2314, 281, 312, 2651, 412, 1011, 11, 558, 30, 50543], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15619845390319825, "compression_ratio": 1.5473684210526315, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552870627321246e-12}, {"id": 94, "seek": 30332, "start": 306.94, "end": 308.86, "text": " Whatever is actively being processed right now.", "tokens": [50546, 8541, 307, 13022, 885, 18846, 558, 586, 13, 50642], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15619845390319825, "compression_ratio": 1.5473684210526315, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552870627321246e-12}, {"id": 95, "seek": 30332, "start": 308.92, "end": 312.54, "text": " And it is heavily, heavily biased toward recency.", "tokens": [50645, 400, 309, 307, 10950, 11, 10950, 28035, 7361, 850, 3020, 13, 50826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15619845390319825, "compression_ratio": 1.5473684210526315, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552870627321246e-12}, {"id": 96, "seek": 30332, "start": 312.76, "end": 312.88, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50837, 1779, 13, 50843], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15619845390319825, "compression_ratio": 1.5473684210526315, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552870627321246e-12}, {"id": 97, "seek": 30332, "start": 312.92, "end": 315.14, "text": " So as new stuff comes in, the old stuff gets shoved out.", "tokens": [50845, 407, 382, 777, 1507, 1487, 294, 11, 264, 1331, 1507, 2170, 2223, 937, 484, 13, 50956], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15619845390319825, "compression_ratio": 1.5473684210526315, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552870627321246e-12}, {"id": 98, "seek": 30332, "start": 315.36, "end": 315.84, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50967, 7587, 13, 50991], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15619845390319825, "compression_ratio": 1.5473684210526315, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552870627321246e-12}, {"id": 99, "seek": 30332, "start": 316.2, "end": 320.06, "text": " As new information flows in, old information is pushed out.", "tokens": [51009, 1018, 777, 1589, 12867, 294, 11, 1331, 1589, 307, 9152, 484, 13, 51202], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15619845390319825, "compression_ratio": 1.5473684210526315, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552870627321246e-12}, {"id": 100, "seek": 32006, "start": 320.06, "end": 335.52, "text": " And from the perspective of the model, the AI operating inside that buffer, there's absolutely zero mathematical difference between a detail that was established 40,000 tokens ago and pushed out, and a detail that was simply never established in the first place.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 490, 264, 4585, 295, 264, 2316, 11, 264, 7318, 7447, 1854, 300, 21762, 11, 456, 311, 3122, 4018, 18894, 2649, 1296, 257, 2607, 300, 390, 7545, 3356, 11, 1360, 22667, 2057, 293, 9152, 484, 11, 293, 257, 2607, 300, 390, 2935, 1128, 7545, 294, 264, 700, 1081, 13, 51138], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0728292387039935, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879017714771516e-12}, {"id": 101, "seek": 32006, "start": 335.68, "end": 335.98, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51146, 3153, 13, 51161], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0728292387039935, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879017714771516e-12}, {"id": 102, "seek": 32006, "start": 336.24, "end": 336.46, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51174, 1033, 13, 51185], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0728292387039935, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879017714771516e-12}, {"id": 103, "seek": 33646, "start": 336.46, "end": 342.47999999999996, "text": " So once it leaves the buffer, it's reduced to the exact same status as things that literally don't exist.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 1564, 309, 5510, 264, 21762, 11, 309, 311, 9212, 281, 264, 1900, 912, 6558, 382, 721, 300, 3736, 500, 380, 2514, 13, 50666], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18359768644292304, "compression_ratio": 1.5210084033613445, "no_speech_prob": 1.432729911272912e-12}, {"id": 104, "seek": 33646, "start": 342.62, "end": 343.41999999999996, "text": " Non-existence.", "tokens": [50673, 8774, 12, 18217, 655, 13, 50713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18359768644292304, "compression_ratio": 1.5210084033613445, "no_speech_prob": 1.432729911272912e-12}, {"id": 105, "seek": 33646, "start": 343.52, "end": 343.78, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50718, 1079, 13, 50731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18359768644292304, "compression_ratio": 1.5210084033613445, "no_speech_prob": 1.432729911272912e-12}, {"id": 106, "seek": 33646, "start": 344.02, "end": 348.34, "text": " The author actually draws a really fascinating parallel here to developmental psychology.", "tokens": [50743, 440, 3793, 767, 20045, 257, 534, 10343, 8952, 510, 281, 30160, 15105, 13, 50959], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18359768644292304, "compression_ratio": 1.5210084033613445, "no_speech_prob": 1.432729911272912e-12}, {"id": 107, "seek": 33646, "start": 348.5, "end": 349.0, "text": " Oh, right.", "tokens": [50967, 876, 11, 558, 13, 50992], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18359768644292304, "compression_ratio": 1.5210084033613445, "no_speech_prob": 1.432729911272912e-12}, {"id": 108, "seek": 33646, "start": 349.24, "end": 351.09999999999997, "text": " But we should probably caveat this.", "tokens": [51004, 583, 321, 820, 1391, 43012, 341, 13, 51097], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18359768644292304, "compression_ratio": 1.5210084033613445, "no_speech_prob": 1.432729911272912e-12}, {"id": 109, "seek": 33646, "start": 351.7, "end": 353.91999999999996, "text": " They're applying this strictly to the architecture, right?", "tokens": [51127, 814, 434, 9275, 341, 20792, 281, 264, 9482, 11, 558, 30, 51238], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18359768644292304, "compression_ratio": 1.5210084033613445, "no_speech_prob": 1.432729911272912e-12}, {"id": 110, "seek": 33646, "start": 353.91999999999996, "end": 354.03999999999996, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51238, 1779, 13, 51244], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18359768644292304, "compression_ratio": 1.5210084033613445, "no_speech_prob": 1.432729911272912e-12}, {"id": 111, "seek": 33646, "start": 354.03999999999996, "end": 355.9, "text": " Not claiming the AI is conscious.", "tokens": [51244, 1726, 19232, 264, 7318, 307, 6648, 13, 51337], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18359768644292304, "compression_ratio": 1.5210084033613445, "no_speech_prob": 1.432729911272912e-12}, {"id": 112, "seek": 35590, "start": 356.28, "end": 356.67999999999995, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50384, 7587, 13, 50404], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15730045522962297, "compression_ratio": 1.5145985401459854, "no_speech_prob": 1.2840971775479604e-12}, {"id": 113, "seek": 35590, "start": 356.88, "end": 358.88, "text": " We are absolutely not saying AI has a mind.", "tokens": [50414, 492, 366, 3122, 406, 1566, 7318, 575, 257, 1575, 13, 50514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15730045522962297, "compression_ratio": 1.5145985401459854, "no_speech_prob": 1.2840971775479604e-12}, {"id": 114, "seek": 35590, "start": 359.2, "end": 362.96, "text": " But structurally, the text brings up the concept of object permanence.", "tokens": [50530, 583, 6594, 6512, 11, 264, 2487, 5607, 493, 264, 3410, 295, 2657, 8105, 655, 13, 50718], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15730045522962297, "compression_ratio": 1.5145985401459854, "no_speech_prob": 1.2840971775479604e-12}, {"id": 115, "seek": 35590, "start": 362.97999999999996, "end": 365.26, "text": " Like that classic test they do with human infants, right?", "tokens": [50719, 1743, 300, 7230, 1500, 436, 360, 365, 1952, 38829, 11, 558, 30, 50833], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15730045522962297, "compression_ratio": 1.5145985401459854, "no_speech_prob": 1.2840971775479604e-12}, {"id": 116, "seek": 35590, "start": 365.79999999999995, "end": 367.23999999999995, "text": " Where you hide a toy under a blanket.", "tokens": [50860, 2305, 291, 6479, 257, 12058, 833, 257, 17907, 13, 50932], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15730045522962297, "compression_ratio": 1.5145985401459854, "no_speech_prob": 1.2840971775479604e-12}, {"id": 117, "seek": 35590, "start": 367.52, "end": 368.29999999999995, "text": " Precisely that.", "tokens": [50946, 48746, 736, 300, 13, 50985], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15730045522962297, "compression_ratio": 1.5145985401459854, "no_speech_prob": 1.2840971775479604e-12}, {"id": 118, "seek": 35590, "start": 368.47999999999996, "end": 376.52, "text": " So for the first 8 to 12 months of human development, an infant acts as if a toy hidden under a cloth has just ceased to exist in the universe.", "tokens": [50994, 407, 337, 264, 700, 1649, 281, 2272, 2493, 295, 1952, 3250, 11, 364, 16757, 10672, 382, 498, 257, 12058, 7633, 833, 257, 13619, 575, 445, 49917, 281, 2514, 294, 264, 6445, 13, 51396], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15730045522962297, "compression_ratio": 1.5145985401459854, "no_speech_prob": 1.2840971775479604e-12}, {"id": 119, "seek": 35590, "start": 376.88, "end": 378.38, "text": " They don't even try to look for it.", "tokens": [51414, 814, 500, 380, 754, 853, 281, 574, 337, 309, 13, 51489], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15730045522962297, "compression_ratio": 1.5145985401459854, "no_speech_prob": 1.2840971775479604e-12}, {"id": 120, "seek": 37838, "start": 378.38, "end": 388.46, "text": " Right, because their cognitive architecture hasn't yet developed the capacity to represent an unobserved object as maintaining a continuous existence.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 11, 570, 641, 15605, 9482, 6132, 380, 1939, 4743, 264, 6042, 281, 2906, 364, 8526, 929, 6913, 2657, 382, 14916, 257, 10957, 9123, 13, 50869], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16258594152089711, "compression_ratio": 1.5159817351598173, "no_speech_prob": 1.536847146939302e-12}, {"id": 121, "seek": 37838, "start": 388.62, "end": 390.36, "text": " Out of sight, literally out of reality.", "tokens": [50877, 5925, 295, 7860, 11, 3736, 484, 295, 4103, 13, 50964], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16258594152089711, "compression_ratio": 1.5159817351598173, "no_speech_prob": 1.536847146939302e-12}, {"id": 122, "seek": 37838, "start": 390.52, "end": 390.82, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50972, 1079, 13, 50987], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16258594152089711, "compression_ratio": 1.5159817351598173, "no_speech_prob": 1.536847146939302e-12}, {"id": 123, "seek": 37838, "start": 391.36, "end": 396.96, "text": " And structurally, mathematically, these AI models behave identically to that infant.", "tokens": [51014, 400, 6594, 6512, 11, 44003, 11, 613, 7318, 5245, 15158, 2473, 984, 281, 300, 16757, 13, 51294], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16258594152089711, "compression_ratio": 1.5159817351598173, "no_speech_prob": 1.536847146939302e-12}, {"id": 124, "seek": 37838, "start": 397.21999999999997, "end": 400.38, "text": " They treat out of sight objects as completely void.", "tokens": [51307, 814, 2387, 484, 295, 7860, 6565, 382, 2584, 22009, 13, 51465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16258594152089711, "compression_ratio": 1.5159817351598173, "no_speech_prob": 1.536847146939302e-12}, {"id": 125, "seek": 40038, "start": 400.38, "end": 409.38, "text": " So every single time the AI generates a new frame, or like a new paragraph, it's basically restarting its developmental stage from zero.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 633, 2167, 565, 264, 7318, 23815, 257, 777, 3920, 11, 420, 411, 257, 777, 18865, 11, 309, 311, 1936, 21022, 278, 1080, 30160, 3233, 490, 4018, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12987886293969972, "compression_ratio": 1.5776892430278884, "no_speech_prob": 1.8686109517357385e-12}, {"id": 126, "seek": 40038, "start": 409.58, "end": 412.65999999999997, "text": " It's looking at a brand new universe every single time.", "tokens": [50825, 467, 311, 1237, 412, 257, 3360, 777, 6445, 633, 2167, 565, 13, 50979], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12987886293969972, "compression_ratio": 1.5776892430278884, "no_speech_prob": 1.8686109517357385e-12}, {"id": 127, "seek": 40038, "start": 412.71999999999997, "end": 413.3, "text": " Okay, but wait.", "tokens": [50982, 1033, 11, 457, 1699, 13, 51011], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12987886293969972, "compression_ratio": 1.5776892430278884, "no_speech_prob": 1.8686109517357385e-12}, {"id": 128, "seek": 40038, "start": 413.5, "end": 421.1, "text": " I have to challenge this premise just a bit, because I know the tech industry is spending, like, billions of dollars right now trying to fix this exact issue.", "tokens": [51021, 286, 362, 281, 3430, 341, 22045, 445, 257, 857, 11, 570, 286, 458, 264, 7553, 3518, 307, 6434, 11, 411, 11, 17375, 295, 3808, 558, 586, 1382, 281, 3191, 341, 1900, 2734, 13, 51401], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12987886293969972, "compression_ratio": 1.5776892430278884, "no_speech_prob": 1.8686109517357385e-12}, {"id": 129, "seek": 40038, "start": 421.15999999999997, "end": 422.14, "text": " They are, definitely.", "tokens": [51404, 814, 366, 11, 2138, 13, 51453], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12987886293969972, "compression_ratio": 1.5776892430278884, "no_speech_prob": 1.8686109517357385e-12}, {"id": 130, "seek": 40038, "start": 422.26, "end": 422.4, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51459, 1779, 13, 51466], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12987886293969972, "compression_ratio": 1.5776892430278884, "no_speech_prob": 1.8686109517357385e-12}, {"id": 131, "seek": 42240, "start": 422.4, "end": 428.78, "text": " So if the buffer is too small, isn't the brute force answer to just make the context window massive, which they are doing.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 498, 264, 21762, 307, 886, 1359, 11, 1943, 380, 264, 47909, 3464, 1867, 281, 445, 652, 264, 4319, 4910, 5994, 11, 597, 436, 366, 884, 13, 50684], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14471274614334106, "compression_ratio": 1.6006493506493507, "no_speech_prob": 1.3096278618854318e-12}, {"id": 132, "seek": 42240, "start": 428.85999999999996, "end": 430.71999999999997, "text": " We're seeing millions of tokens now.", "tokens": [50688, 492, 434, 2577, 6803, 295, 22667, 586, 13, 50781], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14471274614334106, "compression_ratio": 1.6006493506493507, "no_speech_prob": 1.3096278618854318e-12}, {"id": 133, "seek": 42240, "start": 431.23999999999995, "end": 434.73999999999995, "text": " And beyond that, they're using retrieval augmented generation, or RAG.", "tokens": [50807, 400, 4399, 300, 11, 436, 434, 1228, 19817, 3337, 36155, 5125, 11, 420, 14626, 38, 13, 50982], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14471274614334106, "compression_ratio": 1.6006493506493507, "no_speech_prob": 1.3096278618854318e-12}, {"id": 134, "seek": 42240, "start": 434.84, "end": 436.09999999999997, "text": " I mean, we hear about RAG constantly.", "tokens": [50987, 286, 914, 11, 321, 1568, 466, 14626, 38, 6460, 13, 51050], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14471274614334106, "compression_ratio": 1.6006493506493507, "no_speech_prob": 1.3096278618854318e-12}, {"id": 135, "seek": 42240, "start": 436.2, "end": 437.46, "text": " That's the industry standard right now.", "tokens": [51055, 663, 311, 264, 3518, 3832, 558, 586, 13, 51118], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14471274614334106, "compression_ratio": 1.6006493506493507, "no_speech_prob": 1.3096278618854318e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 42240, "start": 437.73999999999995, "end": 437.96, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51132, 865, 13, 51143], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14471274614334106, "compression_ratio": 1.6006493506493507, "no_speech_prob": 1.3096278618854318e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 42240, "start": 438.4, "end": 443.52, "text": " You hook the AI up to a massive vector database so it can search for its own memories.", "tokens": [51165, 509, 6328, 264, 7318, 493, 281, 257, 5994, 8062, 8149, 370, 309, 393, 3164, 337, 1080, 1065, 8495, 13, 51421], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14471274614334106, "compression_ratio": 1.6006493506493507, "no_speech_prob": 1.3096278618854318e-12}, {"id": 138, "seek": 42240, "start": 444.12, "end": 444.26, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51451, 865, 13, 51458], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14471274614334106, "compression_ratio": 1.6006493506493507, "no_speech_prob": 1.3096278618854318e-12}, {"id": 139, "seek": 42240, "start": 444.26, "end": 449.73999999999995, "text": " So why doesn't a massive memory database solve this infant object permanence problem?", "tokens": [51458, 407, 983, 1177, 380, 257, 5994, 4675, 8149, 5039, 341, 16757, 2657, 8105, 655, 1154, 30, 51732], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14471274614334106, "compression_ratio": 1.6006493506493507, "no_speech_prob": 1.3096278618854318e-12}, {"id": 140, "seek": 44974, "start": 449.74, "end": 456.36, "text": " It's a really intuitive engineering objection, and like you said, standard industry practice currently relies heavily on R.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 257, 534, 21769, 7043, 35756, 11, 293, 411, 291, 848, 11, 3832, 3518, 3124, 4362, 30910, 10950, 322, 497, 13, 50696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13971047342559437, "compression_ratio": 1.5560344827586208, "no_speech_prob": 1.1422813649825114e-12}, {"id": 141, "seek": 44974, "start": 456.68, "end": 456.90000000000003, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50712, 1779, 13, 50723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13971047342559437, "compression_ratio": 1.5560344827586208, "no_speech_prob": 1.1422813649825114e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 44974, "start": 457.12, "end": 459.8, "text": " You pair your generative model with a vector database.", "tokens": [50734, 509, 6119, 428, 1337, 1166, 2316, 365, 257, 8062, 8149, 13, 50868], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13971047342559437, "compression_ratio": 1.5560344827586208, "no_speech_prob": 1.1422813649825114e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 44974, "start": 459.8, "end": 467.82, "text": " When the model needs to generate something, it searches the database, retrieves relevant notes, and feeds them back into its active context window.", "tokens": [50868, 1133, 264, 2316, 2203, 281, 8460, 746, 11, 309, 26701, 264, 8149, 11, 19817, 977, 7340, 5570, 11, 293, 23712, 552, 646, 666, 1080, 4967, 4319, 4910, 13, 51269], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13971047342559437, "compression_ratio": 1.5560344827586208, "no_speech_prob": 1.1422813649825114e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 44974, "start": 467.94, "end": 468.8, "text": " Sounds like it should work.", "tokens": [51275, 14576, 411, 309, 820, 589, 13, 51318], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13971047342559437, "compression_ratio": 1.5560344827586208, "no_speech_prob": 1.1422813649825114e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 46880, "start": 468.8, "end": 475.06, "text": " And it does measurably improve performance for certain things, like, you know, answering questions about a specific PDF manual.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 309, 775, 5731, 374, 1188, 3470, 3389, 337, 1629, 721, 11, 411, 11, 291, 458, 11, 13430, 1651, 466, 257, 2685, 17752, 9688, 13, 50678], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13932117961701893, "compression_ratio": 1.5040650406504066, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327296944324774e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 46880, "start": 475.76, "end": 484.14, "text": " But the text argues it completely fails to solve the ontological problem of a persistent world, because a retrieval system stores documents.", "tokens": [50713, 583, 264, 2487, 38218, 309, 2584, 18199, 281, 5039, 264, 6592, 4383, 1154, 295, 257, 24315, 1002, 11, 570, 257, 19817, 3337, 1185, 9512, 8512, 13, 51132], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13932117961701893, "compression_ratio": 1.5040650406504066, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327296944324774e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 46880, "start": 484.38, "end": 487.18, "text": " It does not represent a unified state of reality.", "tokens": [51144, 467, 775, 406, 2906, 257, 26787, 1785, 295, 4103, 13, 51284], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13932117961701893, "compression_ratio": 1.5040650406504066, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327296944324774e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 46880, "start": 487.58000000000004, "end": 487.86, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51304, 1033, 13, 51318], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13932117961701893, "compression_ratio": 1.5040650406504066, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327296944324774e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 46880, "start": 487.98, "end": 489.88, "text": " We need to dive deeper into that distinction.", "tokens": [51324, 492, 643, 281, 9192, 7731, 666, 300, 16844, 13, 51419], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13932117961701893, "compression_ratio": 1.5040650406504066, "no_speech_prob": 1.4327296944324774e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 48988, "start": 489.88, "end": 493.71999999999997, "text": " A database of documents versus an actual world.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 8149, 295, 8512, 5717, 364, 3539, 1002, 13, 50557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15147111853774714, "compression_ratio": 1.6270491803278688, "no_speech_prob": 1.42727203753662e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 48988, "start": 493.98, "end": 499.48, "text": " Because if the database has a record of everything that happened in the courtyard, why isn't that a world?", "tokens": [50570, 1436, 498, 264, 8149, 575, 257, 2136, 295, 1203, 300, 2011, 294, 264, 41364, 11, 983, 1943, 380, 300, 257, 1002, 30, 50845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15147111853774714, "compression_ratio": 1.6270491803278688, "no_speech_prob": 1.42727203753662e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 48988, "start": 499.9, "end": 509.44, "text": " Well, the text outlines three structural, unavoidable failures of document stores that prove they can never really simulate a persistent reality.", "tokens": [50866, 1042, 11, 264, 2487, 40125, 1045, 15067, 11, 36541, 17079, 712, 20774, 295, 4166, 9512, 300, 7081, 436, 393, 1128, 534, 27817, 257, 24315, 4103, 13, 51343], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15147111853774714, "compression_ratio": 1.6270491803278688, "no_speech_prob": 1.42727203753662e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 48988, "start": 509.78, "end": 510.06, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51360, 1033, 13, 51374], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15147111853774714, "compression_ratio": 1.6270491803278688, "no_speech_prob": 1.42727203753662e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 48988, "start": 510.28, "end": 510.62, "text": " Hit me.", "tokens": [51385, 9217, 385, 13, 51402], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15147111853774714, "compression_ratio": 1.6270491803278688, "no_speech_prob": 1.42727203753662e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 48988, "start": 510.71999999999997, "end": 511.71999999999997, "text": " What's the first failure?", "tokens": [51407, 708, 311, 264, 700, 7763, 30, 51457], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15147111853774714, "compression_ratio": 1.6270491803278688, "no_speech_prob": 1.42727203753662e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 48988, "start": 512.18, "end": 514.94, "text": " The first failure is that writing is optional.", "tokens": [51480, 440, 700, 7763, 307, 300, 3579, 307, 17312, 13, 51618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15147111853774714, "compression_ratio": 1.6270491803278688, "no_speech_prob": 1.42727203753662e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 48988, "start": 515.24, "end": 515.7, "text": " Optional?", "tokens": [51633, 29284, 304, 30, 51656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15147111853774714, "compression_ratio": 1.6270491803278688, "no_speech_prob": 1.42727203753662e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 51570, "start": 515.7, "end": 516.1400000000001, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13280853629112244, "compression_ratio": 1.6419753086419753, "no_speech_prob": 1.2694459199102948e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 51570, "start": 516.7800000000001, "end": 524.9000000000001, "text": " The architecture of a generative model paired with a database doesn't mathematically force the AI to document every single change in state.", "tokens": [50419, 440, 9482, 295, 257, 1337, 1166, 2316, 25699, 365, 257, 8149, 1177, 380, 44003, 3464, 264, 7318, 281, 4166, 633, 2167, 1319, 294, 1785, 13, 50825], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13280853629112244, "compression_ratio": 1.6419753086419753, "no_speech_prob": 1.2694459199102948e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 51570, "start": 525.1600000000001, "end": 526.0200000000001, "text": " Ah, I see.", "tokens": [50838, 2438, 11, 286, 536, 13, 50881], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13280853629112244, "compression_ratio": 1.6419753086419753, "no_speech_prob": 1.2694459199102948e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 51570, "start": 526.2800000000001, "end": 529.8000000000001, "text": " Writing a note to the database is just another behavior.", "tokens": [50894, 32774, 257, 3637, 281, 264, 8149, 307, 445, 1071, 5223, 13, 51070], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13280853629112244, "compression_ratio": 1.6419753086419753, "no_speech_prob": 1.2694459199102948e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 51570, "start": 530.0200000000001, "end": 534.5, "text": " It's just another sequence of tokens that the model might or might not choose to generate.", "tokens": [51081, 467, 311, 445, 1071, 8310, 295, 22667, 300, 264, 2316, 1062, 420, 1062, 406, 2826, 281, 8460, 13, 51305], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13280853629112244, "compression_ratio": 1.6419753086419753, "no_speech_prob": 1.2694459199102948e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 51570, "start": 534.72, "end": 540.0400000000001, "text": " So when the AI generates the crack in the wall, it might trigger a function to write that down.", "tokens": [51316, 407, 562, 264, 7318, 23815, 264, 6226, 294, 264, 2929, 11, 309, 1062, 7875, 257, 2445, 281, 2464, 300, 760, 13, 51582], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13280853629112244, "compression_ratio": 1.6419753086419753, "no_speech_prob": 1.2694459199102948e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 54004, "start": 540.04, "end": 546.3199999999999, "text": " Or it might just generate the image of the crack and move right on to generating the fountain, leaving literally no record behind at all.", "tokens": [50365, 1610, 309, 1062, 445, 8460, 264, 3256, 295, 264, 6226, 293, 1286, 558, 322, 281, 17746, 264, 29451, 11, 5012, 3736, 572, 2136, 2261, 412, 439, 13, 50679], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10055187543233236, "compression_ratio": 1.6732673267326732, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488017548499379e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 54004, "start": 546.48, "end": 546.92, "text": " Oh, man.", "tokens": [50687, 876, 11, 587, 13, 50709], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10055187543233236, "compression_ratio": 1.6732673267326732, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488017548499379e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 54004, "start": 547.0, "end": 553.0, "text": " That reminds me of, like, relying on a tired coworker to take perfect meeting notes every single day.", "tokens": [50713, 663, 12025, 385, 295, 11, 411, 11, 24140, 322, 257, 5868, 31998, 260, 281, 747, 2176, 3440, 5570, 633, 2167, 786, 13, 51013], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10055187543233236, "compression_ratio": 1.6732673267326732, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488017548499379e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 54004, "start": 553.0999999999999, "end": 554.4399999999999, "text": " That is a perfect analogy.", "tokens": [51018, 663, 307, 257, 2176, 21663, 13, 51085], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10055187543233236, "compression_ratio": 1.6732673267326732, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488017548499379e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 54004, "start": 554.8, "end": 554.98, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51103, 1779, 13, 51112], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10055187543233236, "compression_ratio": 1.6732673267326732, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488017548499379e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 54004, "start": 555.04, "end": 562.38, "text": " Because sometimes they're going to capture all the action items perfectly, and sometimes they just zone out and forget to write down the most crucial decision we made.", "tokens": [51115, 1436, 2171, 436, 434, 516, 281, 7983, 439, 264, 3069, 4754, 6239, 11, 293, 2171, 436, 445, 6668, 484, 293, 2870, 281, 2464, 760, 264, 881, 11462, 3537, 321, 1027, 13, 51482], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10055187543233236, "compression_ratio": 1.6732673267326732, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488017548499379e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 54004, "start": 562.5999999999999, "end": 565.9399999999999, "text": " You can't build a reliable history on an optional habit.", "tokens": [51493, 509, 393, 380, 1322, 257, 12924, 2503, 322, 364, 17312, 7164, 13, 51660], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10055187543233236, "compression_ratio": 1.6732673267326732, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488017548499379e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 56594, "start": 565.94, "end": 571.5400000000001, "text": " Exactly. And that leads to the second structural failure, which is that retrieval is approximate.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 400, 300, 6689, 281, 264, 1150, 15067, 7763, 11, 597, 307, 300, 19817, 3337, 307, 30874, 13, 50645], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12526016720270705, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.2842930928805285e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 56594, "start": 571.96, "end": 574.08, "text": " Approximate. Meaning it's not exact.", "tokens": [50666, 29551, 87, 2905, 13, 19948, 309, 311, 406, 1900, 13, 50772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12526016720270705, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.2842930928805285e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 56594, "start": 574.22, "end": 577.8800000000001, "text": " Right. Vector databases use what's called similarity search.", "tokens": [50779, 1779, 13, 691, 20814, 22380, 764, 437, 311, 1219, 32194, 3164, 13, 50962], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12526016720270705, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.2842930928805285e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 56594, "start": 578.3800000000001, "end": 585.0, "text": " They map queries and documents into this high-dimensional space, and they look for things that are mathematically close to each other.", "tokens": [50987, 814, 4471, 24109, 293, 8512, 666, 341, 1090, 12, 18759, 1901, 11, 293, 436, 574, 337, 721, 300, 366, 44003, 1998, 281, 1184, 661, 13, 51318], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12526016720270705, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.2842930928805285e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 56594, "start": 585.1600000000001, "end": 586.98, "text": " So they're looking for semantic relevance.", "tokens": [51326, 407, 436, 434, 1237, 337, 47982, 32684, 13, 51417], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12526016720270705, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.2842930928805285e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 56594, "start": 587.1800000000001, "end": 594.7, "text": " Yes. So if your camera pans back to the wall, the system might query the database for Stonewall in Courtyard.", "tokens": [51427, 1079, 13, 407, 498, 428, 2799, 32905, 646, 281, 264, 2929, 11, 264, 1185, 1062, 14581, 264, 8149, 337, 15012, 16256, 294, 6413, 37041, 13, 51803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12526016720270705, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.2842930928805285e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 56594, "start": 594.7800000000001, "end": 595.3000000000001, "text": " Makes sense.", "tokens": [51807, 25245, 2020, 13, 51833], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12526016720270705, "compression_ratio": 1.631578947368421, "no_speech_prob": 1.2842930928805285e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 59530, "start": 595.3, "end": 602.9599999999999, "text": " But what if the database is crowded with descriptions of other walls? Or what if the query is worded slightly differently this time?", "tokens": [50365, 583, 437, 498, 264, 8149, 307, 21634, 365, 24406, 295, 661, 7920, 30, 1610, 437, 498, 264, 14581, 307, 1349, 292, 4748, 7614, 341, 565, 30, 50748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11044388210650571, "compression_ratio": 1.7378277153558053, "no_speech_prob": 1.883236839042568e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 59530, "start": 603.02, "end": 604.26, "text": " It might pull the wrong note.", "tokens": [50751, 467, 1062, 2235, 264, 2085, 3637, 13, 50813], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11044388210650571, "compression_ratio": 1.7378277153558053, "no_speech_prob": 1.883236839042568e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 59530, "start": 604.74, "end": 611.8599999999999, "text": " Exactly. The similarity search might pull the description of the wrong wall or a wall from a completely different courtyard.", "tokens": [50837, 7587, 13, 440, 32194, 3164, 1062, 2235, 264, 3855, 295, 264, 2085, 2929, 420, 257, 2929, 490, 257, 2584, 819, 41364, 13, 51193], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11044388210650571, "compression_ratio": 1.7378277153558053, "no_speech_prob": 1.883236839042568e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 59530, "start": 612.4, "end": 622.06, "text": " It guarantees that you pull something relevant, but it absolutely cannot guarantee that you pull the single, positively-correct prior fact of that specific coordinate in space.", "tokens": [51220, 467, 32567, 300, 291, 2235, 746, 7340, 11, 457, 309, 3122, 2644, 10815, 300, 291, 2235, 264, 2167, 11, 25795, 12, 19558, 2554, 4059, 1186, 295, 300, 2685, 15670, 294, 1901, 13, 51703], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11044388210650571, "compression_ratio": 1.7378277153558053, "no_speech_prob": 1.883236839042568e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 62206, "start": 622.06, "end": 629.7199999999999, "text": " So it's basically searching for a general vibe rather than locking onto an objective, unchangeable coordinate.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 309, 311, 1936, 10808, 337, 257, 2674, 14606, 2831, 813, 23954, 3911, 364, 10024, 11, 517, 15431, 712, 15670, 13, 50748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14305906295776366, "compression_ratio": 1.1702127659574468, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947617354629019e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 62972, "start": 629.72, "end": 637.38, "text": " Exactly right. And then there's the third failure, which honestly is the most fatal of all. Reconciliation is absent.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 558, 13, 400, 550, 456, 311, 264, 2636, 7763, 11, 597, 6095, 307, 264, 881, 24069, 295, 439, 13, 1300, 1671, 27870, 307, 25185, 13, 50748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.060915319124857585, "compression_ratio": 1.1470588235294117, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747661200564035e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 63738, "start": 637.38, "end": 639.16, "text": " Meaning it can't resolve conflicts.", "tokens": [50365, 19948, 309, 393, 380, 14151, 19807, 13, 50454], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1376328882963761, "compression_ratio": 1.25, "no_speech_prob": 1.3830220605901e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 63738, "start": 639.3, "end": 646.04, "text": " Right. Imagine the system miraculously succeeds at the first two steps. It writes down the crack in the wall perfectly.", "tokens": [50461, 1779, 13, 11739, 264, 1185, 30686, 25038, 49263, 412, 264, 700, 732, 4439, 13, 467, 13657, 760, 264, 6226, 294, 264, 2929, 6239, 13, 50798], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1376328882963761, "compression_ratio": 1.25, "no_speech_prob": 1.3830220605901e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 63738, "start": 646.2, "end": 647.16, "text": " Okay. Good job, AI.", "tokens": [50806, 1033, 13, 2205, 1691, 11, 7318, 13, 50854], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1376328882963761, "compression_ratio": 1.25, "no_speech_prob": 1.3830220605901e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 64716, "start": 647.16, "end": 656.5799999999999, "text": " But then later, an event happens in the simulation. Let's say a cart crashes into the wall. The AI generates a new note and writes it to the database.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 550, 1780, 11, 364, 2280, 2314, 294, 264, 16575, 13, 961, 311, 584, 257, 5467, 28642, 666, 264, 2929, 13, 440, 7318, 23815, 257, 777, 3637, 293, 13657, 309, 281, 264, 8149, 13, 50836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11006932355919663, "compression_ratio": 1.592741935483871, "no_speech_prob": 2.5042253427171035e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 64716, "start": 656.98, "end": 660.8399999999999, "text": " The wall has a massive hole in it, and the old crack has spiderwebbed.", "tokens": [50856, 440, 2929, 575, 257, 5994, 5458, 294, 309, 11, 293, 264, 1331, 6226, 575, 17614, 826, 65, 2883, 13, 51049], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11006932355919663, "compression_ratio": 1.592741935483871, "no_speech_prob": 2.5042253427171035e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 64716, "start": 661.16, "end": 662.86, "text": " Okay, so now we have an updated note.", "tokens": [51065, 1033, 11, 370, 586, 321, 362, 364, 10588, 3637, 13, 51150], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11006932355919663, "compression_ratio": 1.592741935483871, "no_speech_prob": 2.5042253427171035e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 64716, "start": 662.92, "end": 670.3399999999999, "text": " But you still have the old note, too. Now your vector database contains two completely conflicting documents about the exact same wall.", "tokens": [51153, 583, 291, 920, 362, 264, 1331, 3637, 11, 886, 13, 823, 428, 8062, 8149, 8306, 732, 2584, 43784, 8512, 466, 264, 1900, 912, 2929, 13, 51524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11006932355919663, "compression_ratio": 1.592741935483871, "no_speech_prob": 2.5042253427171035e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 67034, "start": 670.34, "end": 672.4200000000001, "text": " Oh. They didn't overwrite the first one.", "tokens": [50365, 876, 13, 814, 994, 380, 670, 21561, 264, 700, 472, 13, 50469], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10258222509313512, "compression_ratio": 1.8104575163398693, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691437507669217e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 67034, "start": 672.5600000000001, "end": 681.1800000000001, "text": " No, because the architecture of a document store has no automatic mechanism to force the old note to be revised, overwritten, or deleted based on the new one.", "tokens": [50476, 883, 11, 570, 264, 9482, 295, 257, 4166, 3531, 575, 572, 12509, 7513, 281, 3464, 264, 1331, 3637, 281, 312, 35228, 11, 670, 26859, 11, 420, 22981, 2361, 322, 264, 777, 472, 13, 50907], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10258222509313512, "compression_ratio": 1.8104575163398693, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691437507669217e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 67034, "start": 681.2800000000001, "end": 682.86, "text": " They both just sit there in the archive.", "tokens": [50912, 814, 1293, 445, 1394, 456, 294, 264, 23507, 13, 50991], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10258222509313512, "compression_ratio": 1.8104575163398693, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691437507669217e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 67034, "start": 683.02, "end": 685.6600000000001, "text": " Which means the next time the system queries the wall.", "tokens": [50999, 3013, 1355, 264, 958, 565, 264, 1185, 24109, 264, 2929, 13, 51131], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10258222509313512, "compression_ratio": 1.8104575163398693, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691437507669217e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 67034, "start": 685.88, "end": 689.9200000000001, "text": " It might pull the note about the small crack. It might pull the note about the massive hole.", "tokens": [51142, 467, 1062, 2235, 264, 3637, 466, 264, 1359, 6226, 13, 467, 1062, 2235, 264, 3637, 466, 264, 5994, 5458, 13, 51344], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10258222509313512, "compression_ratio": 1.8104575163398693, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691437507669217e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 67034, "start": 690.12, "end": 694.82, "text": " Or it might pull both and try to hallucinate some weird, impossible hybrid of the two.", "tokens": [51354, 1610, 309, 1062, 2235, 1293, 293, 853, 281, 35212, 13923, 512, 3657, 11, 6243, 13051, 295, 264, 732, 13, 51589], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10258222509313512, "compression_ratio": 1.8104575163398693, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691437507669217e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 67034, "start": 695.12, "end": 699.1800000000001, "text": " Because a database is just an archive of claims that have been made over time.", "tokens": [51604, 1436, 257, 8149, 307, 445, 364, 23507, 295, 9441, 300, 362, 668, 1027, 670, 565, 13, 51807], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10258222509313512, "compression_ratio": 1.8104575163398693, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691437507669217e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 69918, "start": 699.18, "end": 701.66, "text": " It's a filing cabinet of statements.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 257, 26854, 15188, 295, 12363, 13, 50489], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18390874250219502, "compression_ratio": 1.6425531914893616, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252628804071633e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 69918, "start": 701.88, "end": 706.64, "text": " Yes. It is not a unified, reconciled state of currently existing truth.", "tokens": [50500, 1079, 13, 467, 307, 406, 257, 26787, 11, 9993, 3208, 292, 1785, 295, 4362, 6741, 3494, 13, 50738], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18390874250219502, "compression_ratio": 1.6425531914893616, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252628804071633e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 69918, "start": 706.8399999999999, "end": 709.12, "text": " It's a filing cabinet, not a physics engine.", "tokens": [50748, 467, 311, 257, 26854, 15188, 11, 406, 257, 10649, 2848, 13, 50862], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18390874250219502, "compression_ratio": 1.6425531914893616, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252628804071633e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 69918, "start": 709.8, "end": 711.0799999999999, "text": " That makes perfect sense.", "tokens": [50896, 663, 1669, 2176, 2020, 13, 50960], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18390874250219502, "compression_ratio": 1.6425531914893616, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252628804071633e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 69918, "start": 711.4, "end": 717.26, "text": " But let me push back just one more time just to follow this logic to the absolute end.", "tokens": [50976, 583, 718, 385, 2944, 646, 445, 472, 544, 565, 445, 281, 1524, 341, 9952, 281, 264, 8236, 917, 13, 51269], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18390874250219502, "compression_ratio": 1.6425531914893616, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252628804071633e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 69918, "start": 717.38, "end": 717.88, "text": " Go for it.", "tokens": [51275, 1037, 337, 309, 13, 51300], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18390874250219502, "compression_ratio": 1.6425531914893616, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252628804071633e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 69918, "start": 718.0, "end": 720.3, "text": " Let's grant the text a total miracle.", "tokens": [51306, 961, 311, 6386, 264, 2487, 257, 3217, 14660, 13, 51421], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18390874250219502, "compression_ratio": 1.6425531914893616, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252628804071633e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 69918, "start": 720.8, "end": 722.92, "text": " Let's say we engineer a perfect memory module.", "tokens": [51446, 961, 311, 584, 321, 11403, 257, 2176, 4675, 10088, 13, 51552], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18390874250219502, "compression_ratio": 1.6425531914893616, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252628804071633e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 69918, "start": 723.0999999999999, "end": 724.3599999999999, "text": " Okay, a perfect memory.", "tokens": [51561, 1033, 11, 257, 2176, 4675, 13, 51624], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18390874250219502, "compression_ratio": 1.6425531914893616, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252628804071633e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 72436, "start": 724.36, "end": 731.1, "text": " The AI perfectly records the crack, it perfectly retrieves that exact note, and it perfectly reconciles any conflicting info.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 7318, 6239, 7724, 264, 6226, 11, 309, 6239, 19817, 977, 300, 1900, 3637, 11, 293, 309, 6239, 9993, 3208, 279, 604, 43784, 13614, 13, 50702], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11471442805910573, "compression_ratio": 1.6694560669456067, "no_speech_prob": 2.150395963726459e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 72436, "start": 732.0600000000001, "end": 737.0, "text": " The true, accurate state of the wall is sitting right there, prominently in the active context window.", "tokens": [50750, 440, 2074, 11, 8559, 1785, 295, 264, 2929, 307, 3798, 558, 456, 11, 39225, 2276, 294, 264, 4967, 4319, 4910, 13, 50997], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11471442805910573, "compression_ratio": 1.6694560669456067, "no_speech_prob": 2.150395963726459e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 72436, "start": 737.1, "end": 737.32, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51002, 1779, 13, 51013], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11471442805910573, "compression_ratio": 1.6694560669456067, "no_speech_prob": 2.150395963726459e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 72436, "start": 737.5600000000001, "end": 739.96, "text": " Wouldn't the generative AI get it right at that point?", "tokens": [51025, 26291, 380, 264, 1337, 1166, 7318, 483, 309, 558, 412, 300, 935, 30, 51145], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11471442805910573, "compression_ratio": 1.6694560669456067, "no_speech_prob": 2.150395963726459e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 72436, "start": 740.14, "end": 742.24, "text": " It would get it right most of the time, yes.", "tokens": [51154, 467, 576, 483, 309, 558, 881, 295, 264, 565, 11, 2086, 13, 51259], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11471442805910573, "compression_ratio": 1.6694560669456067, "no_speech_prob": 2.150395963726459e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 72436, "start": 742.72, "end": 744.86, "text": " But purely by statistical coincidence.", "tokens": [51283, 583, 17491, 538, 22820, 22137, 13, 51390], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11471442805910573, "compression_ratio": 1.6694560669456067, "no_speech_prob": 2.150395963726459e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 72436, "start": 745.32, "end": 746.54, "text": " Wait, what? Coincidence?", "tokens": [51413, 3802, 11, 437, 30, 3066, 4647, 2778, 30, 51474], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11471442805910573, "compression_ratio": 1.6694560669456067, "no_speech_prob": 2.150395963726459e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 74654, "start": 746.54, "end": 752.24, "text": " Yes, and this introduces the core theoretical difference between statistical continuation and causal continuation.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 11, 293, 341, 31472, 264, 4965, 20864, 2649, 1296, 22820, 29357, 293, 38755, 29357, 13, 50650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1476600403879203, "compression_ratio": 1.6967509025270757, "no_speech_prob": 1.7893554476663964e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 74654, "start": 752.5, "end": 754.66, "text": " Okay, how do those two concepts differ in practice?", "tokens": [50663, 1033, 11, 577, 360, 729, 732, 10392, 743, 294, 3124, 30, 50771], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1476600403879203, "compression_ratio": 1.6967509025270757, "no_speech_prob": 1.7893554476663964e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 74654, "start": 755.38, "end": 756.4, "text": " Because they sound similar.", "tokens": [50807, 1436, 436, 1626, 2531, 13, 50858], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1476600403879203, "compression_ratio": 1.6967509025270757, "no_speech_prob": 1.7893554476663964e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 74654, "start": 756.5, "end": 757.76, "text": " They are fundamentally different.", "tokens": [50863, 814, 366, 17879, 819, 13, 50926], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1476600403879203, "compression_ratio": 1.6967509025270757, "no_speech_prob": 1.7893554476663964e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 74654, "start": 758.28, "end": 761.64, "text": " Statistical continuation asks a probabilistic question.", "tokens": [50952, 16249, 42686, 29357, 8962, 257, 31959, 3142, 1168, 13, 51120], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1476600403879203, "compression_ratio": 1.6967509025270757, "no_speech_prob": 1.7893554476663964e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 74654, "start": 762.5799999999999, "end": 768.74, "text": " Given this specific context window, what is the most likely sequence of tokens or pixels to appear next,", "tokens": [51167, 18600, 341, 2685, 4319, 4910, 11, 437, 307, 264, 881, 3700, 8310, 295, 22667, 420, 18668, 281, 4204, 958, 11, 51475], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1476600403879203, "compression_ratio": 1.6967509025270757, "no_speech_prob": 1.7893554476663964e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 74654, "start": 769.02, "end": 771.52, "text": " based on the vast distribution of my training data?", "tokens": [51489, 2361, 322, 264, 8369, 7316, 295, 452, 3097, 1412, 30, 51614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1476600403879203, "compression_ratio": 1.6967509025270757, "no_speech_prob": 1.7893554476663964e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 74654, "start": 772.04, "end": 773.38, "text": " Okay, it's playing the odds.", "tokens": [51640, 1033, 11, 309, 311, 2433, 264, 17439, 13, 51707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1476600403879203, "compression_ratio": 1.6967509025270757, "no_speech_prob": 1.7893554476663964e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 77338, "start": 773.38, "end": 777.62, "text": " Right. Causal continuation, on the other hand, asks a deterministic question.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 7544, 11765, 29357, 11, 322, 264, 661, 1011, 11, 8962, 257, 15957, 3142, 1168, 13, 50577], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19798524039132254, "compression_ratio": 1.4913793103448276, "no_speech_prob": 1.6875367206056757e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 77338, "start": 778.3, "end": 784.66, "text": " Given the exact prior physical state of this specific system, what must happen next, based on the rigid laws of the world?", "tokens": [50611, 18600, 264, 1900, 4059, 4001, 1785, 295, 341, 2685, 1185, 11, 437, 1633, 1051, 958, 11, 2361, 322, 264, 22195, 6064, 295, 264, 1002, 30, 50929], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19798524039132254, "compression_ratio": 1.4913793103448276, "no_speech_prob": 1.6875367206056757e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 77338, "start": 784.96, "end": 785.4399999999999, "text": " Ah.", "tokens": [50944, 2438, 13, 50968], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19798524039132254, "compression_ratio": 1.4913793103448276, "no_speech_prob": 1.6875367206056757e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 77338, "start": 786.08, "end": 794.4399999999999, "text": " So because models like GPT or SORA are fundamentally next-token predictors, they are completely trapped in statistical continuation.", "tokens": [51000, 407, 570, 5245, 411, 26039, 51, 420, 318, 36860, 366, 17879, 958, 12, 83, 8406, 6069, 830, 11, 436, 366, 2584, 14994, 294, 22820, 29357, 13, 51418], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19798524039132254, "compression_ratio": 1.4913793103448276, "no_speech_prob": 1.6875367206056757e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 77338, "start": 794.66, "end": 795.06, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51429, 7587, 13, 51449], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19798524039132254, "compression_ratio": 1.4913793103448276, "no_speech_prob": 1.6875367206056757e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 79506, "start": 795.06, "end": 800.7199999999999, "text": " Even if you retrieve the perfect, undeniable fact about the cracked wall and place it right in the context window,", "tokens": [50365, 2754, 498, 291, 30254, 264, 2176, 11, 674, 268, 9364, 1186, 466, 264, 25140, 2929, 293, 1081, 309, 558, 294, 264, 4319, 4910, 11, 50648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12446732647651065, "compression_ratio": 1.6543624161073827, "no_speech_prob": 2.192815590565389e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 79506, "start": 801.18, "end": 806.42, "text": " an autoregressive predictor is still, at its absolute core, just evaluating probabilities.", "tokens": [50671, 364, 1476, 418, 3091, 488, 6069, 284, 307, 920, 11, 412, 1080, 8236, 4965, 11, 445, 27479, 33783, 13, 50933], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12446732647651065, "compression_ratio": 1.6543624161073827, "no_speech_prob": 2.192815590565389e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 79506, "start": 806.6199999999999, "end": 807.92, "text": " It's just guessing what sounds right.", "tokens": [50943, 467, 311, 445, 17939, 437, 3263, 558, 13, 51008], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12446732647651065, "compression_ratio": 1.6543624161073827, "no_speech_prob": 2.192815590565389e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 79506, "start": 808.16, "end": 811.52, "text": " The retrieved fact definitely influences the probability distribution.", "tokens": [51020, 440, 19817, 937, 1186, 2138, 21222, 264, 8482, 7316, 13, 51188], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12446732647651065, "compression_ratio": 1.6543624161073827, "no_speech_prob": 2.192815590565389e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 79506, "start": 811.88, "end": 813.8599999999999, "text": " It makes the correct output highly likely.", "tokens": [51206, 467, 1669, 264, 3006, 5598, 5405, 3700, 13, 51305], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12446732647651065, "compression_ratio": 1.6543624161073827, "no_speech_prob": 2.192815590565389e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 79506, "start": 814.16, "end": 817.42, "text": " But the model is simultaneously feeling other statistical pressures.", "tokens": [51320, 583, 264, 2316, 307, 16561, 2633, 661, 22820, 23573, 13, 51483], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12446732647651065, "compression_ratio": 1.6543624161073827, "no_speech_prob": 2.192815590565389e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 79506, "start": 817.5799999999999, "end": 817.92, "text": " Like what?", "tokens": [51491, 1743, 437, 30, 51508], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12446732647651065, "compression_ratio": 1.6543624161073827, "no_speech_prob": 2.192815590565389e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 79506, "start": 818.0799999999999, "end": 821.3, "text": " It's feeling stylistic tendencies from its fine-tuning.", "tokens": [51516, 467, 311, 2633, 23736, 3142, 45488, 490, 1080, 2489, 12, 83, 37726, 13, 51677], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12446732647651065, "compression_ratio": 1.6543624161073827, "no_speech_prob": 2.192815590565389e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 82130, "start": 821.3, "end": 827.8599999999999, "text": " It's feeling the weight of millions of other generic, uncracked stone walls in its training data.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 2633, 264, 3364, 295, 6803, 295, 661, 19577, 11, 6219, 81, 25949, 7581, 7920, 294, 1080, 3097, 1412, 13, 50693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11945280039085532, "compression_ratio": 1.5923344947735192, "no_speech_prob": 2.096507429466543e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 82130, "start": 828.0799999999999, "end": 828.38, "text": " Oh, wow.", "tokens": [50704, 876, 11, 6076, 13, 50719], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11945280039085532, "compression_ratio": 1.5923344947735192, "no_speech_prob": 2.096507429466543e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 82130, "start": 828.4599999999999, "end": 832.68, "text": " So if you run the generation enough times, or if the prompt is just slightly unusual,", "tokens": [50723, 407, 498, 291, 1190, 264, 5125, 1547, 1413, 11, 420, 498, 264, 12391, 307, 445, 4748, 10901, 11, 50934], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11945280039085532, "compression_ratio": 1.5923344947735192, "no_speech_prob": 2.096507429466543e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 82130, "start": 833.3199999999999, "end": 837.3399999999999, "text": " those other statistical pressures can overpower the retrieved fact.", "tokens": [50966, 729, 661, 22820, 23573, 393, 670, 9513, 264, 19817, 937, 1186, 13, 51167], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11945280039085532, "compression_ratio": 1.5923344947735192, "no_speech_prob": 2.096507429466543e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 82130, "start": 837.8599999999999, "end": 845.06, "text": " The AI makes the correct continuation probable, but it fundamentally lacks the architecture to make it necessary.", "tokens": [51193, 440, 7318, 1669, 264, 3006, 29357, 21759, 11, 457, 309, 17879, 31132, 264, 9482, 281, 652, 309, 4818, 13, 51553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11945280039085532, "compression_ratio": 1.5923344947735192, "no_speech_prob": 2.096507429466543e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 82130, "start": 845.24, "end": 848.8199999999999, "text": " It basically treats the truth as a suggestion rather than a physical law.", "tokens": [51562, 467, 1936, 19566, 264, 3494, 382, 257, 16541, 2831, 813, 257, 4001, 2101, 13, 51741], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11945280039085532, "compression_ratio": 1.5923344947735192, "no_speech_prob": 2.096507429466543e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 82130, "start": 848.9, "end": 849.16, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51745, 7587, 13, 51758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11945280039085532, "compression_ratio": 1.5923344947735192, "no_speech_prob": 2.096507429466543e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 84916, "start": 849.16, "end": 854.4599999999999, "text": " That perfectly sets up this wild case study from the text that I found so, so illuminating.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 6239, 6352, 493, 341, 4868, 1389, 2979, 490, 264, 2487, 300, 286, 1352, 370, 11, 370, 28593, 990, 13, 50630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13845923452666312, "compression_ratio": 1.5570469798657718, "no_speech_prob": 1.832195419687599e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 84916, "start": 854.6, "end": 856.52, "text": " The author brings up InspiroBot.", "tokens": [50637, 440, 3793, 5607, 493, 32671, 5182, 33, 310, 13, 50733], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13845923452666312, "compression_ratio": 1.5570469798657718, "no_speech_prob": 1.832195419687599e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 84916, "start": 856.7199999999999, "end": 857.36, "text": " Oh, yes.", "tokens": [50743, 876, 11, 2086, 13, 50775], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13845923452666312, "compression_ratio": 1.5570469798657718, "no_speech_prob": 1.832195419687599e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 84916, "start": 857.78, "end": 858.26, "text": " InspiroBot.", "tokens": [50796, 32671, 5182, 33, 310, 13, 50820], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13845923452666312, "compression_ratio": 1.5570469798657718, "no_speech_prob": 1.832195419687599e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 84916, "start": 858.3399999999999, "end": 866.24, "text": " For anyone listening who isn't familiar, InspiroBot is this older, very funny website that generates absurd, fake, inspirational posters.", "tokens": [50824, 1171, 2878, 4764, 567, 1943, 380, 4963, 11, 32671, 5182, 33, 310, 307, 341, 4906, 11, 588, 4074, 3144, 300, 23815, 19774, 11, 7592, 11, 33554, 28172, 13, 51219], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13845923452666312, "compression_ratio": 1.5570469798657718, "no_speech_prob": 1.832195419687599e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 84916, "start": 866.5, "end": 867.3, "text": " It's a classic.", "tokens": [51232, 467, 311, 257, 7230, 13, 51272], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13845923452666312, "compression_ratio": 1.5570469798657718, "no_speech_prob": 1.832195419687599e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 84916, "start": 867.48, "end": 872.3399999999999, "text": " It takes a random stock photo of like a sunset or mountain, and it slaps on AI-generated text.", "tokens": [51281, 467, 2516, 257, 4974, 4127, 5052, 295, 411, 257, 20142, 420, 6937, 11, 293, 309, 1061, 2382, 322, 7318, 12, 21848, 770, 2487, 13, 51524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13845923452666312, "compression_ratio": 1.5570469798657718, "no_speech_prob": 1.832195419687599e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 84916, "start": 872.4, "end": 875.88, "text": " Like, when you finally give up, a garbage can becomes a dream.", "tokens": [51527, 1743, 11, 562, 291, 2721, 976, 493, 11, 257, 14150, 393, 3643, 257, 3055, 13, 51701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13845923452666312, "compression_ratio": 1.5570469798657718, "no_speech_prob": 1.832195419687599e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 84916, "start": 875.9399999999999, "end": 876.18, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51704, 1779, 13, 51716], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13845923452666312, "compression_ratio": 1.5570469798657718, "no_speech_prob": 1.832195419687599e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 87618, "start": 876.18, "end": 885.1999999999999, "text": " And it's incredibly entertaining because the grammar is flawless, and it perfectly mimics the cadence and structure of a profound philosophical thought, but it means absolutely nothing.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 309, 311, 6252, 20402, 570, 264, 22317, 307, 45693, 11, 293, 309, 6239, 12247, 1167, 264, 46109, 293, 3877, 295, 257, 14382, 25066, 1194, 11, 457, 309, 1355, 3122, 1825, 13, 50816], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08491024706098768, "compression_ratio": 1.3503649635036497, "no_speech_prob": 2.3155702615768048e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 88520, "start": 885.2, "end": 892.1600000000001, "text": " And the author uses InspiroBot to highlight a profound illusion in human-computer interaction.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 3793, 4960, 32671, 5182, 33, 310, 281, 5078, 257, 14382, 18854, 294, 1952, 12, 1112, 13849, 9285, 13, 50713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13208817887580257, "compression_ratio": 1.51131221719457, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007713596847718e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 88520, "start": 892.36, "end": 892.9200000000001, "text": " What's the illusion?", "tokens": [50723, 708, 311, 264, 18854, 30, 50751], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13208817887580257, "compression_ratio": 1.51131221719457, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007713596847718e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 88520, "start": 893.5400000000001, "end": 900.6400000000001, "text": " Well, InspiroBot does not possess an underlying semantic model of human psychology or wisdom or advice, right?", "tokens": [50782, 1042, 11, 32671, 5182, 33, 310, 775, 406, 17490, 364, 14217, 47982, 2316, 295, 1952, 15105, 420, 10712, 420, 5192, 11, 558, 30, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13208817887580257, "compression_ratio": 1.51131221719457, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007713596847718e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 88520, "start": 900.6800000000001, "end": 900.82, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51139, 1779, 13, 51146], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13208817887580257, "compression_ratio": 1.51131221719457, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007713596847718e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 88520, "start": 900.88, "end": 901.5400000000001, "text": " It's just a script.", "tokens": [51149, 467, 311, 445, 257, 5755, 13, 51182], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13208817887580257, "compression_ratio": 1.51131221719457, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007713596847718e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 88520, "start": 901.82, "end": 906.74, "text": " It is simply recombining syntactic fragments using a rigid grammatical template.", "tokens": [51196, 467, 307, 2935, 850, 3548, 1760, 23980, 19892, 29197, 1228, 257, 22195, 17570, 267, 804, 12379, 13, 51442], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13208817887580257, "compression_ratio": 1.51131221719457, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007713596847718e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 90674, "start": 906.74, "end": 911.6800000000001, "text": " The surface form is highly plausible, but where does the actual meaning reside?", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3753, 1254, 307, 5405, 39925, 11, 457, 689, 775, 264, 3539, 3620, 40134, 30, 50612], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12221544439142401, "compression_ratio": 1.575091575091575, "no_speech_prob": 1.4953956042201844e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 90674, "start": 912.02, "end": 914.62, "text": " The meaning is entirely supplied by the human reading it.", "tokens": [50629, 440, 3620, 307, 7696, 27625, 538, 264, 1952, 3760, 309, 13, 50759], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12221544439142401, "compression_ratio": 1.575091575091575, "no_speech_prob": 1.4953956042201844e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 90674, "start": 914.82, "end": 915.26, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50769, 7587, 13, 50791], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12221544439142401, "compression_ratio": 1.575091575091575, "no_speech_prob": 1.4953956042201844e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 90674, "start": 915.58, "end": 927.32, "text": " Our brains are so aggressively wired to find patterns and derive meaning that we read a phrase about a garbage can becoming a dream, and we do the cognitive labor of interpreting it.", "tokens": [50807, 2621, 15442, 366, 370, 32024, 27415, 281, 915, 8294, 293, 28446, 3620, 300, 321, 1401, 257, 9535, 466, 257, 14150, 393, 5617, 257, 3055, 11, 293, 321, 360, 264, 15605, 5938, 295, 37395, 309, 13, 51394], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12221544439142401, "compression_ratio": 1.575091575091575, "no_speech_prob": 1.4953956042201844e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 90674, "start": 927.38, "end": 931.12, "text": " We think, oh, maybe that's a metaphor for finding unexpected beauty when you hit rock bottom.", "tokens": [51397, 492, 519, 11, 1954, 11, 1310, 300, 311, 257, 19157, 337, 5006, 13106, 6643, 562, 291, 2045, 3727, 2767, 13, 51584], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12221544439142401, "compression_ratio": 1.575091575091575, "no_speech_prob": 1.4953956042201844e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 90674, "start": 931.1800000000001, "end": 931.4, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51587, 1779, 13, 51598], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12221544439142401, "compression_ratio": 1.575091575091575, "no_speech_prob": 1.4953956042201844e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 93140, "start": 931.4, "end": 932.84, "text": " But the bot didn't intend that.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 10592, 994, 380, 19759, 300, 13, 50437], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10679755954567445, "compression_ratio": 1.5607843137254902, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484459196969281e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 93140, "start": 932.9399999999999, "end": 933.78, "text": " We built the bridge.", "tokens": [50442, 492, 3094, 264, 7283, 13, 50484], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10679755954567445, "compression_ratio": 1.5607843137254902, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484459196969281e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 93140, "start": 933.9, "end": 934.54, "text": " We did all the work.", "tokens": [50490, 492, 630, 439, 264, 589, 13, 50522], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10679755954567445, "compression_ratio": 1.5607843137254902, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484459196969281e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 93140, "start": 934.86, "end": 937.86, "text": " The human observer performs what we might call a charitable repair.", "tokens": [50538, 440, 1952, 27878, 26213, 437, 321, 1062, 818, 257, 44609, 10535, 13, 50688], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10679755954567445, "compression_ratio": 1.5607843137254902, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484459196969281e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 93140, "start": 938.1999999999999, "end": 948.9, "text": " And the central argument of the text is that modern, state-of-the-art, large-language models are doing the exact same thing as InspiroBot, just on a vastly more complex, multidimensional scale.", "tokens": [50705, 400, 264, 5777, 6770, 295, 264, 2487, 307, 300, 4363, 11, 1785, 12, 2670, 12, 3322, 12, 446, 11, 2416, 12, 25241, 20473, 5245, 366, 884, 264, 1900, 912, 551, 382, 32671, 5182, 33, 310, 11, 445, 322, 257, 41426, 544, 3997, 11, 2120, 327, 332, 11075, 4373, 13, 51240], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10679755954567445, "compression_ratio": 1.5607843137254902, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484459196969281e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 93140, "start": 949.0, "end": 952.02, "text": " They're just very, very good at faking the cadence of reality.", "tokens": [51245, 814, 434, 445, 588, 11, 588, 665, 412, 283, 2456, 264, 46109, 295, 4103, 13, 51396], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10679755954567445, "compression_ratio": 1.5607843137254902, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484459196969281e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 95202, "start": 952.02, "end": 952.6999999999999, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50399], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20237472822081368, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130236473426262e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 95202, "start": 953.0, "end": 959.48, "text": " They navigate a statistical manifold to produce outputs that are highly fluent and structurally flawless.", "tokens": [50414, 814, 12350, 257, 22820, 47138, 281, 5258, 23930, 300, 366, 5405, 40799, 293, 6594, 6512, 45693, 13, 50738], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20237472822081368, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130236473426262e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 95202, "start": 959.92, "end": 963.14, "text": " But the output is fundamentally groundless.", "tokens": [50760, 583, 264, 5598, 307, 17879, 2727, 1832, 13, 50921], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20237472822081368, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130236473426262e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 95202, "start": 963.48, "end": 963.84, "text": " Groundless.", "tokens": [50938, 28371, 1832, 13, 50956], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20237472822081368, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130236473426262e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 95202, "start": 964.06, "end": 964.28, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50967, 865, 13, 50978], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20237472822081368, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130236473426262e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 95202, "start": 964.4, "end": 965.84, "text": " Meaning it has no anchor.", "tokens": [50984, 19948, 309, 575, 572, 18487, 13, 51056], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20237472822081368, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130236473426262e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 95202, "start": 966.28, "end": 971.56, "text": " There is no underlying objective reality that the AI is checking its claims against.", "tokens": [51078, 821, 307, 572, 14217, 10024, 4103, 300, 264, 7318, 307, 8568, 1080, 9441, 1970, 13, 51342], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20237472822081368, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130236473426262e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 95202, "start": 971.76, "end": 975.26, "text": " So when a language model hallucinates a legal citation...", "tokens": [51352, 407, 562, 257, 2856, 2316, 35212, 259, 1024, 257, 5089, 45590, 485, 51527], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20237472822081368, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130236473426262e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 95202, "start": 975.26, "end": 976.18, "text": " Which happens all the time.", "tokens": [51527, 3013, 2314, 439, 264, 565, 13, 51573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20237472822081368, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130236473426262e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 95202, "start": 976.26, "end": 976.6, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51577, 1779, 13, 51594], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20237472822081368, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130236473426262e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 95202, "start": 976.98, "end": 980.02, "text": " The output looks identical to a real citation.", "tokens": [51613, 440, 5598, 1542, 14800, 281, 257, 957, 45590, 13, 51765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20237472822081368, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130236473426262e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 98002, "start": 980.02, "end": 982.0799999999999, "text": " It formats the text perfectly.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 25879, 264, 2487, 6239, 13, 50468], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16462344693062, "compression_ratio": 1.6719745222929936, "no_speech_prob": 1.5126979530100115e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 98002, "start": 982.4, "end": 984.62, "text": " It references real academic journals.", "tokens": [50484, 467, 15400, 957, 7778, 29621, 13, 50595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16462344693062, "compression_ratio": 1.6719745222929936, "no_speech_prob": 1.5126979530100115e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 98002, "start": 984.76, "end": 986.5799999999999, "text": " It uses the correct legal jargon.", "tokens": [50602, 467, 4960, 264, 3006, 5089, 15181, 10660, 13, 50693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16462344693062, "compression_ratio": 1.6719745222929936, "no_speech_prob": 1.5126979530100115e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 98002, "start": 986.78, "end": 988.18, "text": " But it is anchored to nothing.", "tokens": [50703, 583, 309, 307, 12723, 2769, 281, 1825, 13, 50773], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16462344693062, "compression_ratio": 1.6719745222929936, "no_speech_prob": 1.5126979530100115e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 98002, "start": 988.52, "end": 990.9, "text": " It is just InspiroBot wearing a suit.", "tokens": [50790, 467, 307, 445, 32671, 5182, 33, 310, 4769, 257, 5722, 13, 50909], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16462344693062, "compression_ratio": 1.6719745222929936, "no_speech_prob": 1.5126979530100115e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 98002, "start": 991.26, "end": 992.4, "text": " InspiroBot wearing a suit.", "tokens": [50927, 32671, 5182, 33, 310, 4769, 257, 5722, 13, 50984], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16462344693062, "compression_ratio": 1.6719745222929936, "no_speech_prob": 1.5126979530100115e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 98002, "start": 992.54, "end": 994.12, "text": " That's chilling, honestly.", "tokens": [50991, 663, 311, 31047, 11, 6095, 13, 51070], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16462344693062, "compression_ratio": 1.6719745222929936, "no_speech_prob": 1.5126979530100115e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 98002, "start": 994.46, "end": 1000.02, "text": " So if context buffers fail, if document retrieval databases fail, and if statistical next token prediction fails...", "tokens": [51087, 407, 498, 4319, 9204, 433, 3061, 11, 498, 4166, 19817, 3337, 22380, 3061, 11, 293, 498, 22820, 958, 14862, 17630, 18199, 485, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16462344693062, "compression_ratio": 1.6719745222929936, "no_speech_prob": 1.5126979530100115e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 98002, "start": 1000.6, "end": 1001.48, "text": " We have a big problem.", "tokens": [51394, 492, 362, 257, 955, 1154, 13, 51438], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16462344693062, "compression_ratio": 1.6719745222929936, "no_speech_prob": 1.5126979530100115e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 98002, "start": 1001.6, "end": 1005.8, "text": " We have to throw the entire current paradigm out the window if we ever want to build persistent worlds.", "tokens": [51444, 492, 362, 281, 3507, 264, 2302, 2190, 24709, 484, 264, 4910, 498, 321, 1562, 528, 281, 1322, 24315, 13401, 13, 51654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16462344693062, "compression_ratio": 1.6719745222929936, "no_speech_prob": 1.5126979530100115e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 98002, "start": 1006.0, "end": 1008.28, "text": " We need a completely different architectural foundation.", "tokens": [51664, 492, 643, 257, 2584, 819, 26621, 7030, 13, 51778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16462344693062, "compression_ratio": 1.6719745222929936, "no_speech_prob": 1.5126979530100115e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 100828, "start": 1008.28, "end": 1013.56, "text": " Which is exactly where the text pivots from diagnosing the problem to proposing the solution.", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 307, 2293, 689, 264, 2487, 280, 592, 1971, 490, 7234, 6110, 264, 1154, 281, 29939, 264, 3827, 13, 50629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12566164224454673, "compression_ratio": 1.62109375, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071204917740944e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 100828, "start": 1013.76, "end": 1013.9, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50639, 1779, 13, 50646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12566164224454673, "compression_ratio": 1.62109375, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071204917740944e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 100828, "start": 1014.02, "end": 1015.88, "text": " The concept of the semantic field.", "tokens": [50652, 440, 3410, 295, 264, 47982, 2519, 13, 50745], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12566164224454673, "compression_ratio": 1.62109375, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071204917740944e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 100828, "start": 1016.3, "end": 1016.56, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50766, 1079, 13, 50779], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12566164224454673, "compression_ratio": 1.62109375, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071204917740944e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 100828, "start": 1017.0, "end": 1022.98, "text": " And the leap here is moving away from the concept of discrete objects entirely and embracing continuous fields.", "tokens": [50801, 400, 264, 19438, 510, 307, 2684, 1314, 490, 264, 3410, 295, 27706, 6565, 7696, 293, 31596, 10957, 7909, 13, 51100], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12566164224454673, "compression_ratio": 1.62109375, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071204917740944e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 100828, "start": 1023.1999999999999, "end": 1025.52, "text": " That was a huge paradigm shift for me.", "tokens": [51111, 663, 390, 257, 2603, 24709, 5513, 337, 385, 13, 51227], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12566164224454673, "compression_ratio": 1.62109375, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071204917740944e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 100828, "start": 1025.84, "end": 1031.68, "text": " Because when we think about how virtual worlds are built today, they all rely on discrete objects.", "tokens": [51243, 1436, 562, 321, 519, 466, 577, 6374, 13401, 366, 3094, 965, 11, 436, 439, 10687, 322, 27706, 6565, 13, 51535], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12566164224454673, "compression_ratio": 1.62109375, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071204917740944e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 100828, "start": 1031.98, "end": 1032.82, "text": " Pretty much all of them.", "tokens": [51550, 10693, 709, 439, 295, 552, 13, 51592], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12566164224454673, "compression_ratio": 1.62109375, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071204917740944e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 103282, "start": 1032.82, "end": 1035.9399999999998, "text": " Video games use scene graphs or voxel grids.", "tokens": [50365, 9777, 2813, 764, 4145, 24877, 420, 1650, 87, 338, 677, 3742, 13, 50521], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16249523560206094, "compression_ratio": 1.5527426160337552, "no_speech_prob": 1.592225808665082e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 103282, "start": 1036.08, "end": 1040.06, "text": " You have a definitive, you know, wall object, a player object, a sword object.", "tokens": [50528, 509, 362, 257, 28152, 11, 291, 458, 11, 2929, 2657, 11, 257, 4256, 2657, 11, 257, 10576, 2657, 13, 50727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16249523560206094, "compression_ratio": 1.5527426160337552, "no_speech_prob": 1.592225808665082e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 103282, "start": 1040.1399999999999, "end": 1040.34, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50731, 1779, 13, 50741], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16249523560206094, "compression_ratio": 1.5527426160337552, "no_speech_prob": 1.592225808665082e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 103282, "start": 1040.74, "end": 1042.48, "text": " Distinct bounded entities.", "tokens": [50761, 9840, 5460, 37498, 16667, 13, 50848], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16249523560206094, "compression_ratio": 1.5527426160337552, "no_speech_prob": 1.592225808665082e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 103282, "start": 1042.84, "end": 1045.84, "text": " But the text points out the fatal flaw in that approach.", "tokens": [50866, 583, 264, 2487, 2793, 484, 264, 24069, 13717, 294, 300, 3109, 13, 51016], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16249523560206094, "compression_ratio": 1.5527426160337552, "no_speech_prob": 1.592225808665082e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 103282, "start": 1046.1, "end": 1051.5, "text": " If you rely on discrete objects, how do you classify dampness spreading up a stone wall?", "tokens": [51029, 759, 291, 10687, 322, 27706, 6565, 11, 577, 360, 291, 33872, 19498, 1287, 15232, 493, 257, 7581, 2929, 30, 51299], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16249523560206094, "compression_ratio": 1.5527426160337552, "no_speech_prob": 1.592225808665082e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 103282, "start": 1051.7, "end": 1054.6799999999998, "text": " Or how do you classify diffuse sunlight filtering through smoke?", "tokens": [51309, 1610, 577, 360, 291, 33872, 42165, 18379, 30822, 807, 8439, 30, 51458], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16249523560206094, "compression_ratio": 1.5527426160337552, "no_speech_prob": 1.592225808665082e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 105468, "start": 1054.68, "end": 1055.16, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18238867123921712, "compression_ratio": 1.5577689243027888, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622691500518428e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 105468, "start": 1055.5600000000002, "end": 1059.5600000000002, "text": " Or soot slowly accumulating on the ceiling of a cave from a campfire.", "tokens": [50409, 1610, 370, 310, 5692, 12989, 12162, 322, 264, 13655, 295, 257, 11730, 490, 257, 2255, 12037, 13, 50609], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18238867123921712, "compression_ratio": 1.5577689243027888, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622691500518428e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 105468, "start": 1060.1000000000001, "end": 1066.3400000000001, "text": " When you utilize a scene graph, you are forced to decide in advance what counts as a distinct entity.", "tokens": [50636, 1133, 291, 16117, 257, 4145, 4295, 11, 291, 366, 7579, 281, 4536, 294, 7295, 437, 14893, 382, 257, 10644, 13977, 13, 50948], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18238867123921712, "compression_ratio": 1.5577689243027888, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622691500518428e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 105468, "start": 1066.5, "end": 1066.66, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50956, 1779, 13, 50964], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18238867123921712, "compression_ratio": 1.5577689243027888, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622691500518428e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 105468, "start": 1066.74, "end": 1067.42, "text": " You're to the label it.", "tokens": [50968, 509, 434, 281, 264, 7645, 309, 13, 51002], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18238867123921712, "compression_ratio": 1.5577689243027888, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622691500518428e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 105468, "start": 1067.52, "end": 1067.78, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51007, 1079, 13, 51020], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18238867123921712, "compression_ratio": 1.5577689243027888, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622691500518428e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 105468, "start": 1068.18, "end": 1069.72, "text": " Is the soot its own object?", "tokens": [51040, 1119, 264, 370, 310, 1080, 1065, 2657, 30, 51117], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18238867123921712, "compression_ratio": 1.5577689243027888, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622691500518428e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 105468, "start": 1070.14, "end": 1072.22, "text": " Is the dampness a subproperty of the wall?", "tokens": [51138, 1119, 264, 19498, 1287, 257, 1422, 4318, 610, 874, 295, 264, 2929, 30, 51242], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18238867123921712, "compression_ratio": 1.5577689243027888, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622691500518428e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 105468, "start": 1072.3, "end": 1076.16, "text": " Or is it a completely separate water object clinging to the wall object?", "tokens": [51246, 1610, 307, 309, 257, 2584, 4994, 1281, 2657, 596, 8716, 281, 264, 2929, 2657, 30, 51439], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18238867123921712, "compression_ratio": 1.5577689243027888, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622691500518428e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 105468, "start": 1076.3200000000002, "end": 1077.88, "text": " And it gets so messy.", "tokens": [51447, 400, 309, 2170, 370, 16191, 13, 51525], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18238867123921712, "compression_ratio": 1.5577689243027888, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622691500518428e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 105468, "start": 1078.18, "end": 1078.8, "text": " It does.", "tokens": [51540, 467, 775, 13, 51571], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18238867123921712, "compression_ratio": 1.5577689243027888, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622691500518428e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 107880, "start": 1078.8, "end": 1084.84, "text": " Because discreteness forces the engineers to choose a resolution and a set of categories before the simulation even begins.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 2983, 35383, 442, 5874, 264, 11955, 281, 2826, 257, 8669, 293, 257, 992, 295, 10479, 949, 264, 16575, 754, 7338, 13, 50667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2726239049157431, "compression_ratio": 1.6514657980456027, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815665613428843e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 107880, "start": 1085.26, "end": 1092.96, "text": " And the moment the simulation encounters a phenomenon that exists outside or between those rigid categories, the entire system breaks down.", "tokens": [50688, 400, 264, 1623, 264, 16575, 26310, 257, 14029, 300, 8198, 2380, 420, 1296, 729, 22195, 10479, 11, 264, 2302, 1185, 9857, 760, 13, 51073], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2726239049157431, "compression_ratio": 1.6514657980456027, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815665613428843e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 107880, "start": 1093.24, "end": 1098.7, "text": " So what is the semantic field and how does it solve this problem of deciding what an object is?", "tokens": [51087, 407, 437, 307, 264, 47982, 2519, 293, 577, 775, 309, 5039, 341, 1154, 295, 17990, 437, 364, 2657, 307, 30, 51360], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2726239049157431, "compression_ratio": 1.6514657980456027, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815665613428843e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 107880, "start": 1098.98, "end": 1102.2, "text": " Well, the semantic field defines reality mathematically as a mapping.", "tokens": [51374, 1042, 11, 264, 47982, 2519, 23122, 4103, 44003, 382, 257, 18350, 13, 51535], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2726239049157431, "compression_ratio": 1.6514657980456027, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815665613428843e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 107880, "start": 1102.78, "end": 1104.6399999999999, "text": " Formally, it's written as six scholars.", "tokens": [51564, 10126, 379, 11, 309, 311, 3720, 382, 2309, 8553, 13, 51657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2726239049157431, "compression_ratio": 1.6514657980456027, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815665613428843e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 107880, "start": 1105.26, "end": 1105.6599999999999, "text": " Map.", "tokens": [51688, 22053, 13, 51708], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2726239049157431, "compression_ratio": 1.6514657980456027, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815665613428843e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 107880, "start": 1106.12, "end": 1106.6, "text": " Psygey.", "tokens": [51731, 430, 3187, 432, 88, 13, 51755], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2726239049157431, "compression_ratio": 1.6514657980456027, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815665613428843e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 107880, "start": 1106.7, "end": 1107.04, "text": " E-y-d.", "tokens": [51760, 462, 12, 88, 12, 67, 13, 51777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2726239049157431, "compression_ratio": 1.6514657980456027, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815665613428843e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 107880, "start": 1107.3, "end": 1107.52, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51790, 1033, 13, 51801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2726239049157431, "compression_ratio": 1.6514657980456027, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815665613428843e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 107880, "start": 1107.7, "end": 1107.8999999999999, "text": " Whoa.", "tokens": [51810, 7521, 13, 51820], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2726239049157431, "compression_ratio": 1.6514657980456027, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815665613428843e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 107880, "start": 1108.1599999999999, "end": 1108.52, "text": " Math.", "tokens": [51833, 15776, 13, 51851], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2726239049157431, "compression_ratio": 1.6514657980456027, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815665613428843e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 110880, "start": 1108.8, "end": 1115.0, "text": " Let's definitely break that down into a visual for you listening at home because equations on an audio deep dive can be a bit abstract.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 311, 2138, 1821, 300, 760, 666, 257, 5056, 337, 291, 4764, 412, 1280, 570, 11787, 322, 364, 6278, 2452, 9192, 393, 312, 257, 857, 12649, 13, 50675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13100281972733754, "compression_ratio": 1.610062893081761, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111157105288322e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 110880, "start": 1115.28, "end": 1115.62, "text": " Fair enough.", "tokens": [50689, 12157, 1547, 13, 50706], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13100281972733754, "compression_ratio": 1.610062893081761, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111157105288322e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 110880, "start": 1115.74, "end": 1118.76, "text": " It's actually a very intuitive concept once you visualize it.", "tokens": [50712, 467, 311, 767, 257, 588, 21769, 3410, 1564, 291, 23273, 309, 13, 50863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13100281972733754, "compression_ratio": 1.610062893081761, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111157105288322e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 110880, "start": 1118.9199999999998, "end": 1118.96, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50871, 1033, 13, 50873], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13100281972733754, "compression_ratio": 1.610062893081761, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111157105288322e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 110880, "start": 1119.06, "end": 1119.3799999999999, "text": " Well, you know.", "tokens": [50878, 1042, 11, 291, 458, 13, 50894], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13100281972733754, "compression_ratio": 1.610062893081761, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111157105288322e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 110880, "start": 1119.8, "end": 1130.06, "text": " Instead of predefining a list of objects, the field assigns a high dimensional vector of real values to every single continuous point in a given space, which we call the domain.", "tokens": [50915, 7156, 295, 659, 20595, 1760, 257, 1329, 295, 6565, 11, 264, 2519, 6269, 82, 257, 1090, 18795, 8062, 295, 957, 4190, 281, 633, 2167, 10957, 935, 294, 257, 2212, 1901, 11, 597, 321, 818, 264, 9274, 13, 51428], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13100281972733754, "compression_ratio": 1.610062893081761, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111157105288322e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 110880, "start": 1130.24, "end": 1132.8, "text": " So every literal millimeter of space has a data point.", "tokens": [51437, 407, 633, 20411, 17942, 295, 1901, 575, 257, 1412, 935, 13, 51565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13100281972733754, "compression_ratio": 1.610062893081761, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111157105288322e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 110880, "start": 1133.02, "end": 1133.4199999999998, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51576, 7587, 13, 51596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13100281972733754, "compression_ratio": 1.610062893081761, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111157105288322e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 110880, "start": 1133.68, "end": 1135.3999999999999, "text": " Every spatial coordinate has a state.", "tokens": [51609, 2048, 23598, 15670, 575, 257, 1785, 13, 51695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13100281972733754, "compression_ratio": 1.610062893081761, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111157105288322e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 113540, "start": 1135.4, "end": 1139.94, "text": " In this architecture, objects like our stone wall are not hard coded entities in a list.", "tokens": [50365, 682, 341, 9482, 11, 6565, 411, 527, 7581, 2929, 366, 406, 1152, 34874, 16667, 294, 257, 1329, 13, 50592], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14734228090806442, "compression_ratio": 1.1, "no_speech_prob": 1.6613800179338112e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 113994, "start": 1139.94, "end": 1143.38, "text": " They simply emerge as regions of high coherence within the field.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 2935, 21511, 382, 10682, 295, 1090, 26528, 655, 1951, 264, 2519, 13, 50537], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12986376068808816, "compression_ratio": 1.305084745762712, "no_speech_prob": 1.7141155031832889e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 113994, "start": 1143.38, "end": 1144.42, "text": " Oh, that's wild.", "tokens": [50537, 876, 11, 300, 311, 4868, 13, 50589], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12986376068808816, "compression_ratio": 1.305084745762712, "no_speech_prob": 1.7141155031832889e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 113994, "start": 1144.42, "end": 1149.42, "text": " So the boundary of the wall isn't a line of code saying wall ends here.", "tokens": [50589, 407, 264, 12866, 295, 264, 2929, 1943, 380, 257, 1622, 295, 3089, 1566, 2929, 5314, 510, 13, 50839], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12986376068808816, "compression_ratio": 1.305084745762712, "no_speech_prob": 1.7141155031832889e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 114942, "start": 1149.42, "end": 1149.9, "text": " Nope.", "tokens": [50365, 12172, 13, 50389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1950266202290853, "compression_ratio": 1.2277227722772277, "no_speech_prob": 1.926700335733167e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 114942, "start": 1149.9, "end": 1157.98, "text": " It is simply the physical location where the semantic values in the field shift sharply from solid stone to empty air.", "tokens": [50389, 467, 307, 2935, 264, 4001, 4914, 689, 264, 47982, 4190, 294, 264, 2519, 5513, 42893, 490, 5100, 7581, 281, 6707, 1988, 13, 50793], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1950266202290853, "compression_ratio": 1.2277227722772277, "no_speech_prob": 1.926700335733167e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 115798, "start": 1157.98, "end": 1163.58, "text": " But the wall isn't a pattern that the field is currently maintaining.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 2929, 1943, 380, 257, 5102, 300, 264, 2519, 307, 4362, 14916, 13, 50645], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.29174261826735276, "compression_ratio": 1.4565217391304348, "no_speech_prob": 1.821112705080452e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 115798, "start": 1163.58, "end": 1164.76, "text": " I love that so much.", "tokens": [50645, 286, 959, 300, 370, 709, 13, 50704], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.29174261826735276, "compression_ratio": 1.4565217391304348, "no_speech_prob": 1.821112705080452e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 115798, "start": 1164.84, "end": 1167.9, "text": " It's a much more organic way to simulate physics.", "tokens": [50708, 467, 311, 257, 709, 544, 10220, 636, 281, 27817, 10649, 13, 50861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.29174261826735276, "compression_ratio": 1.4565217391304348, "no_speech_prob": 1.821112705080452e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 115798, "start": 1168.0, "end": 1168.84, "text": " But what are the values?", "tokens": [50866, 583, 437, 366, 264, 4190, 30, 50908], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.29174261826735276, "compression_ratio": 1.4565217391304348, "no_speech_prob": 1.821112705080452e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 115798, "start": 1169.04, "end": 1174.46, "text": " Like what does every single microscopic point in this continuous field actually remember about itself?", "tokens": [50918, 1743, 437, 775, 633, 2167, 47897, 935, 294, 341, 10957, 2519, 767, 1604, 466, 2564, 30, 51189], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.29174261826735276, "compression_ratio": 1.4565217391304348, "no_speech_prob": 1.821112705080452e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 117446, "start": 1174.46, "end": 1181.88, "text": " The text establishes that every coordinate in the semantic field simultaneously tracks five specific components of memory.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2487, 8327, 279, 300, 633, 15670, 294, 264, 47982, 2519, 16561, 10218, 1732, 2685, 6677, 295, 4675, 13, 50736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1401110804358194, "compression_ratio": 1.697674418604651, "no_speech_prob": 1.912197180112263e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 117446, "start": 1182.02, "end": 1183.04, "text": " Okay, five components.", "tokens": [50743, 1033, 11, 1732, 6677, 13, 50794], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1401110804358194, "compression_ratio": 1.697674418604651, "no_speech_prob": 1.912197180112263e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 117446, "start": 1183.16, "end": 1183.78, "text": " What's the first one?", "tokens": [50800, 708, 311, 264, 700, 472, 30, 50831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1401110804358194, "compression_ratio": 1.697674418604651, "no_speech_prob": 1.912197180112263e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 117446, "start": 1183.9, "end": 1186.8600000000001, "text": " The first component is phi, which represents coherence.", "tokens": [50837, 440, 700, 6542, 307, 13107, 11, 597, 8855, 26528, 655, 13, 50985], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1401110804358194, "compression_ratio": 1.697674418604651, "no_speech_prob": 1.912197180112263e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 117446, "start": 1187.02, "end": 1188.22, "text": " Coherence, meaning what?", "tokens": [50993, 3066, 511, 655, 11, 3620, 437, 30, 51053], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1401110804358194, "compression_ratio": 1.697674418604651, "no_speech_prob": 1.912197180112263e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 117446, "start": 1188.38, "end": 1190.06, "text": " Coherence answers a structural question.", "tokens": [51061, 3066, 511, 655, 6338, 257, 15067, 1168, 13, 51145], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1401110804358194, "compression_ratio": 1.697674418604651, "no_speech_prob": 1.912197180112263e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 117446, "start": 1190.48, "end": 1193.28, "text": " How stable and well-defined is this specific region?", "tokens": [51166, 1012, 8351, 293, 731, 12, 37716, 307, 341, 2685, 4458, 30, 51306], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1401110804358194, "compression_ratio": 1.697674418604651, "no_speech_prob": 1.912197180112263e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 117446, "start": 1193.54, "end": 1198.06, "text": " So a solid block of granite in our wall has extremely high coherence.", "tokens": [51319, 407, 257, 5100, 3461, 295, 9370, 642, 294, 527, 2929, 575, 4664, 1090, 26528, 655, 13, 51545], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1401110804358194, "compression_ratio": 1.697674418604651, "no_speech_prob": 1.912197180112263e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 117446, "start": 1198.3600000000001, "end": 1201.3, "text": " It is a settled, rigid structure that resists change.", "tokens": [51560, 467, 307, 257, 14819, 11, 22195, 3877, 300, 725, 1751, 1319, 13, 51707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1401110804358194, "compression_ratio": 1.697674418604651, "no_speech_prob": 1.912197180112263e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 117446, "start": 1201.74, "end": 1203.92, "text": " Air, on the other hand, has lower coherence.", "tokens": [51729, 5774, 11, 322, 264, 661, 1011, 11, 575, 3126, 26528, 655, 13, 51838], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1401110804358194, "compression_ratio": 1.697674418604651, "no_speech_prob": 1.912197180112263e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 120392, "start": 1203.92, "end": 1204.3600000000001, "text": " Got it.", "tokens": [50365, 5803, 309, 13, 50387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18977954775788064, "compression_ratio": 1.6072607260726073, "no_speech_prob": 1.531096647036656e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 120392, "start": 1204.38, "end": 1205.7, "text": " So a solid wall has hi-fi.", "tokens": [50388, 407, 257, 5100, 2929, 575, 4879, 12, 13325, 13, 50454], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18977954775788064, "compression_ratio": 1.6072607260726073, "no_speech_prob": 1.531096647036656e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 120392, "start": 1205.8200000000002, "end": 1206.7, "text": " What's the second component?", "tokens": [50460, 708, 311, 264, 1150, 6542, 30, 50504], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18977954775788064, "compression_ratio": 1.6072607260726073, "no_speech_prob": 1.531096647036656e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 120392, "start": 1206.8600000000001, "end": 1208.9, "text": " The second is V, representing flow.", "tokens": [50512, 440, 1150, 307, 691, 11, 13460, 3095, 13, 50614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18977954775788064, "compression_ratio": 1.6072607260726073, "no_speech_prob": 1.531096647036656e-12}, {"id": 363, "seek": 120392, "start": 1209.16, "end": 1210.46, "text": " Flow, like movement.", "tokens": [50627, 32792, 11, 411, 3963, 13, 50692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18977954775788064, "compression_ratio": 1.6072607260726073, "no_speech_prob": 1.531096647036656e-12}, {"id": 364, "seek": 120392, "start": 1210.94, "end": 1211.38, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50716, 7587, 13, 50738], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18977954775788064, "compression_ratio": 1.6072607260726073, "no_speech_prob": 1.531096647036656e-12}, {"id": 365, "seek": 120392, "start": 1212.0600000000002, "end": 1213.88, "text": " Flow answers a dynamic question.", "tokens": [50772, 32792, 6338, 257, 8546, 1168, 13, 50863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18977954775788064, "compression_ratio": 1.6072607260726073, "no_speech_prob": 1.531096647036656e-12}, {"id": 366, "seek": 120392, "start": 1214.1200000000001, "end": 1215.42, "text": " Where is this region going?", "tokens": [50875, 2305, 307, 341, 4458, 516, 30, 50940], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18977954775788064, "compression_ratio": 1.6072607260726073, "no_speech_prob": 1.531096647036656e-12}, {"id": 367, "seek": 120392, "start": 1216.18, "end": 1218.74, "text": " It encodes directed change and momentum.", "tokens": [50978, 467, 2058, 4789, 12898, 1319, 293, 11244, 13, 51106], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18977954775788064, "compression_ratio": 1.6072607260726073, "no_speech_prob": 1.531096647036656e-12}, {"id": 368, "seek": 120392, "start": 1219.14, "end": 1219.48, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51126, 1033, 13, 51143], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18977954775788064, "compression_ratio": 1.6072607260726073, "no_speech_prob": 1.531096647036656e-12}, {"id": 369, "seek": 120392, "start": 1219.6200000000001, "end": 1226.5600000000002, "text": " If you have wind blowing through the courtyard or water cascading down the fountain or even a fire spreading across dry grass,", "tokens": [51150, 759, 291, 362, 2468, 15068, 807, 264, 41364, 420, 1281, 3058, 66, 8166, 760, 264, 29451, 420, 754, 257, 2610, 15232, 2108, 4016, 8054, 11, 51497], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18977954775788064, "compression_ratio": 1.6072607260726073, "no_speech_prob": 1.531096647036656e-12}, {"id": 370, "seek": 120392, "start": 1226.94, "end": 1232.1000000000001, "text": " that directional movement is represented in the vector flow of those specific points in the field.", "tokens": [51516, 300, 42242, 3963, 307, 10379, 294, 264, 8062, 3095, 295, 729, 2685, 2793, 294, 264, 2519, 13, 51774], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18977954775788064, "compression_ratio": 1.6072607260726073, "no_speech_prob": 1.531096647036656e-12}, {"id": 371, "seek": 120392, "start": 1232.3400000000001, "end": 1233.5, "text": " That completely tracks.", "tokens": [51786, 663, 2584, 10218, 13, 51844], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18977954775788064, "compression_ratio": 1.6072607260726073, "no_speech_prob": 1.531096647036656e-12}, {"id": 372, "seek": 123350, "start": 1233.5, "end": 1237.24, "text": " You need a way to store momentum independent of the object itself.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 643, 257, 636, 281, 3531, 11244, 6695, 295, 264, 2657, 2564, 13, 50552], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15457725524902344, "compression_ratio": 1.6592356687898089, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980683573321719e-12}, {"id": 373, "seek": 123350, "start": 1237.46, "end": 1237.94, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50563, 48746, 736, 13, 50587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15457725524902344, "compression_ratio": 1.6592356687898089, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980683573321719e-12}, {"id": 374, "seek": 123350, "start": 1238.28, "end": 1238.52, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50604, 1033, 13, 50616], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15457725524902344, "compression_ratio": 1.6592356687898089, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980683573321719e-12}, {"id": 375, "seek": 123350, "start": 1238.76, "end": 1241.2, "text": " The third component is S, which stands for entropy.", "tokens": [50628, 440, 2636, 6542, 307, 318, 11, 597, 7382, 337, 30867, 13, 50750], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15457725524902344, "compression_ratio": 1.6592356687898089, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980683573321719e-12}, {"id": 376, "seek": 123350, "start": 1241.86, "end": 1246.84, "text": " And this is the one that really, really forced me to rethink how simulations work.", "tokens": [50783, 400, 341, 307, 264, 472, 300, 534, 11, 534, 7579, 385, 281, 34595, 577, 35138, 589, 13, 51032], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15457725524902344, "compression_ratio": 1.6592356687898089, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980683573321719e-12}, {"id": 377, "seek": 123350, "start": 1246.96, "end": 1248.72, "text": " It's arguably the most important one.", "tokens": [51038, 467, 311, 26771, 264, 881, 1021, 472, 13, 51126], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15457725524902344, "compression_ratio": 1.6592356687898089, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980683573321719e-12}, {"id": 378, "seek": 123350, "start": 1249.04, "end": 1253.86, "text": " Entropy is perhaps the most crucial component for making the system computationally possible.", "tokens": [51142, 3951, 27514, 307, 4317, 264, 881, 11462, 6542, 337, 1455, 264, 1185, 24903, 379, 1944, 13, 51383], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15457725524902344, "compression_ratio": 1.6592356687898089, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980683573321719e-12}, {"id": 379, "seek": 123350, "start": 1254.14, "end": 1254.72, "text": " Why is that?", "tokens": [51397, 1545, 307, 300, 30, 51426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15457725524902344, "compression_ratio": 1.6592356687898089, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980683573321719e-12}, {"id": 380, "seek": 123350, "start": 1254.88, "end": 1257.0, "text": " Because entropy tracks honest uncertainty.", "tokens": [51434, 1436, 30867, 10218, 3245, 15697, 13, 51540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15457725524902344, "compression_ratio": 1.6592356687898089, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980683573321719e-12}, {"id": 381, "seek": 123350, "start": 1257.42, "end": 1260.48, "text": " It answers the question, what is not yet known about this coordinate?", "tokens": [51561, 467, 6338, 264, 1168, 11, 437, 307, 406, 1939, 2570, 466, 341, 15670, 30, 51714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15457725524902344, "compression_ratio": 1.6592356687898089, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980683573321719e-12}, {"id": 382, "seek": 123350, "start": 1260.68, "end": 1262.44, "text": " Wait, the world tracks what it doesn't know?", "tokens": [51724, 3802, 11, 264, 1002, 10218, 437, 309, 1177, 380, 458, 30, 51812], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15457725524902344, "compression_ratio": 1.6592356687898089, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980683573321719e-12}, {"id": 383, "seek": 126244, "start": 1262.44, "end": 1262.94, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50390], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19173606666358742, "compression_ratio": 1.4861878453038675, "no_speech_prob": 1.9969074137315967e-12}, {"id": 384, "seek": 126244, "start": 1262.94, "end": 1265.38, "text": " A region might be highly stable.", "tokens": [50390, 316, 4458, 1062, 312, 5405, 8351, 13, 50512], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19173606666358742, "compression_ratio": 1.4861878453038675, "no_speech_prob": 1.9969074137315967e-12}, {"id": 385, "seek": 126244, "start": 1265.8200000000002, "end": 1268.5, "text": " It might have high coherence, like a distant mountain.", "tokens": [50534, 467, 1062, 362, 1090, 26528, 655, 11, 411, 257, 17275, 6937, 13, 50668], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19173606666358742, "compression_ratio": 1.4861878453038675, "no_speech_prob": 1.9969074137315967e-12}, {"id": 386, "seek": 126244, "start": 1269.02, "end": 1275.96, "text": " But if you have only ever observed that mountain from a mile away, you don't actually know what the surface of the rock looks like up close.", "tokens": [50694, 583, 498, 291, 362, 787, 1562, 13095, 300, 6937, 490, 257, 12620, 1314, 11, 291, 500, 380, 767, 458, 437, 264, 3753, 295, 264, 3727, 1542, 411, 493, 1998, 13, 51041], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19173606666358742, "compression_ratio": 1.4861878453038675, "no_speech_prob": 1.9969074137315967e-12}, {"id": 387, "seek": 126244, "start": 1276.04, "end": 1276.16, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51045, 1779, 13, 51051], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19173606666358742, "compression_ratio": 1.4861878453038675, "no_speech_prob": 1.9969074137315967e-12}, {"id": 388, "seek": 126244, "start": 1276.22, "end": 1277.0800000000002, "text": " You haven't seen the gravel.", "tokens": [51054, 509, 2378, 380, 1612, 264, 30001, 13, 51097], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19173606666358742, "compression_ratio": 1.4861878453038675, "no_speech_prob": 1.9969074137315967e-12}, {"id": 389, "seek": 127708, "start": 1277.08, "end": 1278.08, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21033953442985628, "compression_ratio": 1.5170731707317073, "no_speech_prob": 1.700774503871072e-12}, {"id": 390, "seek": 127708, "start": 1278.54, "end": 1280.3999999999999, "text": " Entropy holds the space of possibility.", "tokens": [50438, 3951, 27514, 9190, 264, 1901, 295, 7959, 13, 50531], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21033953442985628, "compression_ratio": 1.5170731707317073, "no_speech_prob": 1.700774503871072e-12}, {"id": 391, "seek": 127708, "start": 1281.0, "end": 1286.6599999999999, "text": " It tracks what outcomes are still genuinely possible for that specific point in space.", "tokens": [50561, 467, 10218, 437, 10070, 366, 920, 17839, 1944, 337, 300, 2685, 935, 294, 1901, 13, 50844], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21033953442985628, "compression_ratio": 1.5170731707317073, "no_speech_prob": 1.700774503871072e-12}, {"id": 392, "seek": 127708, "start": 1286.84, "end": 1291.74, "text": " It's like the system formally admitting, I haven't looked closely at this patch of dirt yet.", "tokens": [50853, 467, 311, 411, 264, 1185, 25983, 44056, 11, 286, 2378, 380, 2956, 8185, 412, 341, 9972, 295, 11483, 1939, 13, 51098], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21033953442985628, "compression_ratio": 1.5170731707317073, "no_speech_prob": 1.700774503871072e-12}, {"id": 393, "seek": 127708, "start": 1291.8999999999999, "end": 1295.1399999999999, "text": " So I don't know if it's just dirt or if there's a gold coin buried there.", "tokens": [51106, 407, 286, 500, 380, 458, 498, 309, 311, 445, 11483, 420, 498, 456, 311, 257, 3821, 11464, 14101, 456, 13, 51268], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21033953442985628, "compression_ratio": 1.5170731707317073, "no_speech_prob": 1.700774503871072e-12}, {"id": 394, "seek": 127708, "start": 1295.3999999999999, "end": 1295.9199999999998, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51281, 7587, 13, 51307], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21033953442985628, "compression_ratio": 1.5170731707317073, "no_speech_prob": 1.700774503871072e-12}, {"id": 395, "seek": 129592, "start": 1295.92, "end": 1299.1000000000001, "text": " Instead of just guessing and rendering a coin, it stores the uncertainty.", "tokens": [50365, 7156, 295, 445, 17939, 293, 22407, 257, 11464, 11, 309, 9512, 264, 15697, 13, 50524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23311919700808642, "compression_ratio": 1.4893617021276595, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251267046142991e-12}, {"id": 396, "seek": 129592, "start": 1299.78, "end": 1300.3400000000001, "text": " That's brilliant.", "tokens": [50558, 663, 311, 10248, 13, 50586], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23311919700808642, "compression_ratio": 1.4893617021276595, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251267046142991e-12}, {"id": 397, "seek": 129592, "start": 1301.0800000000002, "end": 1303.54, "text": " That leads us to the fourth component, R.", "tokens": [50623, 663, 6689, 505, 281, 264, 6409, 6542, 11, 497, 13, 50746], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23311919700808642, "compression_ratio": 1.4893617021276595, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251267046142991e-12}, {"id": 398, "seek": 129592, "start": 1303.76, "end": 1305.3400000000001, "text": " R stands for residue.", "tokens": [50757, 497, 7382, 337, 34799, 13, 50836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23311919700808642, "compression_ratio": 1.4893617021276595, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251267046142991e-12}, {"id": 399, "seek": 129592, "start": 1305.8600000000001, "end": 1307.5600000000002, "text": " Residue is compressed history.", "tokens": [50862, 5015, 327, 622, 307, 30353, 2503, 13, 50947], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23311919700808642, "compression_ratio": 1.4893617021276595, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251267046142991e-12}, {"id": 400, "seek": 129592, "start": 1307.9, "end": 1308.76, "text": " Compressed history.", "tokens": [50964, 6620, 3805, 2503, 13, 51007], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23311919700808642, "compression_ratio": 1.4893617021276595, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251267046142991e-12}, {"id": 401, "seek": 129592, "start": 1309.14, "end": 1309.96, "text": " Like a logbook.", "tokens": [51026, 1743, 257, 3565, 2939, 13, 51067], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23311919700808642, "compression_ratio": 1.4893617021276595, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251267046142991e-12}, {"id": 402, "seek": 129592, "start": 1310.46, "end": 1311.0800000000002, "text": " Sort of.", "tokens": [51092, 26149, 295, 13, 51123], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23311919700808642, "compression_ratio": 1.4893617021276595, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251267046142991e-12}, {"id": 403, "seek": 129592, "start": 1311.18, "end": 1313.54, "text": " But it answers the question, what happened here?", "tokens": [51128, 583, 309, 6338, 264, 1168, 11, 437, 2011, 510, 30, 51246], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23311919700808642, "compression_ratio": 1.4893617021276595, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251267046142991e-12}, {"id": 404, "seek": 131354, "start": 1313.54, "end": 1319.34, "text": " It is not a massive, exhaustive video log of every single microsecond that passed.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 406, 257, 5994, 11, 14687, 488, 960, 3565, 295, 633, 2167, 3123, 37841, 18882, 300, 4678, 13, 50655], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14742857360839845, "compression_ratio": 1.6275167785234899, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684885894777124e-12}, {"id": 405, "seek": 131354, "start": 1319.52, "end": 1320.72, "text": " That would take up too much memory.", "tokens": [50664, 663, 576, 747, 493, 886, 709, 4675, 13, 50724], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14742857360839845, "compression_ratio": 1.6275167785234899, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684885894777124e-12}, {"id": 406, "seek": 131354, "start": 1320.86, "end": 1321.06, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50731, 1779, 13, 50741], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14742857360839845, "compression_ratio": 1.6275167785234899, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684885894777124e-12}, {"id": 407, "seek": 131354, "start": 1321.58, "end": 1325.34, "text": " Rather, it is the causal trace left behind by significant events.", "tokens": [50767, 16571, 11, 309, 307, 264, 38755, 13508, 1411, 2261, 538, 4776, 3931, 13, 50955], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14742857360839845, "compression_ratio": 1.6275167785234899, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684885894777124e-12}, {"id": 408, "seek": 131354, "start": 1325.46, "end": 1326.12, "text": " Give me an example.", "tokens": [50961, 5303, 385, 364, 1365, 13, 50994], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14742857360839845, "compression_ratio": 1.6275167785234899, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684885894777124e-12}, {"id": 409, "seek": 131354, "start": 1326.3999999999999, "end": 1335.58, "text": " If a tree fell in the forest, or if a character dug a trench in the mud, the residue component permanently records the structural disturbance caused by that specific event.", "tokens": [51008, 759, 257, 4230, 5696, 294, 264, 6719, 11, 420, 498, 257, 2517, 22954, 257, 39052, 294, 264, 8933, 11, 264, 34799, 6542, 24042, 7724, 264, 15067, 35684, 7008, 538, 300, 2685, 2280, 13, 51467], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14742857360839845, "compression_ratio": 1.6275167785234899, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684885894777124e-12}, {"id": 410, "seek": 131354, "start": 1335.74, "end": 1337.22, "text": " It's the scars on the world.", "tokens": [51475, 467, 311, 264, 31353, 322, 264, 1002, 13, 51549], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14742857360839845, "compression_ratio": 1.6275167785234899, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684885894777124e-12}, {"id": 411, "seek": 131354, "start": 1337.7, "end": 1340.18, "text": " Very poetic, but yes, essentially.", "tokens": [51573, 4372, 41080, 11, 457, 2086, 11, 4476, 13, 51697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14742857360839845, "compression_ratio": 1.6275167785234899, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684885894777124e-12}, {"id": 412, "seek": 131354, "start": 1340.36, "end": 1342.18, "text": " And finally, the fifth component, Z.", "tokens": [51706, 400, 2721, 11, 264, 9266, 6542, 11, 1176, 13, 51797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14742857360839845, "compression_ratio": 1.6275167785234899, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684885894777124e-12}, {"id": 413, "seek": 134218, "start": 1342.18, "end": 1344.54, "text": " Z is appearance.", "tokens": [50365, 1176, 307, 8967, 13, 50483], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16724363054547992, "compression_ratio": 1.5577689243027888, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899313336910747e-12}, {"id": 414, "seek": 134218, "start": 1345.3, "end": 1346.92, "text": " This answers the most immediate question.", "tokens": [50521, 639, 6338, 264, 881, 11629, 1168, 13, 50602], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16724363054547992, "compression_ratio": 1.5577689243027888, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899313336910747e-12}, {"id": 415, "seek": 134218, "start": 1347.38, "end": 1349.26, "text": " What does this point currently look like?", "tokens": [50625, 708, 775, 341, 935, 4362, 574, 411, 30, 50719], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16724363054547992, "compression_ratio": 1.5577689243027888, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899313336910747e-12}, {"id": 416, "seek": 134218, "start": 1349.42, "end": 1350.8200000000002, "text": " Okay, so just the visual data.", "tokens": [50727, 1033, 11, 370, 445, 264, 5056, 1412, 13, 50797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16724363054547992, "compression_ratio": 1.5577689243027888, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899313336910747e-12}, {"id": 417, "seek": 134218, "start": 1350.98, "end": 1351.22, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50805, 1079, 13, 50817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16724363054547992, "compression_ratio": 1.5577689243027888, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899313336910747e-12}, {"id": 418, "seek": 134218, "start": 1351.6200000000001, "end": 1359.4, "text": " It is the resolved, perceivable content that a camera, a sensor, or an eye actually picks up when it looks at that coordinate.", "tokens": [50837, 467, 307, 264, 20772, 11, 9016, 34376, 2701, 300, 257, 2799, 11, 257, 10200, 11, 420, 364, 3313, 767, 16137, 493, 562, 309, 1542, 412, 300, 15670, 13, 51226], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16724363054547992, "compression_ratio": 1.5577689243027888, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899313336910747e-12}, {"id": 419, "seek": 134218, "start": 1359.72, "end": 1366.2, "text": " Okay, so to recap, every point in the universe holds coherence, flow, entropy, residue, and appearance.", "tokens": [51242, 1033, 11, 370, 281, 20928, 11, 633, 935, 294, 264, 6445, 9190, 26528, 655, 11, 3095, 11, 30867, 11, 34799, 11, 293, 8967, 13, 51566], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16724363054547992, "compression_ratio": 1.5577689243027888, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899313336910747e-12}, {"id": 420, "seek": 134218, "start": 1366.22, "end": 1367.46, "text": " As the foundation, yes.", "tokens": [51567, 1018, 264, 7030, 11, 2086, 13, 51629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16724363054547992, "compression_ratio": 1.5577689243027888, "no_speech_prob": 1.4899313336910747e-12}, {"id": 421, "seek": 136746, "start": 1367.46, "end": 1374.92, "text": " But having a list of values doesn't create a reality unless there are unbreakable rules governing how those values interact, right?", "tokens": [50365, 583, 1419, 257, 1329, 295, 4190, 1177, 380, 1884, 257, 4103, 5969, 456, 366, 517, 13225, 712, 4474, 30054, 577, 729, 4190, 4648, 11, 558, 30, 50738], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15754486532772288, "compression_ratio": 1.478494623655914, "no_speech_prob": 2.0206074227008264e-12}, {"id": 422, "seek": 136746, "start": 1374.96, "end": 1375.1200000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50740, 1779, 13, 50748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15754486532772288, "compression_ratio": 1.478494623655914, "no_speech_prob": 2.0206074227008264e-12}, {"id": 423, "seek": 136746, "start": 1375.5, "end": 1376.48, "text": " A list is just data.", "tokens": [50767, 316, 1329, 307, 445, 1412, 13, 50816], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15754486532772288, "compression_ratio": 1.478494623655914, "no_speech_prob": 2.0206074227008264e-12}, {"id": 424, "seek": 136746, "start": 1376.8400000000001, "end": 1380.08, "text": " And the text lays out golden rules for the semantic field.", "tokens": [50834, 400, 264, 2487, 32714, 484, 9729, 4474, 337, 264, 47982, 2519, 13, 50996], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15754486532772288, "compression_ratio": 1.478494623655914, "no_speech_prob": 2.0206074227008264e-12}, {"id": 425, "seek": 136746, "start": 1380.82, "end": 1382.88, "text": " The most important one is called the entropy constraint.", "tokens": [51033, 440, 881, 1021, 472, 307, 1219, 264, 30867, 25534, 13, 51136], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15754486532772288, "compression_ratio": 1.478494623655914, "no_speech_prob": 2.0206074227008264e-12}, {"id": 426, "seek": 138288, "start": 1382.88, "end": 1385.98, "text": " Walk us through how this governs the simulation.", "tokens": [50365, 10818, 505, 807, 577, 341, 1980, 82, 264, 16575, 13, 50520], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13916598558425902, "compression_ratio": 1.5714285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.721181248741377e-12}, {"id": 427, "seek": 138288, "start": 1385.98, "end": 1390.6000000000001, "text": " The entropy constraint dictates a fundamental law of physics for this virtual universe.", "tokens": [50520, 440, 30867, 25534, 12569, 1024, 257, 8088, 2101, 295, 10649, 337, 341, 6374, 6445, 13, 50751], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13916598558425902, "compression_ratio": 1.5714285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.721181248741377e-12}, {"id": 428, "seek": 138288, "start": 1391.5400000000002, "end": 1395.2, "text": " Entropy, S, can never decrease in an unobserved area.", "tokens": [50798, 3951, 27514, 11, 318, 11, 393, 1128, 11514, 294, 364, 8526, 929, 6913, 1859, 13, 50981], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13916598558425902, "compression_ratio": 1.5714285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.721181248741377e-12}, {"id": 429, "seek": 138288, "start": 1395.3000000000002, "end": 1396.18, "text": " Never decrease.", "tokens": [50986, 7344, 11514, 13, 51030], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13916598558425902, "compression_ratio": 1.5714285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.721181248741377e-12}, {"id": 430, "seek": 138288, "start": 1396.7, "end": 1403.7800000000002, "text": " Which means the AI is mathematically forbidden from secretly deciding what is around the corner until I actually walk around the corner and look.", "tokens": [51056, 3013, 1355, 264, 7318, 307, 44003, 25990, 490, 22611, 17990, 437, 307, 926, 264, 4538, 1826, 286, 767, 1792, 926, 264, 4538, 293, 574, 13, 51410], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13916598558425902, "compression_ratio": 1.5714285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.721181248741377e-12}, {"id": 431, "seek": 140378, "start": 1403.78, "end": 1408.3, "text": " Exactly. The world is not allowed to quietly become more certain about itself in the dark.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 440, 1002, 307, 406, 4350, 281, 19141, 1813, 544, 1629, 466, 2564, 294, 264, 2877, 13, 50591], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1330265531352922, "compression_ratio": 1.6007326007326008, "no_speech_prob": 2.772338131631913e-12}, {"id": 432, "seek": 140378, "start": 1408.56, "end": 1409.6, "text": " Oh, that's so cool.", "tokens": [50604, 876, 11, 300, 311, 370, 1627, 13, 50656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1330265531352922, "compression_ratio": 1.6007326007326008, "no_speech_prob": 2.772338131631913e-12}, {"id": 433, "seek": 140378, "start": 1409.94, "end": 1411.42, "text": " Now, uncertainty can grow.", "tokens": [50673, 823, 11, 15697, 393, 1852, 13, 50747], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1330265531352922, "compression_ratio": 1.6007326007326008, "no_speech_prob": 2.772338131631913e-12}, {"id": 434, "seek": 140378, "start": 1412.1, "end": 1418.3799999999999, "text": " If a massive storm rolled into the courtyard while you were inside, the wind and rain might scramble the environment.", "tokens": [50781, 759, 257, 5994, 7679, 14306, 666, 264, 41364, 1339, 291, 645, 1854, 11, 264, 2468, 293, 4830, 1062, 795, 48382, 264, 2823, 13, 51095], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1330265531352922, "compression_ratio": 1.6007326007326008, "no_speech_prob": 2.772338131631913e-12}, {"id": 435, "seek": 140378, "start": 1419.02, "end": 1425.94, "text": " That increases the entropy of the courtyard because the system knows things have been disturbed, but it doesn't know exactly how they landed.", "tokens": [51127, 663, 8637, 264, 30867, 295, 264, 41364, 570, 264, 1185, 3255, 721, 362, 668, 30558, 11, 457, 309, 1177, 380, 458, 2293, 577, 436, 15336, 13, 51473], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1330265531352922, "compression_ratio": 1.6007326007326008, "no_speech_prob": 2.772338131631913e-12}, {"id": 436, "seek": 140378, "start": 1426.32, "end": 1428.26, "text": " Right. The storm randomized the leaves.", "tokens": [51492, 1779, 13, 440, 7679, 38513, 264, 5510, 13, 51589], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1330265531352922, "compression_ratio": 1.6007326007326008, "no_speech_prob": 2.772338131631913e-12}, {"id": 437, "seek": 142826, "start": 1428.26, "end": 1438.16, "text": " Yes. But uncertainty can only shrink. It can only resolve into a specific hard fact when an observation event actually does the work of looking at it.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 583, 15697, 393, 787, 23060, 13, 467, 393, 787, 14151, 666, 257, 2685, 1152, 1186, 562, 364, 14816, 2280, 767, 775, 264, 589, 295, 1237, 412, 309, 13, 50860], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1418946219272301, "compression_ratio": 1.734982332155477, "no_speech_prob": 1.966105446851718e-12}, {"id": 438, "seek": 142826, "start": 1438.66, "end": 1441.08, "text": " The text uses a really great phrase for this.", "tokens": [50885, 440, 2487, 4960, 257, 534, 869, 9535, 337, 341, 13, 51006], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1418946219272301, "compression_ratio": 1.734982332155477, "no_speech_prob": 1.966105446851718e-12}, {"id": 439, "seek": 142826, "start": 1441.82, "end": 1443.9, "text": " Ignorance is structured, not blank.", "tokens": [51043, 24754, 284, 719, 307, 18519, 11, 406, 8247, 13, 51147], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1418946219272301, "compression_ratio": 1.734982332155477, "no_speech_prob": 1.966105446851718e-12}, {"id": 440, "seek": 142826, "start": 1444.3799999999999, "end": 1450.44, "text": " Ignorance is structured. That completely eliminates the problem of the AI hallucinating things off screen and then getting confused.", "tokens": [51171, 24754, 284, 719, 307, 18519, 13, 663, 2584, 49893, 264, 1154, 295, 264, 7318, 35212, 8205, 721, 766, 2568, 293, 550, 1242, 9019, 13, 51474], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1418946219272301, "compression_ratio": 1.734982332155477, "no_speech_prob": 1.966105446851718e-12}, {"id": 441, "seek": 142826, "start": 1450.56, "end": 1451.66, "text": " It solves it at the root.", "tokens": [51480, 467, 39890, 309, 412, 264, 5593, 13, 51535], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1418946219272301, "compression_ratio": 1.734982332155477, "no_speech_prob": 1.966105446851718e-12}, {"id": 442, "seek": 142826, "start": 1451.96, "end": 1453.78, "text": " But what actually happens when I do look.", "tokens": [51550, 583, 437, 767, 2314, 562, 286, 360, 574, 13, 51641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1418946219272301, "compression_ratio": 1.734982332155477, "no_speech_prob": 1.966105446851718e-12}, {"id": 443, "seek": 142826, "start": 1453.9, "end": 1454.14, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51647, 865, 13, 51659], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1418946219272301, "compression_ratio": 1.734982332155477, "no_speech_prob": 1.966105446851718e-12}, {"id": 444, "seek": 142826, "start": 1454.7, "end": 1456.0, "text": " Because eventually I have to turn the corner.", "tokens": [51687, 1436, 4728, 286, 362, 281, 1261, 264, 4538, 13, 51752], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1418946219272301, "compression_ratio": 1.734982332155477, "no_speech_prob": 1.966105446851718e-12}, {"id": 445, "seek": 142826, "start": 1456.24, "end": 1456.48, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51764, 865, 13, 51776], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1418946219272301, "compression_ratio": 1.734982332155477, "no_speech_prob": 1.966105446851718e-12}, {"id": 446, "seek": 145648, "start": 1456.48, "end": 1461.44, "text": " That brings us to the second golden rule, which the text calls the invention to memory principle.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 1150, 9729, 4978, 11, 597, 264, 2487, 5498, 264, 22265, 281, 4675, 8665, 13, 50613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11513986392897002, "compression_ratio": 1.5793357933579335, "no_speech_prob": 1.367247786342174e-12}, {"id": 447, "seek": 145648, "start": 1461.76, "end": 1471.92, "text": " Right. When you look at an uncertain high entropy region, say you walk up to a blurry, distant patch of the courtyard wall, the AI is forced to invent an appearance.", "tokens": [50629, 1779, 13, 1133, 291, 574, 412, 364, 11308, 1090, 30867, 4458, 11, 584, 291, 1792, 493, 281, 257, 37644, 11, 17275, 9972, 295, 264, 41364, 2929, 11, 264, 7318, 307, 7579, 281, 7962, 364, 8967, 13, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11513986392897002, "compression_ratio": 1.5793357933579335, "no_speech_prob": 1.367247786342174e-12}, {"id": 448, "seek": 145648, "start": 1472.1, "end": 1472.88, "text": " A surrender something.", "tokens": [51146, 316, 22185, 746, 13, 51185], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11513986392897002, "compression_ratio": 1.5793357933579335, "no_speech_prob": 1.367247786342174e-12}, {"id": 449, "seek": 145648, "start": 1473.14, "end": 1480.94, "text": " It must collapse that space of possibility into a specific detail, like a particular arrangement of stones or a specific patch of moss.", "tokens": [51198, 467, 1633, 15584, 300, 1901, 295, 7959, 666, 257, 2685, 2607, 11, 411, 257, 1729, 17620, 295, 14083, 420, 257, 2685, 9972, 295, 36193, 13, 51588], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11513986392897002, "compression_ratio": 1.5793357933579335, "no_speech_prob": 1.367247786342174e-12}, {"id": 450, "seek": 145648, "start": 1481.16, "end": 1481.46, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51599, 1033, 13, 51614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11513986392897002, "compression_ratio": 1.5793357933579335, "no_speech_prob": 1.367247786342174e-12}, {"id": 451, "seek": 148146, "start": 1481.46, "end": 1484.4, "text": " But the critical mechanic is what happens next.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 4924, 23860, 307, 437, 2314, 958, 13, 50512], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16528809535038935, "compression_ratio": 1.5502645502645502, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956320687140034e-12}, {"id": 452, "seek": 148146, "start": 1485.04, "end": 1492.5, "text": " Having invented that detail, the field is obligated by the math to lock that appearance in as ze, the appearance component.", "tokens": [50544, 10222, 14479, 300, 2607, 11, 264, 2519, 307, 9270, 770, 538, 264, 5221, 281, 4017, 300, 8967, 294, 382, 5277, 11, 264, 8967, 6542, 13, 50917], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16528809535038935, "compression_ratio": 1.5502645502645502, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956320687140034e-12}, {"id": 453, "seek": 148146, "start": 1492.66, "end": 1493.74, "text": " So it's permanent now.", "tokens": [50925, 407, 309, 311, 10996, 586, 13, 50979], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16528809535038935, "compression_ratio": 1.5502645502645502, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956320687140034e-12}, {"id": 454, "seek": 148146, "start": 1493.92, "end": 1494.2, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50988, 1079, 13, 51002], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16528809535038935, "compression_ratio": 1.5502645502645502, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956320687140034e-12}, {"id": 455, "seek": 148146, "start": 1494.54, "end": 1500.54, "text": " The next time you look at that exact spot, it is a read operation, not a re-render operation.", "tokens": [51019, 440, 958, 565, 291, 574, 412, 300, 1900, 4008, 11, 309, 307, 257, 1401, 6916, 11, 406, 257, 319, 12, 13292, 6916, 13, 51319], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16528809535038935, "compression_ratio": 1.5502645502645502, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956320687140034e-12}, {"id": 456, "seek": 150054, "start": 1500.54, "end": 1504.46, "text": " You invent it once, and then you are forced to remember it forever.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 7962, 309, 1564, 11, 293, 550, 291, 366, 7579, 281, 1604, 309, 5680, 13, 50561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10676770922781408, "compression_ratio": 1.5114155251141552, "no_speech_prob": 1.3724716892496436e-12}, {"id": 457, "seek": 150054, "start": 1504.86, "end": 1507.8, "text": " Or, well, at least until a physical force in the world changes it.", "tokens": [50581, 1610, 11, 731, 11, 412, 1935, 1826, 257, 4001, 3464, 294, 264, 1002, 2962, 309, 13, 50728], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10676770922781408, "compression_ratio": 1.5114155251141552, "no_speech_prob": 1.3724716892496436e-12}, {"id": 458, "seek": 150054, "start": 1507.86, "end": 1508.26, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50731, 7587, 13, 50751], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10676770922781408, "compression_ratio": 1.5114155251141552, "no_speech_prob": 1.3724716892496436e-12}, {"id": 459, "seek": 150054, "start": 1508.54, "end": 1515.3799999999999, "text": " And that is the exact opposite of how current generative AI works, where it just keeps reinventing the wheel every single time you prompt it.", "tokens": [50765, 400, 300, 307, 264, 1900, 6182, 295, 577, 2190, 1337, 1166, 7318, 1985, 11, 689, 309, 445, 5965, 33477, 278, 264, 5589, 633, 2167, 565, 291, 12391, 309, 13, 51107], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10676770922781408, "compression_ratio": 1.5114155251141552, "no_speech_prob": 1.3724716892496436e-12}, {"id": 460, "seek": 150054, "start": 1515.5, "end": 1515.76, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51113, 1779, 13, 51126], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10676770922781408, "compression_ratio": 1.5114155251141552, "no_speech_prob": 1.3724716892496436e-12}, {"id": 461, "seek": 150054, "start": 1515.8799999999999, "end": 1517.6599999999999, "text": " Current AI is just a memoryless dream.", "tokens": [51132, 15629, 7318, 307, 445, 257, 4675, 1832, 3055, 13, 51221], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10676770922781408, "compression_ratio": 1.5114155251141552, "no_speech_prob": 1.3724716892496436e-12}, {"id": 462, "seek": 151766, "start": 1517.66, "end": 1523.78, "text": " In this field theory, reinventing an already settled low entropy region is structurally impossible.", "tokens": [50365, 682, 341, 2519, 5261, 11, 33477, 278, 364, 1217, 14819, 2295, 30867, 4458, 307, 6594, 6512, 6243, 13, 50671], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17051738975322353, "compression_ratio": 1.571917808219178, "no_speech_prob": 1.4269203223518656e-12}, {"id": 463, "seek": 151766, "start": 1524.5800000000002, "end": 1531.28, "text": " The rules of math simply forbid the generative model from overriding a defined coordinate without a physical cause.", "tokens": [50711, 440, 4474, 295, 5221, 2935, 34117, 264, 1337, 1166, 2316, 490, 670, 81, 2819, 257, 7642, 15670, 1553, 257, 4001, 3082, 13, 51046], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17051738975322353, "compression_ratio": 1.571917808219178, "no_speech_prob": 1.4269203223518656e-12}, {"id": 464, "seek": 151766, "start": 1531.48, "end": 1536.2, "text": " Now, when I was reading through the five components of memory, I noticed something conspicuously missing.", "tokens": [51056, 823, 11, 562, 286, 390, 3760, 807, 264, 1732, 6677, 295, 4675, 11, 286, 5694, 746, 1014, 37509, 84, 5098, 5361, 13, 51292], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17051738975322353, "compression_ratio": 1.571917808219178, "no_speech_prob": 1.4269203223518656e-12}, {"id": 465, "seek": 151766, "start": 1536.48, "end": 1536.8400000000001, "text": " Oh.", "tokens": [51306, 876, 13, 51324], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17051738975322353, "compression_ratio": 1.571917808219178, "no_speech_prob": 1.4269203223518656e-12}, {"id": 466, "seek": 151766, "start": 1537.8000000000002, "end": 1538.44, "text": " What was that?", "tokens": [51372, 708, 390, 300, 30, 51404], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17051738975322353, "compression_ratio": 1.571917808219178, "no_speech_prob": 1.4269203223518656e-12}, {"id": 467, "seek": 151766, "start": 1538.6000000000001, "end": 1544.3000000000002, "text": " When we think about objects in a game, we usually define them by what we can do with them, right?", "tokens": [51412, 1133, 321, 519, 466, 6565, 294, 257, 1216, 11, 321, 2673, 6964, 552, 538, 437, 321, 393, 360, 365, 552, 11, 558, 30, 51697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17051738975322353, "compression_ratio": 1.571917808219178, "no_speech_prob": 1.4269203223518656e-12}, {"id": 468, "seek": 151766, "start": 1544.3400000000001, "end": 1544.96, "text": " It's for ordinances.", "tokens": [51699, 467, 311, 337, 25376, 2676, 13, 51730], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17051738975322353, "compression_ratio": 1.571917808219178, "no_speech_prob": 1.4269203223518656e-12}, {"id": 469, "seek": 154496, "start": 1544.96, "end": 1550.28, "text": " Exactly. A ladder is for climbing. A chair is for sitting. A door is for opening.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 316, 18325, 307, 337, 14780, 13, 316, 6090, 307, 337, 3798, 13, 316, 2853, 307, 337, 5193, 13, 50631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13810647208735627, "compression_ratio": 1.6044776119402986, "no_speech_prob": 1.920545536840401e-12}, {"id": 470, "seek": 154496, "start": 1550.76, "end": 1553.16, "text": " These are affordances in game design.", "tokens": [50655, 1981, 366, 6157, 2676, 294, 1216, 1715, 13, 50775], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13810647208735627, "compression_ratio": 1.6044776119402986, "no_speech_prob": 1.920545536840401e-12}, {"id": 471, "seek": 154496, "start": 1554.04, "end": 1558.72, "text": " But the text deliberately removed affordances from the semantic field itself.", "tokens": [50819, 583, 264, 2487, 23506, 7261, 6157, 2676, 490, 264, 47982, 2519, 2564, 13, 51053], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13810647208735627, "compression_ratio": 1.6044776119402986, "no_speech_prob": 1.920545536840401e-12}, {"id": 472, "seek": 154496, "start": 1558.98, "end": 1559.42, "text": " You did.", "tokens": [51066, 509, 630, 13, 51088], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13810647208735627, "compression_ratio": 1.6044776119402986, "no_speech_prob": 1.920545536840401e-12}, {"id": 473, "seek": 154496, "start": 1559.76, "end": 1564.02, "text": " Why? Why isn't the property of climbability stored inside the ladder?", "tokens": [51105, 1545, 30, 1545, 1943, 380, 264, 4707, 295, 10724, 2310, 12187, 1854, 264, 18325, 30, 51318], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13810647208735627, "compression_ratio": 1.6044776119402986, "no_speech_prob": 1.920545536840401e-12}, {"id": 474, "seek": 154496, "start": 1564.58, "end": 1569.94, "text": " The author answers this with a pretty brilliant thought experiment involving a ladder and a goldfish.", "tokens": [51346, 440, 3793, 6338, 341, 365, 257, 1238, 10248, 1194, 5120, 17030, 257, 18325, 293, 257, 3821, 11608, 13, 51614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13810647208735627, "compression_ratio": 1.6044776119402986, "no_speech_prob": 1.920545536840401e-12}, {"id": 475, "seek": 154496, "start": 1570.04, "end": 1572.42, "text": " Oh, I love this part. Explain the goldfish analogy.", "tokens": [51619, 876, 11, 286, 959, 341, 644, 13, 39574, 264, 3821, 11608, 21663, 13, 51738], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13810647208735627, "compression_ratio": 1.6044776119402986, "no_speech_prob": 1.920545536840401e-12}, {"id": 476, "seek": 157242, "start": 1572.42, "end": 1577.76, "text": " If you place a wooden ladder in the middle of a room, that ladder affords climbing to a human being.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 1081, 257, 14744, 18325, 294, 264, 2808, 295, 257, 1808, 11, 300, 18325, 2096, 5703, 14780, 281, 257, 1952, 885, 13, 50632], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10515691057036194, "compression_ratio": 1.6353591160220995, "no_speech_prob": 1.585640364669405e-12}, {"id": 477, "seek": 157242, "start": 1578.02, "end": 1581.0600000000002, "text": " The human has the physical geometry and the strength to use it.", "tokens": [50645, 440, 1952, 575, 264, 4001, 18426, 293, 264, 3800, 281, 764, 309, 13, 50797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10515691057036194, "compression_ratio": 1.6353591160220995, "no_speech_prob": 1.585640364669405e-12}, {"id": 478, "seek": 157242, "start": 1581.28, "end": 1581.42, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50808, 1779, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10515691057036194, "compression_ratio": 1.6353591160220995, "no_speech_prob": 1.585640364669405e-12}, {"id": 479, "seek": 157242, "start": 1581.6200000000001, "end": 1587.0600000000002, "text": " But if you place a goldfish in a bowl in that same room, the ladder does not afford climbing to the goldfish.", "tokens": [50825, 583, 498, 291, 1081, 257, 3821, 11608, 294, 257, 6571, 294, 300, 912, 1808, 11, 264, 18325, 775, 406, 6157, 14780, 281, 264, 3821, 11608, 13, 51097], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10515691057036194, "compression_ratio": 1.6353591160220995, "no_speech_prob": 1.585640364669405e-12}, {"id": 480, "seek": 157242, "start": 1587.14, "end": 1587.74, "text": " Obviously not.", "tokens": [51101, 7580, 406, 13, 51131], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10515691057036194, "compression_ratio": 1.6353591160220995, "no_speech_prob": 1.585640364669405e-12}, {"id": 481, "seek": 158774, "start": 1587.74, "end": 1591.3, "text": " But the ladder itself, at a molecular level, has not changed at all.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 18325, 2564, 11, 412, 257, 19046, 1496, 11, 575, 406, 3105, 412, 439, 13, 50543], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1666234850883484, "compression_ratio": 1.59375, "no_speech_prob": 1.83245584504943e-12}, {"id": 482, "seek": 158774, "start": 1591.38, "end": 1591.58, "text": " Oh.", "tokens": [50547, 876, 13, 50557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1666234850883484, "compression_ratio": 1.59375, "no_speech_prob": 1.83245584504943e-12}, {"id": 483, "seek": 158774, "start": 1591.7, "end": 1593.8, "text": " What changed is the capability of the observer.", "tokens": [50563, 708, 3105, 307, 264, 13759, 295, 264, 27878, 13, 50668], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1666234850883484, "compression_ratio": 1.59375, "no_speech_prob": 1.83245584504943e-12}, {"id": 484, "seek": 158774, "start": 1594.24, "end": 1603.72, "text": " If you were to store affordance in the semantic field as a core property of the ladder itself, it would have to be an absolute objective fact of the universe.", "tokens": [50690, 759, 291, 645, 281, 3531, 6157, 719, 294, 264, 47982, 2519, 382, 257, 4965, 4707, 295, 264, 18325, 2564, 11, 309, 576, 362, 281, 312, 364, 8236, 10024, 1186, 295, 264, 6445, 13, 51164], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1666234850883484, "compression_ratio": 1.59375, "no_speech_prob": 1.83245584504943e-12}, {"id": 485, "seek": 158774, "start": 1603.9, "end": 1604.88, "text": " I mean, it's not absolute.", "tokens": [51173, 286, 914, 11, 309, 311, 406, 8236, 13, 51222], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1666234850883484, "compression_ratio": 1.59375, "no_speech_prob": 1.83245584504943e-12}, {"id": 486, "seek": 160488, "start": 1604.88, "end": 1618.3400000000001, "text": " So how does the system know I can climb the ladder if the ladder doesn't know it's climbable?", "tokens": [50365, 407, 577, 775, 264, 1185, 458, 286, 393, 10724, 264, 18325, 498, 264, 18325, 1177, 380, 458, 309, 311, 10724, 712, 30, 51038], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2537847849038931, "compression_ratio": 1.2236842105263157, "no_speech_prob": 1.825320710552303e-12}, {"id": 487, "seek": 161834, "start": 1618.34, "end": 1621.1, "text": " The field presents what the text calls cues.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2519, 13533, 437, 264, 2487, 5498, 32192, 13, 50503], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17284925678108312, "compression_ratio": 1.5048076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.41051634348216e-12}, {"id": 488, "seek": 161834, "start": 1621.56, "end": 1621.8999999999999, "text": " Cues.", "tokens": [50526, 383, 1247, 13, 50543], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17284925678108312, "compression_ratio": 1.5048076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.41051634348216e-12}, {"id": 489, "seek": 161834, "start": 1622.12, "end": 1625.76, "text": " A cue is just a localized geometric or semantic pattern.", "tokens": [50554, 316, 22656, 307, 445, 257, 44574, 33246, 420, 47982, 5102, 13, 50736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17284925678108312, "compression_ratio": 1.5048076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.41051634348216e-12}, {"id": 490, "seek": 161834, "start": 1626.3, "end": 1628.72, "text": " The silhouette of a rung, the height of a step.", "tokens": [50763, 440, 38275, 295, 257, 367, 1063, 11, 264, 6681, 295, 257, 1823, 13, 50884], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17284925678108312, "compression_ratio": 1.5048076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.41051634348216e-12}, {"id": 491, "seek": 161834, "start": 1628.8799999999999, "end": 1629.12, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50892, 1033, 13, 50904], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17284925678108312, "compression_ratio": 1.5048076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.41051634348216e-12}, {"id": 492, "seek": 161834, "start": 1629.3799999999999, "end": 1638.4599999999998, "text": " If a human agent approaches the ladder, the human's own capability model recognizes those cues, and that recognition activates the climbing affordance.", "tokens": [50917, 759, 257, 1952, 9461, 11587, 264, 18325, 11, 264, 1952, 311, 1065, 13759, 2316, 26564, 729, 32192, 11, 293, 300, 11150, 43869, 264, 14780, 6157, 719, 13, 51371], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17284925678108312, "compression_ratio": 1.5048076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.41051634348216e-12}, {"id": 493, "seek": 163846, "start": 1638.46, "end": 1641.26, "text": " The world doesn't dictate what you can do.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1002, 1177, 380, 36071, 437, 291, 393, 360, 13, 50505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1077198193767878, "compression_ratio": 1.7290969899665551, "no_speech_prob": 1.274453307643919e-12}, {"id": 494, "seek": 163846, "start": 1641.48, "end": 1647.6200000000001, "text": " It just sits there, presenting physical cues, and your own capabilities determine how you can interact with them.", "tokens": [50516, 467, 445, 12696, 456, 11, 15578, 4001, 32192, 11, 293, 428, 1065, 10862, 6997, 577, 291, 393, 4648, 365, 552, 13, 50823], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1077198193767878, "compression_ratio": 1.7290969899665551, "no_speech_prob": 1.274453307643919e-12}, {"id": 495, "seek": 163846, "start": 1647.8600000000001, "end": 1650.3, "text": " It is such an elegant way to handle interaction.", "tokens": [50835, 467, 307, 1270, 364, 21117, 636, 281, 4813, 9285, 13, 50957], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1077198193767878, "compression_ratio": 1.7290969899665551, "no_speech_prob": 1.274453307643919e-12}, {"id": 496, "seek": 163846, "start": 1650.6200000000001, "end": 1652.4, "text": " It keeps the world state so pristine.", "tokens": [50973, 467, 5965, 264, 1002, 1785, 370, 582, 42745, 13, 51062], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1077198193767878, "compression_ratio": 1.7290969899665551, "no_speech_prob": 1.274453307643919e-12}, {"id": 497, "seek": 163846, "start": 1652.56, "end": 1654.5, "text": " It really minimizes data bloat.", "tokens": [51070, 467, 534, 4464, 5660, 1412, 1749, 267, 13, 51167], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1077198193767878, "compression_ratio": 1.7290969899665551, "no_speech_prob": 1.274453307643919e-12}, {"id": 498, "seek": 163846, "start": 1654.56, "end": 1654.7, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51170, 865, 13, 51177], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1077198193767878, "compression_ratio": 1.7290969899665551, "no_speech_prob": 1.274453307643919e-12}, {"id": 499, "seek": 163846, "start": 1654.8, "end": 1657.52, "text": " The world only has to remember what is physically true.", "tokens": [51182, 440, 1002, 787, 575, 281, 1604, 437, 307, 9762, 2074, 13, 51318], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1077198193767878, "compression_ratio": 1.7290969899665551, "no_speech_prob": 1.274453307643919e-12}, {"id": 500, "seek": 163846, "start": 1657.74, "end": 1659.54, "text": " The coherence, the flow, the entropy.", "tokens": [51329, 440, 26528, 655, 11, 264, 3095, 11, 264, 30867, 13, 51419], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1077198193767878, "compression_ratio": 1.7290969899665551, "no_speech_prob": 1.274453307643919e-12}, {"id": 501, "seek": 163846, "start": 1659.92, "end": 1665.6200000000001, "text": " It doesn't have to clutter its database with infinite lists of what every possible creature in the universe might potentially do with a rock.", "tokens": [51438, 467, 1177, 380, 362, 281, 40614, 1080, 8149, 365, 13785, 14511, 295, 437, 633, 1944, 12797, 294, 264, 6445, 1062, 7263, 360, 365, 257, 3727, 13, 51723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1077198193767878, "compression_ratio": 1.7290969899665551, "no_speech_prob": 1.274453307643919e-12}, {"id": 502, "seek": 166562, "start": 1665.62, "end": 1671.34, "text": " It separates the physics of the world from the biology or the programming of the agents moving through it.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 34149, 264, 10649, 295, 264, 1002, 490, 264, 14956, 420, 264, 9410, 295, 264, 12554, 2684, 807, 309, 13, 50651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21279044378371464, "compression_ratio": 1.4884792626728112, "no_speech_prob": 1.839638033920843e-12}, {"id": 503, "seek": 166562, "start": 1671.54, "end": 1673.9799999999998, "text": " So we have built the semantic field.", "tokens": [50661, 407, 321, 362, 3094, 264, 47982, 2519, 13, 50783], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21279044378371464, "compression_ratio": 1.4884792626728112, "no_speech_prob": 1.839638033920843e-12}, {"id": 504, "seek": 166562, "start": 1674.6999999999998, "end": 1677.58, "text": " We know what it's made of, and we know the rules it has to follow.", "tokens": [50819, 492, 458, 437, 309, 311, 1027, 295, 11, 293, 321, 458, 264, 4474, 309, 575, 281, 1524, 13, 50963], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21279044378371464, "compression_ratio": 1.4884792626728112, "no_speech_prob": 1.839638033920843e-12}, {"id": 505, "seek": 166562, "start": 1678.3, "end": 1681.34, "text": " But here is where the mechanics get really fascinating.", "tokens": [50999, 583, 510, 307, 689, 264, 12939, 483, 534, 10343, 13, 51151], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21279044378371464, "compression_ratio": 1.4884792626728112, "no_speech_prob": 1.839638033920843e-12}, {"id": 506, "seek": 166562, "start": 1681.54, "end": 1682.3, "text": " The right cycle.", "tokens": [51161, 440, 558, 6586, 13, 51199], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21279044378371464, "compression_ratio": 1.4884792626728112, "no_speech_prob": 1.839638033920843e-12}, {"id": 507, "seek": 166562, "start": 1682.54, "end": 1683.02, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51211, 7587, 13, 51235], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21279044378371464, "compression_ratio": 1.4884792626728112, "no_speech_prob": 1.839638033920843e-12}, {"id": 508, "seek": 166562, "start": 1684.06, "end": 1685.7199999999998, "text": " How does anything ever change?", "tokens": [51287, 1012, 775, 1340, 1562, 1319, 30, 51370], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21279044378371464, "compression_ratio": 1.4884792626728112, "no_speech_prob": 1.839638033920843e-12}, {"id": 509, "seek": 168572, "start": 1685.72, "end": 1696.0, "text": " If a tree falls, or if I take a sledgehammer to that stone wall, how does the underlying math process that violent change without breaking the entire reality?", "tokens": [50365, 759, 257, 4230, 8804, 11, 420, 498, 286, 747, 257, 1061, 12203, 39985, 281, 300, 7581, 2929, 11, 577, 775, 264, 14217, 5221, 1399, 300, 11867, 1319, 1553, 7697, 264, 2302, 4103, 30, 50879], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11765679898469344, "compression_ratio": 1.7423076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.41051634348216e-12}, {"id": 510, "seek": 168572, "start": 1696.0, "end": 1704.6200000000001, "text": " To understand how change is processed, we have to look at the primary right equation in the text, which is O-A-T plus one equals M-A-T plus deltas.", "tokens": [50879, 1407, 1223, 577, 1319, 307, 18846, 11, 321, 362, 281, 574, 412, 264, 6194, 558, 5367, 294, 264, 2487, 11, 597, 307, 422, 12, 32, 12, 51, 1804, 472, 6915, 376, 12, 32, 12, 51, 1804, 1103, 83, 296, 13, 51310], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11765679898469344, "compression_ratio": 1.7423076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.41051634348216e-12}, {"id": 511, "seek": 168572, "start": 1704.82, "end": 1712.76, "text": " Which translates to the next state of the world that's O-M-T plus one equals the current state of the world plus a proposed change, the delta psi.", "tokens": [51320, 3013, 28468, 281, 264, 958, 1785, 295, 264, 1002, 300, 311, 422, 12, 44, 12, 51, 1804, 472, 6915, 264, 2190, 1785, 295, 264, 1002, 1804, 257, 10348, 1319, 11, 264, 8289, 20304, 13, 51717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11765679898469344, "compression_ratio": 1.7423076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.41051634348216e-12}, {"id": 512, "seek": 171276, "start": 1712.76, "end": 1717.42, "text": " You've got it. And the most important symbol in that equation is actually the plus sign.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 600, 658, 309, 13, 400, 264, 881, 1021, 5986, 294, 300, 5367, 307, 767, 264, 1804, 1465, 13, 50598], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10899363902577183, "compression_ratio": 1.6444444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485574620168531e-12}, {"id": 513, "seek": 171276, "start": 1717.5, "end": 1718.48, "text": " The plus sign. Why?", "tokens": [50602, 440, 1804, 1465, 13, 1545, 30, 50651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10899363902577183, "compression_ratio": 1.6444444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485574620168531e-12}, {"id": 514, "seek": 171276, "start": 1718.84, "end": 1723.6, "text": " Because writing in the system is never a total overwrite. It is an additive proposal.", "tokens": [50669, 1436, 3579, 294, 264, 1185, 307, 1128, 257, 3217, 670, 21561, 13, 467, 307, 364, 45558, 11494, 13, 50907], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10899363902577183, "compression_ratio": 1.6444444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485574620168531e-12}, {"id": 515, "seek": 171276, "start": 1723.76, "end": 1724.12, "text": " Additive.", "tokens": [50915, 5349, 2187, 13, 50933], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10899363902577183, "compression_ratio": 1.6444444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485574620168531e-12}, {"id": 516, "seek": 171276, "start": 1724.32, "end": 1729.24, "text": " Yes. You take the current established state of reality and you add the proposed change on top of it.", "tokens": [50943, 1079, 13, 509, 747, 264, 2190, 7545, 1785, 295, 4103, 293, 291, 909, 264, 10348, 1319, 322, 1192, 295, 309, 13, 51189], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10899363902577183, "compression_ratio": 1.6444444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485574620168531e-12}, {"id": 517, "seek": 171276, "start": 1729.26, "end": 1730.06, "text": " Okay, that makes sense.", "tokens": [51190, 1033, 11, 300, 1669, 2020, 13, 51230], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10899363902577183, "compression_ratio": 1.6444444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485574620168531e-12}, {"id": 518, "seek": 171276, "start": 1730.2, "end": 1736.26, "text": " A system that freely overwrites its past state eventually drifts into chaos, which is what we see with current AI.", "tokens": [51237, 316, 1185, 300, 16433, 670, 86, 30931, 1080, 1791, 1785, 4728, 1224, 8065, 666, 14158, 11, 597, 307, 437, 321, 536, 365, 2190, 7318, 13, 51540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10899363902577183, "compression_ratio": 1.6444444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485574620168531e-12}, {"id": 519, "seek": 173626, "start": 1736.26, "end": 1743.8, "text": " A system that only adds changes mathematically preserves everything in the environment that isn't specifically being altered by that action.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 1185, 300, 787, 10860, 2962, 44003, 1183, 9054, 1203, 294, 264, 2823, 300, 1943, 380, 4682, 885, 28783, 538, 300, 3069, 13, 50742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22256908238491166, "compression_ratio": 1.7601476014760147, "no_speech_prob": 1.668476229572946e-12}, {"id": 520, "seek": 173626, "start": 1743.9, "end": 1749.78, "text": " But where does this proposal, this delta psi, actually originate from? Who is proposing the change?", "tokens": [50747, 583, 689, 775, 341, 11494, 11, 341, 8289, 20304, 11, 767, 4957, 473, 490, 30, 2102, 307, 29939, 264, 1319, 30, 51041], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22256908238491166, "compression_ratio": 1.7601476014760147, "no_speech_prob": 1.668476229572946e-12}, {"id": 521, "seek": 173626, "start": 1750.36, "end": 1755.72, "text": " Changes originate from two distinct sources. The first source is intrinsic physics.", "tokens": [51070, 761, 10350, 4957, 473, 490, 732, 10644, 7139, 13, 440, 700, 4009, 307, 35698, 10649, 13, 51338], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22256908238491166, "compression_ratio": 1.7601476014760147, "no_speech_prob": 1.668476229572946e-12}, {"id": 522, "seek": 173626, "start": 1756.1, "end": 1757.16, "text": " Intrinsic physics.", "tokens": [51357, 5681, 81, 1292, 299, 10649, 13, 51410], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22256908238491166, "compression_ratio": 1.7601476014760147, "no_speech_prob": 1.668476229572946e-12}, {"id": 523, "seek": 173626, "start": 1757.34, "end": 1760.08, "text": " Denoted mathematically as math pick knowledge.", "tokens": [51419, 6458, 23325, 44003, 382, 5221, 1888, 3601, 13, 51556], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22256908238491166, "compression_ratio": 1.7601476014760147, "no_speech_prob": 1.668476229572946e-12}, {"id": 524, "seek": 173626, "start": 1760.3, "end": 1764.2, "text": " This is what the environment does on its own without anyone touching it.", "tokens": [51567, 639, 307, 437, 264, 2823, 775, 322, 1080, 1065, 1553, 2878, 11175, 309, 13, 51762], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22256908238491166, "compression_ratio": 1.7601476014760147, "no_speech_prob": 1.668476229572946e-12}, {"id": 525, "seek": 173626, "start": 1764.34, "end": 1764.86, "text": " Like gravity.", "tokens": [51769, 1743, 12110, 13, 51795], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22256908238491166, "compression_ratio": 1.7601476014760147, "no_speech_prob": 1.668476229572946e-12}, {"id": 526, "seek": 176486, "start": 1764.86, "end": 1774.86, "text": " Exactly. Entropy naturally relaxing over time as a storm settles, coherence smoothing out as mud dries, gravity pulling water down a slope.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 3951, 27514, 8195, 20103, 670, 565, 382, 257, 7679, 5584, 904, 11, 26528, 655, 899, 6259, 571, 484, 382, 8933, 33997, 11, 12110, 8407, 1281, 760, 257, 13525, 13, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11769391976150811, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 2.03627501145498e-12}, {"id": 527, "seek": 176486, "start": 1775.56, "end": 1778.3799999999999, "text": " Intrinsic physics happens automatically and continuously.", "tokens": [50900, 5681, 81, 1292, 299, 10649, 2314, 6772, 293, 15684, 13, 51041], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11769391976150811, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 2.03627501145498e-12}, {"id": 528, "seek": 176486, "start": 1778.6599999999999, "end": 1779.86, "text": " And the second source of change.", "tokens": [51055, 400, 264, 1150, 4009, 295, 1319, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11769391976150811, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 2.03627501145498e-12}, {"id": 529, "seek": 176486, "start": 1779.8999999999999, "end": 1783.1999999999998, "text": " The second source is neural proposals, denoted as math pathway.", "tokens": [51117, 440, 1150, 4009, 307, 18161, 20198, 11, 1441, 23325, 382, 5221, 18590, 13, 51282], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11769391976150811, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 2.03627501145498e-12}, {"id": 530, "seek": 176486, "start": 1783.5, "end": 1786.62, "text": " These are driven by the intended actions of agents within the world.", "tokens": [51297, 1981, 366, 9555, 538, 264, 10226, 5909, 295, 12554, 1951, 264, 1002, 13, 51453], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11769391976150811, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 2.03627501145498e-12}, {"id": 531, "seek": 176486, "start": 1786.76, "end": 1789.5, "text": " Like a player choosing to swing a sledgehammer at the wall.", "tokens": [51460, 1743, 257, 4256, 10875, 281, 11173, 257, 1061, 12203, 39985, 412, 264, 2929, 13, 51597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11769391976150811, "compression_ratio": 1.6206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 2.03627501145498e-12}, {"id": 532, "seek": 178950, "start": 1789.5, "end": 1792.88, "text": " Right. The agent selects an action based on its capabilities.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 440, 9461, 3048, 82, 364, 3069, 2361, 322, 1080, 10862, 13, 50534], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10670900933536483, "compression_ratio": 1.517094017094017, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920915844361283e-12}, {"id": 533, "seek": 178950, "start": 1793.44, "end": 1801.34, "text": " And a neural model generates a fluent, highly expressive proposal for what that swing would physically do to the semantic field.", "tokens": [50562, 400, 257, 18161, 2316, 23815, 257, 40799, 11, 5405, 40189, 11494, 337, 437, 300, 11173, 576, 9762, 360, 281, 264, 47982, 2519, 13, 50957], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10670900933536483, "compression_ratio": 1.517094017094017, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920915844361283e-12}, {"id": 534, "seek": 178950, "start": 1801.5, "end": 1808.72, "text": " But hold on. If we're letting a neural network generate the proposal, aren't we just inviting hallucinations right back into the system?", "tokens": [50965, 583, 1797, 322, 13, 759, 321, 434, 8295, 257, 18161, 3209, 8460, 264, 11494, 11, 3212, 380, 321, 445, 18202, 35212, 10325, 558, 646, 666, 264, 1185, 30, 51326], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10670900933536483, "compression_ratio": 1.517094017094017, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920915844361283e-12}, {"id": 535, "seek": 178950, "start": 1808.94, "end": 1810.46, "text": " That's a very fair concern.", "tokens": [51337, 663, 311, 257, 588, 3143, 3136, 13, 51413], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10670900933536483, "compression_ratio": 1.517094017094017, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920915844361283e-12}, {"id": 536, "seek": 181046, "start": 1810.46, "end": 1814.74, "text": " Right. What stops the neural network from generating something completely impossible?", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 708, 10094, 264, 18161, 3209, 490, 17746, 746, 2584, 6243, 30, 50579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11673050710599717, "compression_ratio": 1.5342465753424657, "no_speech_prob": 3.080193001700482e-12}, {"id": 537, "seek": 181046, "start": 1815.4, "end": 1826.6000000000001, "text": " Like what if I try to dig a hole with a shovel and the neural network proposes that the patch of ground is simultaneously perfectly undisturbed grass and a freshly dug six foot grave?", "tokens": [50612, 1743, 437, 498, 286, 853, 281, 2528, 257, 5458, 365, 257, 29789, 293, 264, 18161, 3209, 2365, 4201, 300, 264, 9972, 295, 2727, 307, 16561, 6239, 674, 468, 374, 2883, 8054, 293, 257, 34412, 22954, 2309, 2671, 12525, 30, 51172], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11673050710599717, "compression_ratio": 1.5342465753424657, "no_speech_prob": 3.080193001700482e-12}, {"id": 538, "seek": 181046, "start": 1827.1200000000001, "end": 1830.78, "text": " How does the universe not just accept that garbage data and break?", "tokens": [51198, 1012, 775, 264, 6445, 406, 445, 3241, 300, 14150, 1412, 293, 1821, 30, 51381], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11673050710599717, "compression_ratio": 1.5342465753424657, "no_speech_prob": 3.080193001700482e-12}, {"id": 539, "seek": 183078, "start": 1830.78, "end": 1833.56, "text": " That is the exact vulnerability you would expect.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 264, 1900, 24210, 291, 576, 2066, 13, 50504], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1396302025893639, "compression_ratio": 1.7170418006430868, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431013671712845e-12}, {"id": 540, "seek": 183078, "start": 1833.72, "end": 1836.68, "text": " And it is where the brilliance of this architecture truly shines.", "tokens": [50512, 400, 309, 307, 689, 264, 8695, 6276, 295, 341, 9482, 4908, 28056, 13, 50660], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1396302025893639, "compression_ratio": 1.7170418006430868, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431013671712845e-12}, {"id": 541, "seek": 183078, "start": 1836.8999999999999, "end": 1840.94, "text": " The system does not just blindly accept the neural proposal and add it to the world.", "tokens": [50671, 440, 1185, 775, 406, 445, 47744, 3241, 264, 18161, 11494, 293, 909, 309, 281, 264, 1002, 13, 50873], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1396302025893639, "compression_ratio": 1.7170418006430868, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431013671712845e-12}, {"id": 542, "seek": 183078, "start": 1841.04, "end": 1841.6, "text": " What does it do?", "tokens": [50878, 708, 775, 309, 360, 30, 50906], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1396302025893639, "compression_ratio": 1.7170418006430868, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431013671712845e-12}, {"id": 543, "seek": 183078, "start": 1841.7, "end": 1846.58, "text": " It forces the proposal through a rigorous mathematical filter called constraint projection.", "tokens": [50911, 467, 5874, 264, 11494, 807, 257, 29882, 18894, 6608, 1219, 25534, 22743, 13, 51155], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1396302025893639, "compression_ratio": 1.7170418006430868, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431013671712845e-12}, {"id": 544, "seek": 183078, "start": 1846.84, "end": 1847.72, "text": " Constraint projection?", "tokens": [51168, 8574, 424, 686, 22743, 30, 51212], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1396302025893639, "compression_ratio": 1.7170418006430868, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431013671712845e-12}, {"id": 545, "seek": 183078, "start": 1848.02, "end": 1850.6399999999999, "text": " How does the projection actually filter the proposal?", "tokens": [51227, 1012, 775, 264, 22743, 767, 6608, 264, 11494, 30, 51358], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1396302025893639, "compression_ratio": 1.7170418006430868, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431013671712845e-12}, {"id": 546, "seek": 183078, "start": 1851.04, "end": 1859.04, "text": " I want you to visualize a semantic pressure solve, similar to how a traditional physics engine stops a character from walking through a solid wall.", "tokens": [51378, 286, 528, 291, 281, 23273, 257, 47982, 3321, 5039, 11, 2531, 281, 577, 257, 5164, 10649, 2848, 10094, 257, 2517, 490, 4494, 807, 257, 5100, 2929, 13, 51778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1396302025893639, "compression_ratio": 1.7170418006430868, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431013671712845e-12}, {"id": 547, "seek": 185904, "start": 1859.04, "end": 1860.82, "text": " Okay, like collision detection.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 411, 24644, 17784, 13, 50454], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21903088449061603, "compression_ratio": 1.6244541484716157, "no_speech_prob": 1.927631231718463e-12}, {"id": 548, "seek": 185904, "start": 1861.1599999999999, "end": 1861.92, "text": " Similar, yes.", "tokens": [50471, 10905, 11, 2086, 13, 50509], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21903088449061603, "compression_ratio": 1.6244541484716157, "no_speech_prob": 1.927631231718463e-12}, {"id": 549, "seek": 185904, "start": 1862.48, "end": 1867.3, "text": " The established semantic field has an invisible, multidimensional manifold of constraints.", "tokens": [50537, 440, 7545, 47982, 2519, 575, 364, 14603, 11, 2120, 327, 332, 11075, 47138, 295, 18491, 13, 50778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21903088449061603, "compression_ratio": 1.6244541484716157, "no_speech_prob": 1.927631231718463e-12}, {"id": 550, "seek": 185904, "start": 1867.7, "end": 1873.5, "text": " It has the rules of entropy, the laws of physics, and the accumulated residue of past events.", "tokens": [50798, 467, 575, 264, 4474, 295, 30867, 11, 264, 6064, 295, 10649, 11, 293, 264, 31346, 34799, 295, 1791, 3931, 13, 51088], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21903088449061603, "compression_ratio": 1.6244541484716157, "no_speech_prob": 1.927631231718463e-12}, {"id": 551, "seek": 185904, "start": 1874.02, "end": 1881.42, "text": " When the neural model proposes a change, the system projects that proposal onto the nearest admissible state on that constraint manifold.", "tokens": [51114, 1133, 264, 18161, 2316, 2365, 4201, 257, 1319, 11, 264, 1185, 4455, 300, 11494, 3911, 264, 23831, 5910, 41073, 1785, 322, 300, 25534, 47138, 13, 51484], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21903088449061603, "compression_ratio": 1.6244541484716157, "no_speech_prob": 1.927631231718463e-12}, {"id": 552, "seek": 185904, "start": 1881.76, "end": 1882.08, "text": " Oh.", "tokens": [51501, 876, 13, 51517], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21903088449061603, "compression_ratio": 1.6244541484716157, "no_speech_prob": 1.927631231718463e-12}, {"id": 553, "seek": 188208, "start": 1882.08, "end": 1890.3, "text": " If the proposal violates the rules of reality, the system doesn't necessarily throw the entire action away, it bends the proposal.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 264, 11494, 3448, 1024, 264, 4474, 295, 4103, 11, 264, 1185, 1177, 380, 4725, 3507, 264, 2302, 3069, 1314, 11, 309, 42990, 264, 11494, 13, 50776], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11793725103394598, "compression_ratio": 1.6548042704626333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362174202338986e-12}, {"id": 554, "seek": 188208, "start": 1890.48, "end": 1890.96, "text": " It bends it.", "tokens": [50785, 467, 42990, 309, 13, 50809], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11793725103394598, "compression_ratio": 1.6548042704626333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362174202338986e-12}, {"id": 555, "seek": 188208, "start": 1891.12, "end": 1897.4199999999998, "text": " It mathematically corrects the impossible details while trying to honor the core intent of the agent's action as much as possible.", "tokens": [50817, 467, 44003, 3006, 82, 264, 6243, 4365, 1339, 1382, 281, 5968, 264, 4965, 8446, 295, 264, 9461, 311, 3069, 382, 709, 382, 1944, 13, 51132], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11793725103394598, "compression_ratio": 1.6548042704626333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362174202338986e-12}, {"id": 556, "seek": 188208, "start": 1897.4399999999998, "end": 1897.9199999999998, "text": " Oh, I see.", "tokens": [51133, 876, 11, 286, 536, 13, 51157], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11793725103394598, "compression_ratio": 1.6548042704626333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362174202338986e-12}, {"id": 557, "seek": 188208, "start": 1898.02, "end": 1900.08, "text": " So, let's say I want to dig a deep grave.", "tokens": [51162, 407, 11, 718, 311, 584, 286, 528, 281, 2528, 257, 2452, 12525, 13, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11793725103394598, "compression_ratio": 1.6548042704626333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362174202338986e-12}, {"id": 558, "seek": 188208, "start": 1900.62, "end": 1906.6599999999999, "text": " But the world's residue component knows that there's a massive layer of solid bedrock just two inches below the topsoil.", "tokens": [51292, 583, 264, 1002, 311, 34799, 6542, 3255, 300, 456, 311, 257, 5994, 4583, 295, 5100, 2901, 17799, 445, 732, 8478, 2507, 264, 1192, 539, 388, 13, 51594], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11793725103394598, "compression_ratio": 1.6548042704626333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362174202338986e-12}, {"id": 559, "seek": 188208, "start": 1906.74, "end": 1907.34, "text": " Perfect example.", "tokens": [51598, 10246, 1365, 13, 51628], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11793725103394598, "compression_ratio": 1.6548042704626333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362174202338986e-12}, {"id": 560, "seek": 190734, "start": 1907.34, "end": 1909.9399999999998, "text": " The neural network proposes a six-foot hole.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 18161, 3209, 2365, 4201, 257, 2309, 12, 13498, 5458, 13, 50495], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13837287961974626, "compression_ratio": 1.705685618729097, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169079963823663e-12}, {"id": 561, "seek": 190734, "start": 1910.72, "end": 1919.8, "text": " The projection system looks at the bedrock constraint and says, uh, you cannot have a six-foot hole here that violates the established coherence of the bedrock.", "tokens": [50534, 440, 22743, 1185, 1542, 412, 264, 2901, 17799, 25534, 293, 1619, 11, 2232, 11, 291, 2644, 362, 257, 2309, 12, 13498, 5458, 510, 300, 3448, 1024, 264, 7545, 26528, 655, 295, 264, 2901, 17799, 13, 50988], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13837287961974626, "compression_ratio": 1.705685618729097, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169079963823663e-12}, {"id": 562, "seek": 190734, "start": 1920.1, "end": 1920.36, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51003, 865, 13, 51016], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13837287961974626, "compression_ratio": 1.705685618729097, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169079963823663e-12}, {"id": 563, "seek": 190734, "start": 1920.8799999999999, "end": 1925.04, "text": " But I will project your digging action onto the nearest allowable reality.", "tokens": [51042, 583, 286, 486, 1716, 428, 17343, 3069, 3911, 264, 23831, 2089, 712, 4103, 13, 51250], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13837287961974626, "compression_ratio": 1.705685618729097, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169079963823663e-12}, {"id": 564, "seek": 190734, "start": 1925.5, "end": 1930.86, "text": " I will give you a shallow two-inch scrape in the dirt and some sparks flying off your shovel as it hits the rock.", "tokens": [51273, 286, 486, 976, 291, 257, 20488, 732, 12, 12415, 32827, 294, 264, 11483, 293, 512, 44102, 7137, 766, 428, 29789, 382, 309, 8664, 264, 3727, 13, 51541], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13837287961974626, "compression_ratio": 1.705685618729097, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169079963823663e-12}, {"id": 565, "seek": 190734, "start": 1930.9399999999998, "end": 1931.3799999999999, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51545, 7587, 13, 51567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13837287961974626, "compression_ratio": 1.705685618729097, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169079963823663e-12}, {"id": 566, "seek": 190734, "start": 1931.54, "end": 1934.1799999999998, "text": " It physically corrects your action against the truth of the world.", "tokens": [51575, 467, 9762, 3006, 82, 428, 3069, 1970, 264, 3494, 295, 264, 1002, 13, 51707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13837287961974626, "compression_ratio": 1.705685618729097, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169079963823663e-12}, {"id": 567, "seek": 190734, "start": 1934.3799999999999, "end": 1935.74, "text": " It's a perfect division of labor.", "tokens": [51717, 467, 311, 257, 2176, 10044, 295, 5938, 13, 51785], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13837287961974626, "compression_ratio": 1.705685618729097, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169079963823663e-12}, {"id": 568, "seek": 193574, "start": 1935.74, "end": 1941.14, "text": " The neural model provides the creativity, the fluency, and the expressiveness of the action.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 18161, 2316, 6417, 264, 12915, 11, 264, 5029, 3020, 11, 293, 264, 5109, 8477, 295, 264, 3069, 13, 50635], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1543549579122792, "compression_ratio": 1.802919708029197, "no_speech_prob": 1.6743970576368894e-12}, {"id": 569, "seek": 193574, "start": 1941.76, "end": 1945.7, "text": " But the constraint projection provides the absolute authority of reality.", "tokens": [50666, 583, 264, 25534, 22743, 6417, 264, 8236, 8281, 295, 4103, 13, 50863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1543549579122792, "compression_ratio": 1.802919708029197, "no_speech_prob": 1.6743970576368894e-12}, {"id": 570, "seek": 193574, "start": 1945.94, "end": 1946.42, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50875, 7587, 13, 50899], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1543549579122792, "compression_ratio": 1.802919708029197, "no_speech_prob": 1.6743970576368894e-12}, {"id": 571, "seek": 193574, "start": 1946.74, "end": 1950.32, "text": " But projecting the proposal isn't the final step of the right cycle, is it?", "tokens": [50915, 583, 43001, 264, 11494, 1943, 380, 264, 2572, 1823, 295, 264, 558, 6586, 11, 307, 309, 30, 51094], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1543549579122792, "compression_ratio": 1.802919708029197, "no_speech_prob": 1.6743970576368894e-12}, {"id": 572, "seek": 193574, "start": 1950.78, "end": 1953.36, "text": " After it gets bent into shape, there is a commit phase.", "tokens": [51117, 2381, 309, 2170, 14075, 666, 3909, 11, 456, 307, 257, 5599, 5574, 13, 51246], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1543549579122792, "compression_ratio": 1.802919708029197, "no_speech_prob": 1.6743970576368894e-12}, {"id": 573, "seek": 193574, "start": 1953.94, "end": 1956.0, "text": " What is the system doing during the commit phase?", "tokens": [51275, 708, 307, 264, 1185, 884, 1830, 264, 5599, 5574, 30, 51378], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1543549579122792, "compression_ratio": 1.802919708029197, "no_speech_prob": 1.6743970576368894e-12}, {"id": 574, "seek": 193574, "start": 1956.2, "end": 1958.78, "text": " Committing is the arbitration phase of the universe.", "tokens": [51388, 3046, 2414, 307, 264, 14931, 2405, 5574, 295, 264, 6445, 13, 51517], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1543549579122792, "compression_ratio": 1.802919708029197, "no_speech_prob": 1.6743970576368894e-12}, {"id": 575, "seek": 193574, "start": 1959.42, "end": 1963.92, "text": " Projection evaluates a single proposal in isolation against the static environment.", "tokens": [51549, 9849, 313, 6133, 1024, 257, 2167, 11494, 294, 16001, 1970, 264, 13437, 2823, 13, 51774], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1543549579122792, "compression_ratio": 1.802919708029197, "no_speech_prob": 1.6743970576368894e-12}, {"id": 576, "seek": 196392, "start": 1963.92, "end": 1967.14, "text": " But what happens if two agents are interacting dynamically?", "tokens": [50365, 583, 437, 2314, 498, 732, 12554, 366, 18017, 43492, 30, 50526], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18156842151320124, "compression_ratio": 1.5246636771300448, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457263732183367e-12}, {"id": 577, "seek": 196392, "start": 1967.28, "end": 1967.68, "text": " Oh, right.", "tokens": [50533, 876, 11, 558, 13, 50553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18156842151320124, "compression_ratio": 1.5246636771300448, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457263732183367e-12}, {"id": 578, "seek": 196392, "start": 1967.8000000000002, "end": 1968.52, "text": " Like multiplayer.", "tokens": [50559, 1743, 27325, 13, 50595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18156842151320124, "compression_ratio": 1.5246636771300448, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457263732183367e-12}, {"id": 579, "seek": 196392, "start": 1968.98, "end": 1969.2, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50618, 1779, 13, 50629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18156842151320124, "compression_ratio": 1.5246636771300448, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457263732183367e-12}, {"id": 580, "seek": 196392, "start": 1969.7, "end": 1978.54, "text": " What if you and I are both in the courtyard and we both grab the exact same heavy stone bench and try to pull it in completely opposite directions the exact same millisecond?", "tokens": [50654, 708, 498, 291, 293, 286, 366, 1293, 294, 264, 41364, 293, 321, 1293, 4444, 264, 1900, 912, 4676, 7581, 10638, 293, 853, 281, 2235, 309, 294, 2584, 6182, 11095, 264, 1900, 912, 27940, 18882, 30, 51096], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18156842151320124, "compression_ratio": 1.5246636771300448, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457263732183367e-12}, {"id": 581, "seek": 196392, "start": 1978.6200000000001, "end": 1978.8200000000002, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51100, 1779, 13, 51110], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18156842151320124, "compression_ratio": 1.5246636771300448, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457263732183367e-12}, {"id": 582, "seek": 196392, "start": 1979.14, "end": 1982.38, "text": " My individual proposal to move it left is physically possible.", "tokens": [51126, 1222, 2609, 11494, 281, 1286, 309, 1411, 307, 9762, 1944, 13, 51288], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18156842151320124, "compression_ratio": 1.5246636771300448, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457263732183367e-12}, {"id": 583, "seek": 198238, "start": 1982.38, "end": 1985.64, "text": " And your proposal to move it right is physically possible.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 428, 11494, 281, 1286, 309, 558, 307, 9762, 1944, 13, 50528], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16069489337028342, "compression_ratio": 1.62, "no_speech_prob": 1.3830297584255247e-12}, {"id": 584, "seek": 198238, "start": 1985.92, "end": 1988.88, "text": " But they fundamentally contradict each other.", "tokens": [50542, 583, 436, 17879, 28900, 1184, 661, 13, 50690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16069489337028342, "compression_ratio": 1.62, "no_speech_prob": 1.3830297584255247e-12}, {"id": 585, "seek": 198238, "start": 1988.96, "end": 1989.92, "text": " They can't both happen.", "tokens": [50694, 814, 393, 380, 1293, 1051, 13, 50742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16069489337028342, "compression_ratio": 1.62, "no_speech_prob": 1.3830297584255247e-12}, {"id": 586, "seek": 198238, "start": 1990.3400000000001, "end": 1994.46, "text": " The commit stage arbitrates these collisions using a causal graph.", "tokens": [50763, 440, 5599, 3233, 14931, 12507, 613, 46537, 1228, 257, 38755, 4295, 13, 50969], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16069489337028342, "compression_ratio": 1.62, "no_speech_prob": 1.3830297584255247e-12}, {"id": 587, "seek": 198238, "start": 1994.72, "end": 1995.44, "text": " How does that work?", "tokens": [50982, 1012, 775, 300, 589, 30, 51018], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16069489337028342, "compression_ratio": 1.62, "no_speech_prob": 1.3830297584255247e-12}, {"id": 588, "seek": 198238, "start": 1995.5600000000002, "end": 2006.8600000000001, "text": " If our proposals don't conflict, say, you move the bench and I open a door on the other side of the courtyard, the graph sees no overlap and both proposals commit to reality simultaneously.", "tokens": [51024, 759, 527, 20198, 500, 380, 6596, 11, 584, 11, 291, 1286, 264, 10638, 293, 286, 1269, 257, 2853, 322, 264, 661, 1252, 295, 264, 41364, 11, 264, 4295, 8194, 572, 19959, 293, 1293, 20198, 5599, 281, 4103, 16561, 13, 51589], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16069489337028342, "compression_ratio": 1.62, "no_speech_prob": 1.3830297584255247e-12}, {"id": 589, "seek": 200686, "start": 2006.86, "end": 2017.84, "text": " But if our proposals collide on the same coordinate, the commit stage resolves the physics, perhaps determining that the bench doesn't move at all or it rotates based on our combined force.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 498, 527, 20198, 49093, 322, 264, 912, 15670, 11, 264, 5599, 3233, 7923, 977, 264, 10649, 11, 4317, 23751, 300, 264, 10638, 1177, 380, 1286, 412, 439, 420, 309, 42133, 2361, 322, 527, 9354, 3464, 13, 50914], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15187652812284583, "compression_ratio": 1.5757575757575757, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108446599857109e-12}, {"id": 590, "seek": 200686, "start": 2018.1, "end": 2018.26, "text": " Got it.", "tokens": [50927, 5803, 309, 13, 50935], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15187652812284583, "compression_ratio": 1.5757575757575757, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108446599857109e-12}, {"id": 591, "seek": 200686, "start": 2018.52, "end": 2022.6599999999999, "text": " And crucially, this is also the stage where the system executes what it calls refusal.", "tokens": [50948, 400, 5140, 1909, 11, 341, 307, 611, 264, 3233, 689, 264, 1185, 4454, 1819, 437, 309, 5498, 48948, 13, 51155], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15187652812284583, "compression_ratio": 1.5757575757575757, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108446599857109e-12}, {"id": 592, "seek": 200686, "start": 2023.08, "end": 2023.6, "text": " Refusal.", "tokens": [51176, 16957, 11765, 13, 51202], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15187652812284583, "compression_ratio": 1.5757575757575757, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108446599857109e-12}, {"id": 593, "seek": 200686, "start": 2023.9599999999998, "end": 2027.9599999999998, "text": " Under what circumstances does the universe refuse a proposal entirely?", "tokens": [51220, 6974, 437, 9121, 775, 264, 6445, 16791, 257, 11494, 7696, 30, 51420], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15187652812284583, "compression_ratio": 1.5757575757575757, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108446599857109e-12}, {"id": 594, "seek": 202796, "start": 2027.96, "end": 2043.66, "text": " If a neural proposal is so wild, so profoundly divorced from the constraints of reality, that trying to bend it onto an admissible state would completely obliterate the original intent of the action, the system simply refuses it.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 257, 18161, 11494, 307, 370, 4868, 11, 370, 39954, 27670, 490, 264, 18491, 295, 4103, 11, 300, 1382, 281, 11229, 309, 3911, 364, 5910, 41073, 1785, 576, 2584, 23740, 1681, 473, 264, 3380, 8446, 295, 264, 3069, 11, 264, 1185, 2935, 33222, 309, 13, 51150], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12247748176256816, "compression_ratio": 1.5807860262008733, "no_speech_prob": 1.9276188718136966e-12}, {"id": 595, "seek": 202796, "start": 2043.78, "end": 2044.64, "text": " It just blocks it.", "tokens": [51156, 467, 445, 8474, 309, 13, 51199], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12247748176256816, "compression_ratio": 1.5807860262008733, "no_speech_prob": 1.9276188718136966e-12}, {"id": 596, "seek": 202796, "start": 2044.68, "end": 2045.58, "text": " It rejects the code.", "tokens": [51201, 467, 8248, 82, 264, 3089, 13, 51246], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12247748176256816, "compression_ratio": 1.5807860262008733, "no_speech_prob": 1.9276188718136966e-12}, {"id": 597, "seek": 202796, "start": 2045.66, "end": 2046.88, "text": " The event does not happen.", "tokens": [51250, 440, 2280, 775, 406, 1051, 13, 51311], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12247748176256816, "compression_ratio": 1.5807860262008733, "no_speech_prob": 1.9276188718136966e-12}, {"id": 598, "seek": 202796, "start": 2047.4, "end": 2048.94, "text": " No trace is left in the residue.", "tokens": [51337, 883, 13508, 307, 1411, 294, 264, 34799, 13, 51414], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12247748176256816, "compression_ratio": 1.5807860262008733, "no_speech_prob": 1.9276188718136966e-12}, {"id": 599, "seek": 202796, "start": 2049.12, "end": 2049.58, "text": " It is an error.", "tokens": [51423, 467, 307, 364, 6713, 13, 51446], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12247748176256816, "compression_ratio": 1.5807860262008733, "no_speech_prob": 1.9276188718136966e-12}, {"id": 600, "seek": 202796, "start": 2049.6, "end": 2050.7, "text": " It never stalks.", "tokens": [51447, 467, 1128, 21789, 82, 13, 51502], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12247748176256816, "compression_ratio": 1.5807860262008733, "no_speech_prob": 1.9276188718136966e-12}, {"id": 601, "seek": 205070, "start": 2050.7, "end": 2063.22, "text": " For that water to look realistic, a neural proposal for the water's chaotic movement is being generated, projected against constraints, and committed to reality every single fraction of a second.", "tokens": [50365, 1171, 300, 1281, 281, 574, 12465, 11, 257, 18161, 11494, 337, 264, 1281, 311, 27013, 3963, 307, 885, 10833, 11, 26231, 1970, 18491, 11, 293, 7784, 281, 4103, 633, 2167, 14135, 295, 257, 1150, 13, 50991], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07648510980133963, "compression_ratio": 1.7259786476868328, "no_speech_prob": 1.973625689960512e-12}, {"id": 602, "seek": 205070, "start": 2063.3399999999997, "end": 2066.24, "text": " So the water is basically replacing itself constantly.", "tokens": [50997, 407, 264, 1281, 307, 1936, 19139, 2564, 6460, 13, 51142], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07648510980133963, "compression_ratio": 1.7259786476868328, "no_speech_prob": 1.973625689960512e-12}, {"id": 603, "seek": 205070, "start": 2066.52, "end": 2072.6, "text": " The water you are looking at right now is composed of entirely different semantic states than the water you were looking at a minute ago.", "tokens": [51156, 440, 1281, 291, 366, 1237, 412, 558, 586, 307, 18204, 295, 7696, 819, 47982, 4368, 813, 264, 1281, 291, 645, 1237, 412, 257, 3456, 2057, 13, 51460], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07648510980133963, "compression_ratio": 1.7259786476868328, "no_speech_prob": 1.973625689960512e-12}, {"id": 604, "seek": 205070, "start": 2072.8799999999997, "end": 2076.2, "text": " It is in a state of constant, violent change.", "tokens": [51474, 467, 307, 294, 257, 1785, 295, 5754, 11, 11867, 1319, 13, 51640], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07648510980133963, "compression_ratio": 1.7259786476868328, "no_speech_prob": 1.973625689960512e-12}, {"id": 605, "seek": 205070, "start": 2076.3399999999997, "end": 2079.3999999999996, "text": " Yet the fountain itself remains completely stable.", "tokens": [51647, 10890, 264, 29451, 2564, 7023, 2584, 8351, 13, 51800], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07648510980133963, "compression_ratio": 1.7259786476868328, "no_speech_prob": 1.973625689960512e-12}, {"id": 606, "seek": 207940, "start": 2079.4, "end": 2081.6800000000003, "text": " It doesn't dissolve into a puddle.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1177, 380, 30150, 666, 257, 14166, 2285, 13, 50479], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19108529388904572, "compression_ratio": 1.7978339350180506, "no_speech_prob": 2.218650610452677e-12}, {"id": 607, "seek": 207940, "start": 2082.2200000000003, "end": 2083.14, "text": " How is that possible?", "tokens": [50506, 1012, 307, 300, 1944, 30, 50552], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19108529388904572, "compression_ratio": 1.7978339350180506, "no_speech_prob": 2.218650610452677e-12}, {"id": 608, "seek": 207940, "start": 2083.42, "end": 2087.4, "text": " The text explains that the system operates on multiple overlapping timescales.", "tokens": [50566, 440, 2487, 13948, 300, 264, 1185, 22577, 322, 3866, 33535, 1413, 66, 4229, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19108529388904572, "compression_ratio": 1.7978339350180506, "no_speech_prob": 2.218650610452677e-12}, {"id": 609, "seek": 207940, "start": 2087.96, "end": 2090.34, "text": " It uses fast clocks and slow clocks.", "tokens": [50793, 467, 4960, 2370, 41528, 293, 2964, 41528, 13, 50912], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19108529388904572, "compression_ratio": 1.7978339350180506, "no_speech_prob": 2.218650610452677e-12}, {"id": 610, "seek": 207940, "start": 2090.56, "end": 2091.92, "text": " Fast clocks and slow clocks, yes.", "tokens": [50923, 15968, 41528, 293, 2964, 41528, 11, 2086, 13, 50991], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19108529388904572, "compression_ratio": 1.7978339350180506, "no_speech_prob": 2.218650610452677e-12}, {"id": 611, "seek": 207940, "start": 2092.2000000000003, "end": 2096.64, "text": " The appearance component Z and the float component V update on a fast clock.", "tokens": [51005, 440, 8967, 6542, 1176, 293, 264, 15706, 6542, 691, 5623, 322, 257, 2370, 7830, 13, 51227], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19108529388904572, "compression_ratio": 1.7978339350180506, "no_speech_prob": 2.218650610452677e-12}, {"id": 612, "seek": 207940, "start": 2096.86, "end": 2099.56, "text": " That handles the chaotic splashing of the water.", "tokens": [51238, 663, 18722, 264, 27013, 45981, 295, 264, 1281, 13, 51373], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19108529388904572, "compression_ratio": 1.7978339350180506, "no_speech_prob": 2.218650610452677e-12}, {"id": 613, "seek": 207940, "start": 2099.6600000000003, "end": 2100.94, "text": " Okay, the fast-moving stuff.", "tokens": [51378, 1033, 11, 264, 2370, 12, 3280, 798, 1507, 13, 51442], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19108529388904572, "compression_ratio": 1.7978339350180506, "no_speech_prob": 2.218650610452677e-12}, {"id": 614, "seek": 207940, "start": 2101.04, "end": 2106.26, "text": " But the coherence component, phi, and the topological structure of the field update on a slow clock.", "tokens": [51447, 583, 264, 26528, 655, 6542, 11, 13107, 11, 293, 264, 1192, 4383, 3877, 295, 264, 2519, 5623, 322, 257, 2964, 7830, 13, 51708], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19108529388904572, "compression_ratio": 1.7978339350180506, "no_speech_prob": 2.218650610452677e-12}, {"id": 615, "seek": 207940, "start": 2106.34, "end": 2108.32, "text": " That handles the heavy stone basin.", "tokens": [51712, 663, 18722, 264, 4676, 7581, 34863, 13, 51811], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19108529388904572, "compression_ratio": 1.7978339350180506, "no_speech_prob": 2.218650610452677e-12}, {"id": 616, "seek": 210832, "start": 2108.32, "end": 2111.52, "text": " Ah, so they're being updated on entirely different schedules.", "tokens": [50365, 2438, 11, 370, 436, 434, 885, 10588, 322, 7696, 819, 28078, 13, 50525], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14554970935710426, "compression_ratio": 1.6594202898550725, "no_speech_prob": 1.579700888328095e-12}, {"id": 617, "seek": 210832, "start": 2112.0800000000004, "end": 2114.7200000000003, "text": " The stone isn't being asked to change as often as the water.", "tokens": [50553, 440, 7581, 1943, 380, 885, 2351, 281, 1319, 382, 2049, 382, 264, 1281, 13, 50685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14554970935710426, "compression_ratio": 1.6594202898550725, "no_speech_prob": 1.579700888328095e-12}, {"id": 618, "seek": 210832, "start": 2115.1000000000004, "end": 2115.6600000000003, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50704, 7587, 13, 50732], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14554970935710426, "compression_ratio": 1.6594202898550725, "no_speech_prob": 1.579700888328095e-12}, {"id": 619, "seek": 210832, "start": 2116.06, "end": 2120.26, "text": " And because of that division, the fountain becomes a dynamic fixed point.", "tokens": [50752, 400, 570, 295, 300, 10044, 11, 264, 29451, 3643, 257, 8546, 6806, 935, 13, 50962], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14554970935710426, "compression_ratio": 1.6594202898550725, "no_speech_prob": 1.579700888328095e-12}, {"id": 620, "seek": 210832, "start": 2120.8, "end": 2124.92, "text": " Despite the continuous, chaotic proposals happening to the water on the fast clock,", "tokens": [50989, 11334, 264, 10957, 11, 27013, 20198, 2737, 281, 264, 1281, 322, 264, 2370, 7830, 11, 51195], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14554970935710426, "compression_ratio": 1.6594202898550725, "no_speech_prob": 1.579700888328095e-12}, {"id": 621, "seek": 210832, "start": 2125.26, "end": 2130.5, "text": " every time those proposals are projected against the rigid constraints of the stone basin on the slow clock,", "tokens": [51212, 633, 565, 729, 20198, 366, 26231, 1970, 264, 22195, 18491, 295, 264, 7581, 34863, 322, 264, 2964, 7830, 11, 51474], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14554970935710426, "compression_ratio": 1.6594202898550725, "no_speech_prob": 1.579700888328095e-12}, {"id": 622, "seek": 210832, "start": 2130.84, "end": 2134.44, "text": " they reliably commit to the exact same overall macro shape.", "tokens": [51491, 436, 49927, 5599, 281, 264, 1900, 912, 4787, 18887, 3909, 13, 51671], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14554970935710426, "compression_ratio": 1.6594202898550725, "no_speech_prob": 1.579700888328095e-12}, {"id": 623, "seek": 213444, "start": 2134.44, "end": 2134.84, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50365, 3153, 13, 50385], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.5495210488637289, "compression_ratio": 0.3333333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671662101715556e-12}, {"id": 624, "seek": 213484, "start": 2134.84, "end": 2144.38, "text": " The cycle loops endlessly, millions of times, but the math keeps returning the system to the same stable, recognizable configuration.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 6586, 16121, 44920, 11, 6803, 295, 1413, 11, 457, 264, 5221, 5965, 12678, 264, 1185, 281, 264, 912, 8351, 11, 40757, 11694, 13, 50842], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1778769568791465, "compression_ratio": 1.4673366834170853, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011325074284267e-12}, {"id": 625, "seek": 213484, "start": 2144.84, "end": 2148.1200000000003, "text": " That completely flipped my understanding of what an object is.", "tokens": [50865, 663, 2584, 26273, 452, 3701, 295, 437, 364, 2657, 307, 13, 51029], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1778769568791465, "compression_ratio": 1.4673366834170853, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011325074284267e-12}, {"id": 626, "seek": 213484, "start": 2148.38, "end": 2153.48, "text": " In this architecture, identity isn't like a sticky label on a file that says fountain asset 01.", "tokens": [51042, 682, 341, 9482, 11, 6575, 1943, 380, 411, 257, 14470, 7645, 322, 257, 3991, 300, 1619, 29451, 11999, 23185, 13, 51297], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1778769568791465, "compression_ratio": 1.4673366834170853, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011325074284267e-12}, {"id": 627, "seek": 215348, "start": 2153.48, "end": 2154.68, "text": " No, not at all.", "tokens": [50365, 883, 11, 406, 412, 439, 13, 50425], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12478400128228324, "compression_ratio": 1.7226277372262773, "no_speech_prob": 1.94274110687509e-12}, {"id": 628, "seek": 215348, "start": 2154.92, "end": 2155.86, "text": " Identity is a verb.", "tokens": [50437, 25905, 507, 307, 257, 9595, 13, 50484], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12478400128228324, "compression_ratio": 1.7226277372262773, "no_speech_prob": 1.94274110687509e-12}, {"id": 629, "seek": 215348, "start": 2156.52, "end": 2162.94, "text": " It is the object's ongoing ability to survive this brutal mathematical update cycle over and over again without devolving into noise.", "tokens": [50517, 467, 307, 264, 2657, 311, 10452, 3485, 281, 7867, 341, 17878, 18894, 5623, 6586, 670, 293, 670, 797, 1553, 1905, 401, 798, 666, 5658, 13, 50838], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12478400128228324, "compression_ratio": 1.7226277372262773, "no_speech_prob": 1.94274110687509e-12}, {"id": 630, "seek": 215348, "start": 2163.4, "end": 2165.7400000000002, "text": " Identity is a continuous achievement of the physics engine.", "tokens": [50861, 25905, 507, 307, 257, 10957, 15838, 295, 264, 10649, 2848, 13, 50978], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12478400128228324, "compression_ratio": 1.7226277372262773, "no_speech_prob": 1.94274110687509e-12}, {"id": 631, "seek": 215348, "start": 2165.92, "end": 2168.12, "text": " Identity is a trajectory that survives time.", "tokens": [50987, 25905, 507, 307, 257, 21512, 300, 46231, 565, 13, 51097], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12478400128228324, "compression_ratio": 1.7226277372262773, "no_speech_prob": 1.94274110687509e-12}, {"id": 632, "seek": 215348, "start": 2168.34, "end": 2172.8, "text": " We have established the rules, the semantic field, and the right cycle that governs change.", "tokens": [51108, 492, 362, 7545, 264, 4474, 11, 264, 47982, 2519, 11, 293, 264, 558, 6586, 300, 1980, 82, 1319, 13, 51331], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12478400128228324, "compression_ratio": 1.7226277372262773, "no_speech_prob": 1.94274110687509e-12}, {"id": 633, "seek": 215348, "start": 2172.98, "end": 2177.06, "text": " But what is the invisible machinery holding this entire universe together underneath it all?", "tokens": [51340, 583, 437, 307, 264, 14603, 27302, 5061, 341, 2302, 6445, 1214, 7223, 309, 439, 30, 51544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12478400128228324, "compression_ratio": 1.7226277372262773, "no_speech_prob": 1.94274110687509e-12}, {"id": 634, "seek": 215348, "start": 2177.08, "end": 2177.62, "text": " The physics.", "tokens": [51545, 440, 10649, 13, 51572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12478400128228324, "compression_ratio": 1.7226277372262773, "no_speech_prob": 1.94274110687509e-12}, {"id": 635, "seek": 217762, "start": 2177.62, "end": 2181.58, "text": " Right. What guarantees that the constraint projection actually works?", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 708, 32567, 300, 264, 25534, 22743, 767, 1985, 30, 50563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11422795747455798, "compression_ratio": 1.6592592592592592, "no_speech_prob": 3.0443538315272356e-12}, {"id": 636, "seek": 217762, "start": 2182.18, "end": 2186.0, "text": " Let's get into the deep physics and math of these AI worlds.", "tokens": [50593, 961, 311, 483, 666, 264, 2452, 10649, 293, 5221, 295, 613, 7318, 13401, 13, 50784], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11422795747455798, "compression_ratio": 1.6592592592592592, "no_speech_prob": 3.0443538315272356e-12}, {"id": 637, "seek": 217762, "start": 2186.2599999999998, "end": 2192.02, "text": " To make this system mathematically rigorous, the text introduces the framework of variational dynamics.", "tokens": [50797, 1407, 652, 341, 1185, 44003, 29882, 11, 264, 2487, 31472, 264, 8388, 295, 3034, 1478, 15679, 13, 51085], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11422795747455798, "compression_ratio": 1.6592592592592592, "no_speech_prob": 3.0443538315272356e-12}, {"id": 638, "seek": 217762, "start": 2192.42, "end": 2193.52, "text": " Variational dynamics.", "tokens": [51105, 32511, 1478, 15679, 13, 51160], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11422795747455798, "compression_ratio": 1.6592592592592592, "no_speech_prob": 3.0443538315272356e-12}, {"id": 639, "seek": 217762, "start": 2193.7, "end": 2200.7, "text": " The entire semantic field is governed by an overarching energy functional, which is denoted mathematically as H.", "tokens": [51169, 440, 2302, 47982, 2519, 307, 35529, 538, 364, 45501, 2281, 11745, 11, 597, 307, 1441, 23325, 44003, 382, 389, 13, 51519], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11422795747455798, "compression_ratio": 1.6592592592592592, "no_speech_prob": 3.0443538315272356e-12}, {"id": 640, "seek": 217762, "start": 2201.04, "end": 2205.94, "text": " Is this energy in the literal physics sense, like kinetic or potential energy?", "tokens": [51536, 1119, 341, 2281, 294, 264, 20411, 10649, 2020, 11, 411, 27135, 420, 3995, 2281, 30, 51781], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11422795747455798, "compression_ratio": 1.6592592592592592, "no_speech_prob": 3.0443538315272356e-12}, {"id": 641, "seek": 220594, "start": 2205.94, "end": 2208.64, "text": " It acts exactly like energy in a physical system.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 10672, 2293, 411, 2281, 294, 257, 4001, 1185, 13, 50500], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1518836833061056, "compression_ratio": 1.6473029045643153, "no_speech_prob": 1.616911357409101e-12}, {"id": 642, "seek": 220594, "start": 2209.12, "end": 2212.88, "text": " The field is in a perpetual state of trying to minimize this energy functional.", "tokens": [50524, 440, 2519, 307, 294, 257, 48216, 1785, 295, 1382, 281, 17522, 341, 2281, 11745, 13, 50712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1518836833061056, "compression_ratio": 1.6473029045643153, "no_speech_prob": 1.616911357409101e-12}, {"id": 643, "seek": 220594, "start": 2213.0, "end": 2213.7400000000002, "text": " Trying to minimize it.", "tokens": [50718, 20180, 281, 17522, 309, 13, 50755], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1518836833061056, "compression_ratio": 1.6473029045643153, "no_speech_prob": 1.616911357409101e-12}, {"id": 644, "seek": 220594, "start": 2213.92, "end": 2216.7000000000003, "text": " You can visualize it as a landscape of hills and valleys.", "tokens": [50764, 509, 393, 23273, 309, 382, 257, 9661, 295, 21379, 293, 45614, 13, 50903], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1518836833061056, "compression_ratio": 1.6473029045643153, "no_speech_prob": 1.616911357409101e-12}, {"id": 645, "seek": 220594, "start": 2217.38, "end": 2226.0, "text": " Gradient descent naturally pulls the field's values, its coherence, and its entropy down into the valleys towards stable, low-energy configurations.", "tokens": [50937, 16710, 1196, 23475, 8195, 16982, 264, 2519, 311, 4190, 11, 1080, 26528, 655, 11, 293, 1080, 30867, 760, 666, 264, 45614, 3030, 8351, 11, 2295, 12, 49016, 31493, 13, 51368], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1518836833061056, "compression_ratio": 1.6473029045643153, "no_speech_prob": 1.616911357409101e-12}, {"id": 646, "seek": 220594, "start": 2226.4, "end": 2227.3, "text": " Like water flowing downhill.", "tokens": [51388, 1743, 1281, 13974, 29929, 13, 51433], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1518836833061056, "compression_ratio": 1.6473029045643153, "no_speech_prob": 1.616911357409101e-12}, {"id": 647, "seek": 220594, "start": 2227.62, "end": 2228.18, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51449, 7587, 13, 51477], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1518836833061056, "compression_ratio": 1.6473029045643153, "no_speech_prob": 1.616911357409101e-12}, {"id": 648, "seek": 222818, "start": 2228.18, "end": 2240.2, "text": " When we talked earlier about intrinsic physics happening automatically, like a storm settling or mud drying, that is simply the mathematics of the field sliding down the energy gradient into a comfortable, admissible state.", "tokens": [50365, 1133, 321, 2825, 3071, 466, 35698, 10649, 2737, 6772, 11, 411, 257, 7679, 33841, 420, 8933, 22709, 11, 300, 307, 2935, 264, 18666, 295, 264, 2519, 21169, 760, 264, 2281, 16235, 666, 257, 4619, 11, 5910, 41073, 1785, 13, 50966], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08951629681533642, "compression_ratio": 1.6719367588932805, "no_speech_prob": 1.555205942325999e-12}, {"id": 649, "seek": 222818, "start": 2240.48, "end": 2243.6, "text": " Okay, I follow the visual of sliding down into a valley.", "tokens": [50980, 1033, 11, 286, 1524, 264, 5056, 295, 21169, 760, 666, 257, 17636, 13, 51136], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08951629681533642, "compression_ratio": 1.6719367588932805, "no_speech_prob": 1.555205942325999e-12}, {"id": 650, "seek": 222818, "start": 2244.14, "end": 2252.66, "text": " But wait, if every single thing in the universe is just sliding down an energy gradient to a stop, how does the fountain keep flowing forever?", "tokens": [51163, 583, 1699, 11, 498, 633, 2167, 551, 294, 264, 6445, 307, 445, 21169, 760, 364, 2281, 16235, 281, 257, 1590, 11, 577, 775, 264, 29451, 1066, 13974, 5680, 30, 51589], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08951629681533642, "compression_ratio": 1.6719367588932805, "no_speech_prob": 1.555205942325999e-12}, {"id": 651, "seek": 225266, "start": 2252.66, "end": 2254.22, "text": " That's the paradox, isn't it?", "tokens": [50365, 663, 311, 264, 26221, 11, 1943, 380, 309, 30, 50443], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15303886347803577, "compression_ratio": 1.6563573883161513, "no_speech_prob": 1.75475595425717e-12}, {"id": 652, "seek": 225266, "start": 2254.3599999999997, "end": 2254.52, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50450, 1779, 13, 50458], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15303886347803577, "compression_ratio": 1.6563573883161513, "no_speech_prob": 1.75475595425717e-12}, {"id": 653, "seek": 225266, "start": 2254.8999999999996, "end": 2260.14, "text": " Wouldn't a system that is constantly minimizing its energy eventually freeze completely solid?", "tokens": [50477, 26291, 380, 257, 1185, 300, 307, 6460, 46608, 1080, 2281, 4728, 15959, 2584, 5100, 30, 50739], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15303886347803577, "compression_ratio": 1.6563573883161513, "no_speech_prob": 1.75475595425717e-12}, {"id": 654, "seek": 225266, "start": 2260.3999999999996, "end": 2260.72, "text": " Mm-hmm.", "tokens": [50752, 8266, 12, 10250, 13, 50768], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15303886347803577, "compression_ratio": 1.6563573883161513, "no_speech_prob": 1.75475595425717e-12}, {"id": 655, "seek": 225266, "start": 2260.94, "end": 2265.2599999999998, "text": " Wouldn't we just end up with flat puddles instead of dynamic fountains?", "tokens": [50779, 26291, 380, 321, 445, 917, 493, 365, 4962, 14166, 21915, 2602, 295, 8546, 283, 792, 2315, 30, 50995], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15303886347803577, "compression_ratio": 1.6563573883161513, "no_speech_prob": 1.75475595425717e-12}, {"id": 656, "seek": 225266, "start": 2265.44, "end": 2267.7599999999998, "text": " That is the brilliance of the mathematical design.", "tokens": [51004, 663, 307, 264, 8695, 6276, 295, 264, 18894, 1715, 13, 51120], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15303886347803577, "compression_ratio": 1.6563573883161513, "no_speech_prob": 1.75475595425717e-12}, {"id": 657, "seek": 225266, "start": 2267.96, "end": 2279.12, "text": " To sustain continuous motion without draining all the energy out of the system, the fast clock components, specifically flow and coherence, engage in what the text calls Hamiltonian oscillation.", "tokens": [51130, 1407, 6769, 10957, 5394, 1553, 42916, 439, 264, 2281, 484, 295, 264, 1185, 11, 264, 2370, 7830, 6677, 11, 4682, 3095, 293, 26528, 655, 11, 4683, 294, 437, 264, 2487, 5498, 18484, 952, 18225, 399, 13, 51688], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15303886347803577, "compression_ratio": 1.6563573883161513, "no_speech_prob": 1.75475595425717e-12}, {"id": 658, "seek": 225266, "start": 2279.2599999999998, "end": 2280.54, "text": " Hamiltonian oscillation.", "tokens": [51695, 18484, 952, 18225, 399, 13, 51759], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15303886347803577, "compression_ratio": 1.6563573883161513, "no_speech_prob": 1.75475595425717e-12}, {"id": 659, "seek": 228054, "start": 2280.54, "end": 2282.42, "text": " They definitely need an analogy for that.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 2138, 643, 364, 21663, 337, 300, 13, 50459], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15785735845565796, "compression_ratio": 1.712837837837838, "no_speech_prob": 2.0595430742786913e-12}, {"id": 660, "seek": 228054, "start": 2282.48, "end": 2283.84, "text": " How does that keep the fountain moving?", "tokens": [50462, 1012, 775, 300, 1066, 264, 29451, 2684, 30, 50530], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15785735845565796, "compression_ratio": 1.712837837837838, "no_speech_prob": 2.0595430742786913e-12}, {"id": 661, "seek": 228054, "start": 2284.2, "end": 2287.5, "text": " Think of a pendulum swinging or a planet orbiting a star.", "tokens": [50548, 6557, 295, 257, 44103, 29500, 420, 257, 5054, 48985, 257, 3543, 13, 50713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15785735845565796, "compression_ratio": 1.712837837837838, "no_speech_prob": 2.0595430742786913e-12}, {"id": 662, "seek": 228054, "start": 2287.84, "end": 2288.1, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50730, 1033, 13, 50743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15785735845565796, "compression_ratio": 1.712837837837838, "no_speech_prob": 2.0595430742786913e-12}, {"id": 663, "seek": 228054, "start": 2288.22, "end": 2291.44, "text": " In a perfect vacuum, a pendulum doesn't lose energy.", "tokens": [50749, 682, 257, 2176, 14224, 11, 257, 44103, 1177, 380, 3624, 2281, 13, 50910], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15785735845565796, "compression_ratio": 1.712837837837838, "no_speech_prob": 2.0595430742786913e-12}, {"id": 664, "seek": 228054, "start": 2291.7, "end": 2295.96, "text": " It constantly trades potential energy for kinetic energy back and forth forever.", "tokens": [50923, 467, 6460, 21287, 3995, 2281, 337, 27135, 2281, 646, 293, 5220, 5680, 13, 51136], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15785735845565796, "compression_ratio": 1.712837837837838, "no_speech_prob": 2.0595430742786913e-12}, {"id": 665, "seek": 228054, "start": 2296.08, "end": 2296.32, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51142, 1779, 13, 51154], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15785735845565796, "compression_ratio": 1.712837837837838, "no_speech_prob": 2.0595430742786913e-12}, {"id": 666, "seek": 228054, "start": 2296.4, "end": 2297.32, "text": " It just keeps going.", "tokens": [51158, 467, 445, 5965, 516, 13, 51204], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15785735845565796, "compression_ratio": 1.712837837837838, "no_speech_prob": 2.0595430742786913e-12}, {"id": 667, "seek": 228054, "start": 2297.32, "end": 2305.7599999999998, "text": " In the semantic field, instead of flowing downhill into a valley to lose energy, the field can flow sideways along a contour of constant energy.", "tokens": [51204, 682, 264, 47982, 2519, 11, 2602, 295, 13974, 29929, 666, 257, 17636, 281, 3624, 2281, 11, 264, 2519, 393, 3095, 26092, 2051, 257, 21234, 295, 5754, 2281, 13, 51626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15785735845565796, "compression_ratio": 1.712837837837838, "no_speech_prob": 2.0595430742786913e-12}, {"id": 668, "seek": 228054, "start": 2305.92, "end": 2306.4, "text": " Sideways.", "tokens": [51634, 19026, 942, 13, 51658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15785735845565796, "compression_ratio": 1.712837837837838, "no_speech_prob": 2.0595430742786913e-12}, {"id": 669, "seek": 228054, "start": 2306.7, "end": 2307.04, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51673, 1079, 13, 51690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15785735845565796, "compression_ratio": 1.712837837837838, "no_speech_prob": 2.0595430742786913e-12}, {"id": 670, "seek": 228054, "start": 2307.56, "end": 2310.34, "text": " It perfectly trades coherence for flow.", "tokens": [51716, 467, 6239, 21287, 26528, 655, 337, 3095, 13, 51855], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15785735845565796, "compression_ratio": 1.712837837837838, "no_speech_prob": 2.0595430742786913e-12}, {"id": 671, "seek": 231054, "start": 2310.54, "end": 2312.24, "text": " Back and forth, endlessly.", "tokens": [50365, 5833, 293, 5220, 11, 44920, 13, 50450], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24022535596575056, "compression_ratio": 1.4479166666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.861047340540045e-12}, {"id": 672, "seek": 231054, "start": 2312.62, "end": 2312.86, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50469, 3153, 13, 50481], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24022535596575056, "compression_ratio": 1.4479166666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.861047340540045e-12}, {"id": 673, "seek": 231054, "start": 2312.86, "end": 2317.7799999999997, "text": " As the flow of the water rises, its coherence briefly dips, and vice versa.", "tokens": [50481, 1018, 264, 3095, 295, 264, 1281, 21373, 11, 1080, 26528, 655, 10515, 47814, 11, 293, 11964, 25650, 13, 50727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24022535596575056, "compression_ratio": 1.4479166666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.861047340540045e-12}, {"id": 674, "seek": 231054, "start": 2318.2799999999997, "end": 2320.96, "text": " It is mathematically orbiting its own existence.", "tokens": [50752, 467, 307, 44003, 48985, 1080, 1065, 9123, 13, 50886], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24022535596575056, "compression_ratio": 1.4479166666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.861047340540045e-12}, {"id": 675, "seek": 231054, "start": 2321.7599999999998, "end": 2326.16, "text": " The fountain's water cycles indefinitely without ever losing overall energy to the exchange.", "tokens": [50926, 440, 29451, 311, 1281, 17796, 24162, 10925, 1553, 1562, 7027, 4787, 2281, 281, 264, 7742, 13, 51146], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24022535596575056, "compression_ratio": 1.4479166666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.861047340540045e-12}, {"id": 676, "seek": 231054, "start": 2326.36, "end": 2328.0, "text": " It is a conservative system.", "tokens": [51156, 467, 307, 257, 13780, 1185, 13, 51238], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24022535596575056, "compression_ratio": 1.4479166666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.861047340540045e-12}, {"id": 677, "seek": 232800, "start": 2328.0, "end": 2332.16, "text": " So the fountain is literally mathematically orbiting its own shape.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 264, 29451, 307, 3736, 44003, 48985, 1080, 1065, 3909, 13, 50573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21763036442899156, "compression_ratio": 1.551219512195122, "no_speech_prob": 1.7654580054815572e-12}, {"id": 678, "seek": 232800, "start": 2332.96, "end": 2334.84, "text": " That is incredibly beautiful.", "tokens": [50613, 663, 307, 6252, 2238, 13, 50707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21763036442899156, "compression_ratio": 1.551219512195122, "no_speech_prob": 1.7654580054815572e-12}, {"id": 679, "seek": 232800, "start": 2334.96, "end": 2336.14, "text": " It's very elegant math.", "tokens": [50713, 467, 311, 588, 21117, 5221, 13, 50772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21763036442899156, "compression_ratio": 1.551219512195122, "no_speech_prob": 1.7654580054815572e-12}, {"id": 680, "seek": 232800, "start": 2336.38, "end": 2338.96, "text": " But that covers consistency over time for a single object.", "tokens": [50784, 583, 300, 10538, 14416, 670, 565, 337, 257, 2167, 2657, 13, 50913], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21763036442899156, "compression_ratio": 1.551219512195122, "no_speech_prob": 1.7654580054815572e-12}, {"id": 681, "seek": 232800, "start": 2339.3, "end": 2339.58, "text": " Mm-hmm.", "tokens": [50930, 8266, 12, 10250, 13, 50944], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21763036442899156, "compression_ratio": 1.551219512195122, "no_speech_prob": 1.7654580054815572e-12}, {"id": 682, "seek": 232800, "start": 2339.7, "end": 2341.14, "text": " What about spatial consistency?", "tokens": [50950, 708, 466, 23598, 14416, 30, 51022], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21763036442899156, "compression_ratio": 1.551219512195122, "no_speech_prob": 1.7654580054815572e-12}, {"id": 683, "seek": 232800, "start": 2341.42, "end": 2344.62, "text": " We've talked about a single point or a single fountain, but let's zoom out.", "tokens": [51036, 492, 600, 2825, 466, 257, 2167, 935, 420, 257, 2167, 29451, 11, 457, 718, 311, 8863, 484, 13, 51196], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21763036442899156, "compression_ratio": 1.551219512195122, "no_speech_prob": 1.7654580054815572e-12}, {"id": 684, "seek": 232800, "start": 2344.66, "end": 2344.84, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51198, 1033, 13, 51207], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21763036442899156, "compression_ratio": 1.551219512195122, "no_speech_prob": 1.7654580054815572e-12}, {"id": 685, "seek": 232800, "start": 2344.88, "end": 2345.4, "text": " Let's zoom out.", "tokens": [51209, 961, 311, 8863, 484, 13, 51235], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21763036442899156, "compression_ratio": 1.551219512195122, "no_speech_prob": 1.7654580054815572e-12}, {"id": 686, "seek": 234540, "start": 2345.4, "end": 2354.3, "text": " What if the AI generates a massive, sprawling courtyard, and the left side of the courtyard generates a beautiful, ornate archway door?", "tokens": [50365, 708, 498, 264, 7318, 23815, 257, 5994, 11, 22734, 1688, 41364, 11, 293, 264, 1411, 1252, 295, 264, 41364, 23815, 257, 2238, 11, 420, 77, 473, 3912, 676, 2853, 30, 50810], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11060236417330228, "compression_ratio": 1.6047904191616766, "no_speech_prob": 1.8104581419112198e-12}, {"id": 687, "seek": 234540, "start": 2354.52, "end": 2354.86, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50821, 1033, 13, 50838], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11060236417330228, "compression_ratio": 1.6047904191616766, "no_speech_prob": 1.8104581419112198e-12}, {"id": 688, "seek": 234540, "start": 2355.02, "end": 2361.02, "text": " But the right side of the courtyard generates a solid, unbroken wall that completely blocks where the door was supposed to be.", "tokens": [50846, 583, 264, 558, 1252, 295, 264, 41364, 23815, 257, 5100, 11, 517, 37947, 2929, 300, 2584, 8474, 689, 264, 2853, 390, 3442, 281, 312, 13, 51146], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11060236417330228, "compression_ratio": 1.6047904191616766, "no_speech_prob": 1.8104581419112198e-12}, {"id": 689, "seek": 236102, "start": 2361.02, "end": 2364.42, "text": " How does the math catch a spatial contradiction like that?", "tokens": [50365, 1012, 775, 264, 5221, 3745, 257, 23598, 34937, 411, 300, 30, 50535], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18073712517233456, "compression_ratio": 1.5942028985507246, "no_speech_prob": 2.1928101695545266e-12}, {"id": 690, "seek": 236102, "start": 2364.7599999999998, "end": 2369.34, "text": " Catching spatial contradictions requires a concept from advanced topology known as sheaves.", "tokens": [50552, 23869, 278, 23598, 15858, 15607, 7029, 257, 3410, 490, 7339, 1192, 1793, 2570, 382, 750, 5423, 13, 50781], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18073712517233456, "compression_ratio": 1.5942028985507246, "no_speech_prob": 2.1928101695545266e-12}, {"id": 691, "seek": 236102, "start": 2369.58, "end": 2370.06, "text": " Sheaves.", "tokens": [50793, 1240, 5423, 13, 50817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18073712517233456, "compression_ratio": 1.5942028985507246, "no_speech_prob": 2.1928101695545266e-12}, {"id": 692, "seek": 236102, "start": 2370.32, "end": 2371.16, "text": " Like a bundle of wheat.", "tokens": [50830, 1743, 257, 24438, 295, 16691, 13, 50872], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18073712517233456, "compression_ratio": 1.5942028985507246, "no_speech_prob": 2.1928101695545266e-12}, {"id": 693, "seek": 236102, "start": 2371.48, "end": 2373.36, "text": " Spelled the same, but different concept.", "tokens": [50888, 3550, 5929, 264, 912, 11, 457, 819, 3410, 13, 50982], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18073712517233456, "compression_ratio": 1.5942028985507246, "no_speech_prob": 2.1928101695545266e-12}, {"id": 694, "seek": 236102, "start": 2374.18, "end": 2378.66, "text": " Sheaf theory deals precisely with the mathematics of local to global consistency.", "tokens": [51023, 1240, 2792, 5261, 11215, 13402, 365, 264, 18666, 295, 2654, 281, 4338, 14416, 13, 51247], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18073712517233456, "compression_ratio": 1.5942028985507246, "no_speech_prob": 2.1928101695545266e-12}, {"id": 695, "seek": 236102, "start": 2379.0, "end": 2379.24, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51264, 1033, 13, 51276], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18073712517233456, "compression_ratio": 1.5942028985507246, "no_speech_prob": 2.1928101695545266e-12}, {"id": 696, "seek": 236102, "start": 2379.28, "end": 2379.92, "text": " How does it work?", "tokens": [51278, 1012, 775, 309, 589, 30, 51310], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18073712517233456, "compression_ratio": 1.5942028985507246, "no_speech_prob": 2.1928101695545266e-12}, {"id": 697, "seek": 237992, "start": 2379.92, "end": 2386.1, "text": " I want you to imagine covering our entire courtyard in hundreds of overlapping mathematical patches like a quilt.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 528, 291, 281, 3811, 10322, 527, 2302, 41364, 294, 6779, 295, 33535, 18894, 26531, 411, 257, 27566, 13, 50674], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07210299006679602, "compression_ratio": 1.8506944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482822915054763e-12}, {"id": 698, "seek": 237992, "start": 2386.86, "end": 2395.96, "text": " A sheaf is a mathematical structure that checks to ensure that the locally admissible data in patch A perfectly glues together with the locally admissible data in patch B,", "tokens": [50712, 316, 750, 2792, 307, 257, 18894, 3877, 300, 13834, 281, 5586, 300, 264, 16143, 5910, 41073, 1412, 294, 9972, 316, 6239, 1563, 1247, 1214, 365, 264, 16143, 5910, 41073, 1412, 294, 9972, 363, 11, 51167], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07210299006679602, "compression_ratio": 1.8506944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482822915054763e-12}, {"id": 699, "seek": 237992, "start": 2396.42, "end": 2399.2000000000003, "text": " specifically along the exact strip where they overlap.", "tokens": [51190, 4682, 2051, 264, 1900, 12828, 689, 436, 19959, 13, 51329], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07210299006679602, "compression_ratio": 1.8506944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482822915054763e-12}, {"id": 700, "seek": 237992, "start": 2399.66, "end": 2402.1800000000003, "text": " It's like stitching a panorama photo together on your phone.", "tokens": [51352, 467, 311, 411, 30714, 257, 2462, 32988, 5052, 1214, 322, 428, 2593, 13, 51478], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07210299006679602, "compression_ratio": 1.8506944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482822915054763e-12}, {"id": 701, "seek": 237992, "start": 2402.2400000000002, "end": 2403.26, "text": " A perfect analogy.", "tokens": [51481, 316, 2176, 21663, 13, 51532], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07210299006679602, "compression_ratio": 1.8506944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482822915054763e-12}, {"id": 702, "seek": 237992, "start": 2403.26, "end": 2409.84, "text": " The algorithm forces the left picture and the right picture to agree on where the horizon line is in the middle.", "tokens": [51532, 440, 9284, 5874, 264, 1411, 3036, 293, 264, 558, 3036, 281, 3986, 322, 689, 264, 18046, 1622, 307, 294, 264, 2808, 13, 51861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07210299006679602, "compression_ratio": 1.8506944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482822915054763e-12}, {"id": 703, "seek": 240992, "start": 2409.92, "end": 2410.2400000000002, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50381], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16791299012330202, "compression_ratio": 1.72, "no_speech_prob": 1.868777702029867e-12}, {"id": 704, "seek": 240992, "start": 2410.6, "end": 2417.42, "text": " And what is truly fascinating here is how sheaf theory fundamentally redefines the concept of an AI hallucination.", "tokens": [50399, 400, 437, 307, 4908, 10343, 510, 307, 577, 750, 2792, 5261, 17879, 38818, 1652, 264, 3410, 295, 364, 7318, 35212, 2486, 13, 50740], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16791299012330202, "compression_ratio": 1.72, "no_speech_prob": 1.868777702029867e-12}, {"id": 705, "seek": 240992, "start": 2417.62, "end": 2418.56, "text": " Oh, how so?", "tokens": [50750, 876, 11, 577, 370, 30, 50797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16791299012330202, "compression_ratio": 1.72, "no_speech_prob": 1.868777702029867e-12}, {"id": 706, "seek": 240992, "start": 2418.7200000000003, "end": 2424.06, "text": " In current language models, a hallucination is just viewed as a wrong fact, a bad output.", "tokens": [50805, 682, 2190, 2856, 5245, 11, 257, 35212, 2486, 307, 445, 19174, 382, 257, 2085, 1186, 11, 257, 1578, 5598, 13, 51072], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16791299012330202, "compression_ratio": 1.72, "no_speech_prob": 1.868777702029867e-12}, {"id": 707, "seek": 240992, "start": 2424.1800000000003, "end": 2424.4, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51078, 1779, 13, 51089], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16791299012330202, "compression_ratio": 1.72, "no_speech_prob": 1.868777702029867e-12}, {"id": 708, "seek": 240992, "start": 2424.5, "end": 2430.28, "text": " But in this field theory, a hallucination is diagnosed mathematically as a cohomological obstruction.", "tokens": [51094, 583, 294, 341, 2519, 5261, 11, 257, 35212, 2486, 307, 16899, 44003, 382, 257, 21683, 298, 4383, 49711, 13, 51383], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16791299012330202, "compression_ratio": 1.72, "no_speech_prob": 1.868777702029867e-12}, {"id": 709, "seek": 240992, "start": 2430.28, "end": 2431.94, "text": " Co-homological obstruction.", "tokens": [51383, 3066, 12, 71, 298, 4383, 49711, 13, 51466], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16791299012330202, "compression_ratio": 1.72, "no_speech_prob": 1.868777702029867e-12}, {"id": 710, "seek": 240992, "start": 2432.16, "end": 2434.64, "text": " That sounds like a fatal diagnosis for a simulation.", "tokens": [51477, 663, 3263, 411, 257, 24069, 15217, 337, 257, 16575, 13, 51601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16791299012330202, "compression_ratio": 1.72, "no_speech_prob": 1.868777702029867e-12}, {"id": 711, "seek": 240992, "start": 2435.08, "end": 2436.16, "text": " It essentially is.", "tokens": [51623, 467, 4476, 307, 13, 51677], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16791299012330202, "compression_ratio": 1.72, "no_speech_prob": 1.868777702029867e-12}, {"id": 712, "seek": 243616, "start": 2436.16, "end": 2444.5, "text": " Imagine you are stitching that panorama and the left side has a horizon line, but the right side is tilted at a 45 degree angle.", "tokens": [50365, 11739, 291, 366, 30714, 300, 2462, 32988, 293, 264, 1411, 1252, 575, 257, 18046, 1622, 11, 457, 264, 558, 1252, 307, 43229, 412, 257, 6905, 4314, 5802, 13, 50782], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11482593116410282, "compression_ratio": 1.68259385665529, "no_speech_prob": 1.8613179574022976e-12}, {"id": 713, "seek": 243616, "start": 2444.8999999999996, "end": 2445.68, "text": " You can't put them together.", "tokens": [50802, 509, 393, 380, 829, 552, 1214, 13, 50841], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11482593116410282, "compression_ratio": 1.68259385665529, "no_speech_prob": 1.8613179574022976e-12}, {"id": 714, "seek": 243616, "start": 2445.7999999999997, "end": 2447.8999999999996, "text": " You cannot glue them together without tearing the image.", "tokens": [50847, 509, 2644, 8998, 552, 1214, 1553, 29401, 264, 3256, 13, 50952], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11482593116410282, "compression_ratio": 1.68259385665529, "no_speech_prob": 1.8613179574022976e-12}, {"id": 715, "seek": 243616, "start": 2448.64, "end": 2456.22, "text": " A cohomological obstruction means that the local patches of reality, which might look perfectly fine and physically accurate when viewed in isolation,", "tokens": [50989, 316, 21683, 298, 4383, 49711, 1355, 300, 264, 2654, 26531, 295, 4103, 11, 597, 1062, 574, 6239, 2489, 293, 9762, 8559, 562, 19174, 294, 16001, 11, 51368], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11482593116410282, "compression_ratio": 1.68259385665529, "no_speech_prob": 1.8613179574022976e-12}, {"id": 716, "seek": 243616, "start": 2456.94, "end": 2461.98, "text": " mathematically cannot be glued into a single non-contradictory global reality.", "tokens": [51404, 44003, 2644, 312, 28008, 666, 257, 2167, 2107, 12, 9000, 6206, 985, 827, 4338, 4103, 13, 51656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11482593116410282, "compression_ratio": 1.68259385665529, "no_speech_prob": 1.8613179574022976e-12}, {"id": 717, "seek": 243616, "start": 2462.18, "end": 2464.7, "text": " Because the overlapping data contradicts itself.", "tokens": [51666, 1436, 264, 33535, 1412, 28900, 82, 2564, 13, 51792], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11482593116410282, "compression_ratio": 1.68259385665529, "no_speech_prob": 1.8613179574022976e-12}, {"id": 718, "seek": 246470, "start": 2464.7, "end": 2465.2999999999997, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50395], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18083305792375046, "compression_ratio": 1.547008547008547, "no_speech_prob": 2.3160579357139888e-12}, {"id": 719, "seek": 246470, "start": 2465.8199999999997, "end": 2472.18, "text": " The sheaf theory detects this geometric obstruction and prevents that impossible reality from committing to the database.", "tokens": [50421, 440, 750, 2792, 5261, 5531, 82, 341, 33246, 49711, 293, 22367, 300, 6243, 4103, 490, 26659, 281, 264, 8149, 13, 50739], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18083305792375046, "compression_ratio": 1.547008547008547, "no_speech_prob": 2.3160579357139888e-12}, {"id": 720, "seek": 246470, "start": 2472.52, "end": 2475.3799999999997, "text": " The math literally acts as the immune system of space.", "tokens": [50756, 440, 5221, 3736, 10672, 382, 264, 11992, 1185, 295, 1901, 13, 50899], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18083305792375046, "compression_ratio": 1.547008547008547, "no_speech_prob": 2.3160579357139888e-12}, {"id": 721, "seek": 246470, "start": 2475.54, "end": 2476.02, "text": " It does.", "tokens": [50907, 467, 775, 13, 50931], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18083305792375046, "compression_ratio": 1.547008547008547, "no_speech_prob": 2.3160579357139888e-12}, {"id": 722, "seek": 246470, "start": 2476.2999999999997, "end": 2477.2799999999997, "text": " But what about time?", "tokens": [50945, 583, 437, 466, 565, 30, 50994], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18083305792375046, "compression_ratio": 1.547008547008547, "no_speech_prob": 2.3160579357139888e-12}, {"id": 723, "seek": 246470, "start": 2478.8599999999997, "end": 2483.14, "text": " If sheaves protect the spatial geometry of the world, what protects the history?", "tokens": [51073, 759, 750, 5423, 2371, 264, 23598, 18426, 295, 264, 1002, 11, 437, 22583, 264, 2503, 30, 51287], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18083305792375046, "compression_ratio": 1.547008547008547, "no_speech_prob": 2.3160579357139888e-12}, {"id": 724, "seek": 246470, "start": 2483.3199999999997, "end": 2484.2799999999997, "text": " Conservation laws.", "tokens": [51296, 40131, 6064, 13, 51344], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18083305792375046, "compression_ratio": 1.547008547008547, "no_speech_prob": 2.3160579357139888e-12}, {"id": 725, "seek": 246470, "start": 2484.5, "end": 2486.64, "text": " Let me set up a hypothetical scenario for you.", "tokens": [51355, 961, 385, 992, 493, 257, 33053, 9005, 337, 291, 13, 51462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18083305792375046, "compression_ratio": 1.547008547008547, "no_speech_prob": 2.3160579357139888e-12}, {"id": 726, "seek": 248664, "start": 2486.64, "end": 2494.02, "text": " Let's say a malicious user, or just a really severe glitch in the system, tampers with the AI's historical log.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 311, 584, 257, 33496, 4195, 11, 420, 445, 257, 534, 8922, 23552, 294, 264, 1185, 11, 21424, 433, 365, 264, 7318, 311, 8584, 3565, 13, 50734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19115897070003462, "compression_ratio": 1.575268817204301, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967552359138272e-12}, {"id": 727, "seek": 248664, "start": 2494.46, "end": 2496.98, "text": " It rewrites what happened in the courtyard yesterday.", "tokens": [50756, 467, 319, 86, 30931, 437, 2011, 294, 264, 41364, 5186, 13, 50882], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19115897070003462, "compression_ratio": 1.575268817204301, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967552359138272e-12}, {"id": 728, "seek": 248664, "start": 2497.42, "end": 2500.12, "text": " How does the system catch a lie in the timeline?", "tokens": [50904, 1012, 775, 264, 1185, 3745, 257, 4544, 294, 264, 12933, 30, 51039], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19115897070003462, "compression_ratio": 1.575268817204301, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967552359138272e-12}, {"id": 729, "seek": 248664, "start": 2500.12, "end": 2503.3799999999997, "text": " To defend the timeline, the text relies on Nother's theorem.", "tokens": [51039, 1407, 8602, 264, 12933, 11, 264, 2487, 30910, 322, 426, 802, 311, 20904, 13, 51202], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19115897070003462, "compression_ratio": 1.575268817204301, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967552359138272e-12}, {"id": 730, "seek": 248664, "start": 2503.54, "end": 2504.14, "text": " Nother's theorem.", "tokens": [51210, 426, 802, 311, 20904, 13, 51240], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19115897070003462, "compression_ratio": 1.575268817204301, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967552359138272e-12}, {"id": 731, "seek": 250414, "start": 2504.14, "end": 2504.7999999999997, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50398], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19158061563152157, "compression_ratio": 1.5771144278606966, "no_speech_prob": 2.0439316471970725e-12}, {"id": 732, "seek": 250414, "start": 2505.24, "end": 2509.6, "text": " In physics, Nother's theorem relates continuous symmetries to conservation laws.", "tokens": [50420, 682, 10649, 11, 426, 802, 311, 20904, 16155, 10957, 14232, 302, 2244, 281, 16185, 6064, 13, 50638], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19158061563152157, "compression_ratio": 1.5771144278606966, "no_speech_prob": 2.0439316471970725e-12}, {"id": 733, "seek": 250414, "start": 2510.16, "end": 2515.0, "text": " It states that for every symmetry in nature, there is a corresponding conserved quantity.", "tokens": [50666, 467, 4368, 300, 337, 633, 25440, 294, 3687, 11, 456, 307, 257, 11760, 1014, 6913, 11275, 13, 50908], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19158061563152157, "compression_ratio": 1.5771144278606966, "no_speech_prob": 2.0439316471970725e-12}, {"id": 734, "seek": 250414, "start": 2515.2, "end": 2515.44, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50918, 1033, 13, 50930], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19158061563152157, "compression_ratio": 1.5771144278606966, "no_speech_prob": 2.0439316471970725e-12}, {"id": 735, "seek": 250414, "start": 2515.68, "end": 2523.68, "text": " The text applies this to the semantic field, revealing three temporal conservation laws that fiercely protect the history of the world.", "tokens": [50942, 440, 2487, 13165, 341, 281, 264, 47982, 2519, 11, 23983, 1045, 30881, 16185, 6064, 300, 16334, 42879, 2371, 264, 2503, 295, 264, 1002, 13, 51342], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19158061563152157, "compression_ratio": 1.5771144278606966, "no_speech_prob": 2.0439316471970725e-12}, {"id": 736, "seek": 252368, "start": 2523.68, "end": 2532.2999999999997, "text": " A tampered history log will always, inevitably, get caught violating one of three specific symmetries, resulting in one of three lies.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 7677, 40004, 2503, 3565, 486, 1009, 11, 28171, 11, 483, 5415, 42201, 472, 295, 1045, 2685, 14232, 302, 2244, 11, 16505, 294, 472, 295, 1045, 9134, 13, 50796], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10519329401162955, "compression_ratio": 1.640495867768595, "no_speech_prob": 1.4217106224928555e-12}, {"id": 737, "seek": 252368, "start": 2532.7999999999997, "end": 2534.14, "text": " Let's break down the three lies.", "tokens": [50821, 961, 311, 1821, 760, 264, 1045, 9134, 13, 50888], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10519329401162955, "compression_ratio": 1.640495867768595, "no_speech_prob": 1.4217106224928555e-12}, {"id": 738, "seek": 252368, "start": 2534.3999999999996, "end": 2536.7799999999997, "text": " What is the first way a tampered history gets caught?", "tokens": [50901, 708, 307, 264, 700, 636, 257, 7677, 40004, 2503, 2170, 5415, 30, 51020], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10519329401162955, "compression_ratio": 1.640495867768595, "no_speech_prob": 1.4217106224928555e-12}, {"id": 739, "seek": 252368, "start": 2536.98, "end": 2539.16, "text": " Lie number one is the energy lie.", "tokens": [51030, 11197, 1230, 472, 307, 264, 2281, 4544, 13, 51139], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10519329401162955, "compression_ratio": 1.640495867768595, "no_speech_prob": 1.4217106224928555e-12}, {"id": 740, "seek": 252368, "start": 2539.24, "end": 2540.12, "text": " The energy lie.", "tokens": [51143, 440, 2281, 4544, 13, 51187], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10519329401162955, "compression_ratio": 1.640495867768595, "no_speech_prob": 1.4217106224928555e-12}, {"id": 741, "seek": 252368, "start": 2540.2999999999997, "end": 2547.04, "text": " Imagine the database log claims that the fountain's water suddenly started moving twice as fast at 3.00 p.m. yesterday.", "tokens": [51196, 11739, 264, 8149, 3565, 9441, 300, 264, 29451, 311, 1281, 5800, 1409, 2684, 6091, 382, 2370, 412, 805, 13, 628, 280, 13, 76, 13, 5186, 13, 51533], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10519329401162955, "compression_ratio": 1.640495867768595, "no_speech_prob": 1.4217106224928555e-12}, {"id": 742, "seek": 252368, "start": 2547.2, "end": 2547.46, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51541, 1033, 13, 51554], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10519329401162955, "compression_ratio": 1.640495867768595, "no_speech_prob": 1.4217106224928555e-12}, {"id": 743, "seek": 254746, "start": 2547.46, "end": 2555.5, "text": " But when the system checks the logs, there is no record of a storm, no added pump, and no external force proposed to cause that acceleration.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 562, 264, 1185, 13834, 264, 20820, 11, 456, 307, 572, 2136, 295, 257, 7679, 11, 572, 3869, 5889, 11, 293, 572, 8320, 3464, 10348, 281, 3082, 300, 17162, 13, 50767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12348717967356283, "compression_ratio": 1.60828025477707, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760884993625603e-12}, {"id": 744, "seek": 254746, "start": 2555.7, "end": 2556.96, "text": " The energy just came out of nowhere.", "tokens": [50777, 440, 2281, 445, 1361, 484, 295, 11159, 13, 50840], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12348717967356283, "compression_ratio": 1.60828025477707, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760884993625603e-12}, {"id": 745, "seek": 254746, "start": 2557.16, "end": 2557.62, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50850, 7587, 13, 50873], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12348717967356283, "compression_ratio": 1.60828025477707, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760884993625603e-12}, {"id": 746, "seek": 254746, "start": 2558.12, "end": 2561.26, "text": " That sudden jump in energy violates time translation symmetry.", "tokens": [50898, 663, 3990, 3012, 294, 2281, 3448, 1024, 565, 12853, 25440, 13, 51055], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12348717967356283, "compression_ratio": 1.60828025477707, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760884993625603e-12}, {"id": 747, "seek": 254746, "start": 2561.7400000000002, "end": 2563.54, "text": " Energy must be conserved across time.", "tokens": [51079, 14939, 1633, 312, 1014, 6913, 2108, 565, 13, 51169], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12348717967356283, "compression_ratio": 1.60828025477707, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760884993625603e-12}, {"id": 748, "seek": 254746, "start": 2564.04, "end": 2571.16, "text": " If the energy in a region jumps without a mathematically licensed source or an influx from a neighboring patch, the system knows the history is lying.", "tokens": [51194, 759, 264, 2281, 294, 257, 4458, 16704, 1553, 257, 44003, 25225, 4009, 420, 364, 9922, 2449, 490, 257, 31521, 9972, 11, 264, 1185, 3255, 264, 2503, 307, 8493, 13, 51550], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12348717967356283, "compression_ratio": 1.60828025477707, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760884993625603e-12}, {"id": 749, "seek": 254746, "start": 2571.6, "end": 2571.92, "text": " Caught.", "tokens": [51572, 7544, 1599, 13, 51588], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12348717967356283, "compression_ratio": 1.60828025477707, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760884993625603e-12}, {"id": 750, "seek": 254746, "start": 2572.2, "end": 2573.58, "text": " You cannot get free energy.", "tokens": [51602, 509, 2644, 483, 1737, 2281, 13, 51671], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12348717967356283, "compression_ratio": 1.60828025477707, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760884993625603e-12}, {"id": 751, "seek": 254746, "start": 2574.2400000000002, "end": 2574.44, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51704, 1033, 13, 51714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12348717967356283, "compression_ratio": 1.60828025477707, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760884993625603e-12}, {"id": 752, "seek": 254746, "start": 2574.66, "end": 2575.96, "text": " What is lie number two?", "tokens": [51725, 708, 307, 4544, 1230, 732, 30, 51790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12348717967356283, "compression_ratio": 1.60828025477707, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760884993625603e-12}, {"id": 753, "seek": 257596, "start": 2575.96, "end": 2577.86, "text": " Lie number two is the order lie.", "tokens": [50365, 11197, 1230, 732, 307, 264, 1668, 4544, 13, 50460], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13514387903134684, "compression_ratio": 1.7491525423728813, "no_speech_prob": 1.610996384036889e-12}, {"id": 754, "seek": 257596, "start": 2578.04, "end": 2578.7400000000002, "text": " The order lie.", "tokens": [50469, 440, 1668, 4544, 13, 50504], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13514387903134684, "compression_ratio": 1.7491525423728813, "no_speech_prob": 1.610996384036889e-12}, {"id": 755, "seek": 257596, "start": 2579.32, "end": 2583.08, "text": " Imagine two completely harmless, disconnected events occur.", "tokens": [50533, 11739, 732, 2584, 40160, 11, 29426, 3931, 5160, 13, 50721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13514387903134684, "compression_ratio": 1.7491525423728813, "no_speech_prob": 1.610996384036889e-12}, {"id": 756, "seek": 257596, "start": 2583.86, "end": 2591.82, "text": " You move a small bench on the extreme east side of the courtyard, and I inspect a tiny crack on the extreme west side of the courtyard.", "tokens": [50760, 509, 1286, 257, 1359, 10638, 322, 264, 8084, 10648, 1252, 295, 264, 41364, 11, 293, 286, 15018, 257, 5870, 6226, 322, 264, 8084, 7009, 1252, 295, 264, 41364, 13, 51158], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13514387903134684, "compression_ratio": 1.7491525423728813, "no_speech_prob": 1.610996384036889e-12}, {"id": 757, "seek": 257596, "start": 2592.14, "end": 2592.38, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51174, 1033, 13, 51186], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13514387903134684, "compression_ratio": 1.7491525423728813, "no_speech_prob": 1.610996384036889e-12}, {"id": 758, "seek": 257596, "start": 2592.56, "end": 2593.8, "text": " Two things happening far apart.", "tokens": [51195, 4453, 721, 2737, 1400, 4936, 13, 51257], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13514387903134684, "compression_ratio": 1.7491525423728813, "no_speech_prob": 1.610996384036889e-12}, {"id": 759, "seek": 257596, "start": 2593.98, "end": 2605.12, "text": " Because these events are separated by space and have no causal link, the total amount of residue accumulated in the world should be the exact same, regardless of whether you moved the bench first or I inspected the crack first.", "tokens": [51266, 1436, 613, 3931, 366, 12005, 538, 1901, 293, 362, 572, 38755, 2113, 11, 264, 3217, 2372, 295, 34799, 31346, 294, 264, 1002, 820, 312, 264, 1900, 912, 11, 10060, 295, 1968, 291, 4259, 264, 10638, 700, 420, 286, 1028, 10729, 264, 6226, 700, 13, 51823], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13514387903134684, "compression_ratio": 1.7491525423728813, "no_speech_prob": 1.610996384036889e-12}, {"id": 760, "seek": 257596, "start": 2605.12, "end": 2605.48, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51823, 1779, 13, 51841], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13514387903134684, "compression_ratio": 1.7491525423728813, "no_speech_prob": 1.610996384036889e-12}, {"id": 761, "seek": 260596, "start": 2605.96, "end": 2607.02, "text": " The order shouldn't matter.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1668, 4659, 380, 1871, 13, 50418], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10407223278963113, "compression_ratio": 1.5201793721973094, "no_speech_prob": 1.455068704414586e-12}, {"id": 762, "seek": 260596, "start": 2607.02, "end": 2617.32, "text": " But if a tampered log shows that the total physical residue of the courtyard changes depending on the order in which those two events are recorded, that violates domain relabeling symmetry.", "tokens": [50418, 583, 498, 257, 7677, 40004, 3565, 3110, 300, 264, 3217, 4001, 34799, 295, 264, 41364, 2962, 5413, 322, 264, 1668, 294, 597, 729, 732, 3931, 366, 8287, 11, 300, 3448, 1024, 9274, 1039, 455, 11031, 25440, 13, 50933], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10407223278963113, "compression_ratio": 1.5201793721973094, "no_speech_prob": 1.455068704414586e-12}, {"id": 763, "seek": 260596, "start": 2617.8, "end": 2618.38, "text": " Meaning what?", "tokens": [50957, 19948, 437, 30, 50986], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10407223278963113, "compression_ratio": 1.5201793721973094, "no_speech_prob": 1.455068704414586e-12}, {"id": 764, "seek": 260596, "start": 2618.52, "end": 2624.26, "text": " It means the causal graph has been corrupted and events are falsely interacting across time and space.", "tokens": [50993, 467, 1355, 264, 38755, 4295, 575, 668, 39480, 293, 3931, 366, 16720, 736, 18017, 2108, 565, 293, 1901, 13, 51280], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10407223278963113, "compression_ratio": 1.5201793721973094, "no_speech_prob": 1.455068704414586e-12}, {"id": 765, "seek": 260596, "start": 2624.46, "end": 2624.7, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51290, 3153, 13, 51302], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10407223278963113, "compression_ratio": 1.5201793721973094, "no_speech_prob": 1.455068704414586e-12}, {"id": 766, "seek": 262470, "start": 2624.7, "end": 2629.12, "text": " So it catches timeline tampering by checking if the butterfly effect is behaving correctly.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 309, 25496, 12933, 7677, 20055, 538, 8568, 498, 264, 22140, 1802, 307, 35263, 8944, 13, 50586], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15270360310872397, "compression_ratio": 1.6198347107438016, "no_speech_prob": 2.0034364792143045e-12}, {"id": 767, "seek": 262470, "start": 2630.04, "end": 2630.56, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50632, 7587, 13, 50658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15270360310872397, "compression_ratio": 1.6198347107438016, "no_speech_prob": 2.0034364792143045e-12}, {"id": 768, "seek": 262470, "start": 2630.96, "end": 2631.74, "text": " And the third lie.", "tokens": [50678, 400, 264, 2636, 4544, 13, 50717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15270360310872397, "compression_ratio": 1.6198347107438016, "no_speech_prob": 2.0034364792143045e-12}, {"id": 769, "seek": 262470, "start": 2631.9199999999996, "end": 2633.68, "text": " The third is the coherence lie.", "tokens": [50726, 440, 2636, 307, 264, 26528, 655, 4544, 13, 50814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15270360310872397, "compression_ratio": 1.6198347107438016, "no_speech_prob": 2.0034364792143045e-12}, {"id": 770, "seek": 262470, "start": 2633.8599999999997, "end": 2634.9199999999996, "text": " The coherence lie.", "tokens": [50823, 440, 26528, 655, 4544, 13, 50876], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15270360310872397, "compression_ratio": 1.6198347107438016, "no_speech_prob": 2.0034364792143045e-12}, {"id": 771, "seek": 262470, "start": 2635.16, "end": 2646.8599999999997, "text": " Imagine a patch of foggy, entirely unobserved ground in a dark corner of the courtyard suddenly becomes a fully certain, highly coherent, perfectly rendered stone path in the historical logs.", "tokens": [50888, 11739, 257, 9972, 295, 13648, 1480, 11, 7696, 8526, 929, 6913, 2727, 294, 257, 2877, 4538, 295, 264, 41364, 5800, 3643, 257, 4498, 1629, 11, 5405, 36239, 11, 6239, 28748, 7581, 3100, 294, 264, 8584, 20820, 13, 51473], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15270360310872397, "compression_ratio": 1.6198347107438016, "no_speech_prob": 2.0034364792143045e-12}, {"id": 772, "seek": 262470, "start": 2646.98, "end": 2648.3799999999997, "text": " Just spontaneously generated.", "tokens": [51479, 1449, 47632, 10833, 13, 51549], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15270360310872397, "compression_ratio": 1.6198347107438016, "no_speech_prob": 2.0034364792143045e-12}, {"id": 773, "seek": 264838, "start": 2648.38, "end": 2657.94, "text": " Yes, but there is no record of any observation event to act as a source of that certainty, and there is no inflow of coherence from surrounding resolved areas.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 11, 457, 456, 307, 572, 2136, 295, 604, 14816, 2280, 281, 605, 382, 257, 4009, 295, 300, 27022, 11, 293, 456, 307, 572, 9922, 305, 295, 26528, 655, 490, 11498, 20772, 3179, 13, 50843], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14611893779826615, "compression_ratio": 1.4864864864864864, "no_speech_prob": 1.950357410296366e-12}, {"id": 774, "seek": 264838, "start": 2658.34, "end": 2661.48, "text": " The certainty just materialized out of thin air in the dark.", "tokens": [50863, 440, 27022, 445, 2527, 1602, 484, 295, 5862, 1988, 294, 264, 2877, 13, 51020], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14611893779826615, "compression_ratio": 1.4864864864864864, "no_speech_prob": 1.950357410296366e-12}, {"id": 775, "seek": 266148, "start": 2661.48, "end": 2664.36, "text": " Which violates that entropy constraint we talked about.", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 3448, 1024, 300, 30867, 25534, 321, 2825, 466, 13, 50509], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1515289306640625, "compression_ratio": 1.6821428571428572, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147401120548578e-12}, {"id": 776, "seek": 266148, "start": 2664.52, "end": 2664.88, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50517, 7587, 13, 50535], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1515289306640625, "compression_ratio": 1.6821428571428572, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147401120548578e-12}, {"id": 777, "seek": 266148, "start": 2665.26, "end": 2667.58, "text": " This violates spatial translation symmetry.", "tokens": [50554, 639, 3448, 1024, 23598, 12853, 25440, 13, 50670], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1515289306640625, "compression_ratio": 1.6821428571428572, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147401120548578e-12}, {"id": 778, "seek": 266148, "start": 2668.26, "end": 2670.9, "text": " Total coherence is a conserved quantity.", "tokens": [50704, 23170, 26528, 655, 307, 257, 1014, 6913, 11275, 13, 50836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1515289306640625, "compression_ratio": 1.6821428571428572, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147401120548578e-12}, {"id": 779, "seek": 266148, "start": 2671.46, "end": 2672.88, "text": " It cannot be created from nothing.", "tokens": [50864, 467, 2644, 312, 2942, 490, 1825, 13, 50935], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1515289306640625, "compression_ratio": 1.6821428571428572, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147401120548578e-12}, {"id": 780, "seek": 266148, "start": 2673.1, "end": 2676.98, "text": " It must flow from somewhere or be generated by an active observation.", "tokens": [50946, 467, 1633, 3095, 490, 4079, 420, 312, 10833, 538, 364, 4967, 14816, 13, 51140], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1515289306640625, "compression_ratio": 1.6821428571428572, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147401120548578e-12}, {"id": 781, "seek": 266148, "start": 2677.32, "end": 2678.76, "text": " It's like accounting for reality.", "tokens": [51157, 467, 311, 411, 19163, 337, 4103, 13, 51229], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1515289306640625, "compression_ratio": 1.6821428571428572, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147401120548578e-12}, {"id": 782, "seek": 266148, "start": 2679.38, "end": 2687.32, "text": " Every single ounce of certainty, every joule of energy, and every strand of causality must perfectly balance the books, or the universe rejects the ledger.", "tokens": [51260, 2048, 2167, 29860, 295, 27022, 11, 633, 11110, 306, 295, 2281, 11, 293, 633, 14955, 295, 3302, 1860, 1633, 6239, 4772, 264, 3642, 11, 420, 264, 6445, 8248, 82, 264, 4684, 1321, 13, 51657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1515289306640625, "compression_ratio": 1.6821428571428572, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147401120548578e-12}, {"id": 783, "seek": 266148, "start": 2687.4, "end": 2688.72, "text": " It is a very strict audit.", "tokens": [51661, 467, 307, 257, 588, 10910, 17748, 13, 51727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1515289306640625, "compression_ratio": 1.6821428571428572, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147401120548578e-12}, {"id": 784, "seek": 268872, "start": 2688.72, "end": 2691.04, "text": " This leads me to a really mind-bending question.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 6689, 385, 281, 257, 534, 1575, 12, 65, 2029, 1168, 13, 50481], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14754487609863282, "compression_ratio": 1.7814814814814814, "no_speech_prob": 1.5193201514593357e-12}, {"id": 785, "seek": 268872, "start": 2691.7799999999997, "end": 2698.14, "text": " If we have all this intense math making these isolated worlds perfect, what happens when you have two perfect worlds?", "tokens": [50518, 759, 321, 362, 439, 341, 9447, 5221, 1455, 613, 14621, 13401, 2176, 11, 437, 2314, 562, 291, 362, 732, 2176, 13401, 30, 50836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14754487609863282, "compression_ratio": 1.7814814814814814, "no_speech_prob": 1.5193201514593357e-12}, {"id": 786, "seek": 268872, "start": 2698.3199999999997, "end": 2699.66, "text": " Ah, cross-world identity.", "tokens": [50845, 2438, 11, 3278, 12, 13217, 6575, 13, 50912], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14754487609863282, "compression_ratio": 1.7814814814814814, "no_speech_prob": 1.5193201514593357e-12}, {"id": 787, "seek": 268872, "start": 2700.02, "end": 2700.24, "text": " All right.", "tokens": [50930, 1057, 558, 13, 50941], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14754487609863282, "compression_ratio": 1.7814814814814814, "no_speech_prob": 1.5193201514593357e-12}, {"id": 788, "seek": 268872, "start": 2700.4599999999996, "end": 2706.72, "text": " Let's say I run a simulation of a courtyard on my local computer, and you run a simulation of a courtyard on your computer.", "tokens": [50952, 961, 311, 584, 286, 1190, 257, 16575, 295, 257, 41364, 322, 452, 2654, 3820, 11, 293, 291, 1190, 257, 16575, 295, 257, 41364, 322, 428, 3820, 13, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14754487609863282, "compression_ratio": 1.7814814814814814, "no_speech_prob": 1.5193201514593357e-12}, {"id": 789, "seek": 268872, "start": 2707.24, "end": 2708.4399999999996, "text": " They both have fountains.", "tokens": [51291, 814, 1293, 362, 283, 792, 2315, 13, 51351], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14754487609863282, "compression_ratio": 1.7814814814814814, "no_speech_prob": 1.5193201514593357e-12}, {"id": 790, "seek": 268872, "start": 2709.0, "end": 2710.0, "text": " Are they the same fountain?", "tokens": [51379, 2014, 436, 264, 912, 29451, 30, 51429], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14754487609863282, "compression_ratio": 1.7814814814814814, "no_speech_prob": 1.5193201514593357e-12}, {"id": 791, "seek": 268872, "start": 2710.48, "end": 2715.16, "text": " To answer our question of cross-world identity, the text turns to category theory.", "tokens": [51453, 1407, 1867, 527, 1168, 295, 3278, 12, 13217, 6575, 11, 264, 2487, 4523, 281, 7719, 5261, 13, 51687], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14754487609863282, "compression_ratio": 1.7814814814814814, "no_speech_prob": 1.5193201514593357e-12}, {"id": 792, "seek": 268872, "start": 2715.48, "end": 2716.2999999999997, "text": " Category theory.", "tokens": [51703, 383, 48701, 5261, 13, 51744], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14754487609863282, "compression_ratio": 1.7814814814814814, "no_speech_prob": 1.5193201514593357e-12}, {"id": 793, "seek": 271630, "start": 2716.3, "end": 2720.94, "text": " In category theory, we abstract away from the raw, specific data.", "tokens": [50365, 682, 7719, 5261, 11, 321, 12649, 1314, 490, 264, 8936, 11, 2685, 1412, 13, 50597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16301062137265748, "compression_ratio": 1.6914285714285715, "no_speech_prob": 1.5791136844314768e-12}, {"id": 794, "seek": 271630, "start": 2721.54, "end": 2728.52, "text": " We don't look at the exact, specific drops of water, or the exact, specific pattern of residue on the stone.", "tokens": [50627, 492, 500, 380, 574, 412, 264, 1900, 11, 2685, 11438, 295, 1281, 11, 420, 264, 1900, 11, 2685, 5102, 295, 34799, 322, 264, 7581, 13, 50976], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16301062137265748, "compression_ratio": 1.6914285714285715, "no_speech_prob": 1.5791136844314768e-12}, {"id": 795, "seek": 271630, "start": 2728.6600000000003, "end": 2729.5600000000004, "text": " We ignore the details.", "tokens": [50983, 492, 11200, 264, 4365, 13, 51028], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16301062137265748, "compression_ratio": 1.6914285714285715, "no_speech_prob": 1.5791136844314768e-12}, {"id": 796, "seek": 271630, "start": 2730.0, "end": 2731.3, "text": " We look at the architectural relationships.", "tokens": [51050, 492, 574, 412, 264, 26621, 6159, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16301062137265748, "compression_ratio": 1.6914285714285715, "no_speech_prob": 1.5791136844314768e-12}, {"id": 797, "seek": 271630, "start": 2732.1600000000003, "end": 2734.6200000000003, "text": " We look for structure-preserving morphisms.", "tokens": [51158, 492, 574, 337, 3877, 12, 14508, 20186, 25778, 13539, 13, 51281], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16301062137265748, "compression_ratio": 1.6914285714285715, "no_speech_prob": 1.5791136844314768e-12}, {"id": 798, "seek": 271630, "start": 2735.2000000000003, "end": 2735.7200000000003, "text": " Morphisms.", "tokens": [51310, 5146, 950, 13539, 13, 51336], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16301062137265748, "compression_ratio": 1.6914285714285715, "no_speech_prob": 1.5791136844314768e-12}, {"id": 799, "seek": 273572, "start": 2735.72, "end": 2750.72, "text": " If we map the mathematical trajectories of your fountain and the trajectories of my fountain, and we find that they share the exact same structural dynamics, the same fast and slow clocks, the same Hamiltonian oscillations, they're declared isomorphic.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 321, 4471, 264, 18894, 18257, 2083, 295, 428, 29451, 293, 264, 18257, 2083, 295, 452, 29451, 11, 293, 321, 915, 300, 436, 2073, 264, 1900, 912, 15067, 15679, 11, 264, 912, 2370, 293, 2964, 41528, 11, 264, 912, 18484, 952, 18225, 763, 11, 436, 434, 15489, 307, 32702, 299, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09406182549216531, "compression_ratio": 1.6153846153846154, "no_speech_prob": 1.4050162942813582e-12}, {"id": 800, "seek": 275072, "start": 2750.72, "end": 2758.18, "text": " So they are mathematically the same kind of thing, even if they have completely different specific histories and exist on different hard drives.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 436, 366, 44003, 264, 912, 733, 295, 551, 11, 754, 498, 436, 362, 2584, 819, 2685, 30631, 293, 2514, 322, 819, 1152, 11754, 13, 50738], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16713960291975635, "compression_ratio": 1.733788395904437, "no_speech_prob": 2.0519215666869872e-12}, {"id": 801, "seek": 275072, "start": 2758.2599999999998, "end": 2758.7, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50742, 7587, 13, 50764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16713960291975635, "compression_ratio": 1.733788395904437, "no_speech_prob": 2.0519215666869872e-12}, {"id": 802, "seek": 275072, "start": 2758.8199999999997, "end": 2762.7799999999997, "text": " It's like having two copies of the same architectural blueprint that were built into two different houses.", "tokens": [50770, 467, 311, 411, 1419, 732, 14341, 295, 264, 912, 26621, 35868, 300, 645, 3094, 666, 732, 819, 8078, 13, 50968], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16713960291975635, "compression_ratio": 1.733788395904437, "no_speech_prob": 2.0519215666869872e-12}, {"id": 803, "seek": 275072, "start": 2763.2599999999998, "end": 2764.52, "text": " Exactly that concept.", "tokens": [50992, 7587, 300, 3410, 13, 51055], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16713960291975635, "compression_ratio": 1.733788395904437, "no_speech_prob": 2.0519215666869872e-12}, {"id": 804, "seek": 275072, "start": 2764.7, "end": 2765.9399999999996, "text": " But what if they aren't identical?", "tokens": [51064, 583, 437, 498, 436, 3212, 380, 14800, 30, 51126], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16713960291975635, "compression_ratio": 1.733788395904437, "no_speech_prob": 2.0519215666869872e-12}, {"id": 805, "seek": 275072, "start": 2766.3599999999997, "end": 2771.1, "text": " What if your fountain has slightly thicker water or is slightly more damp than mine?", "tokens": [51147, 708, 498, 428, 29451, 575, 4748, 18142, 1281, 420, 307, 4748, 544, 19498, 813, 3892, 30, 51384], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16713960291975635, "compression_ratio": 1.733788395904437, "no_speech_prob": 2.0519215666869872e-12}, {"id": 806, "seek": 275072, "start": 2771.3399999999997, "end": 2771.56, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51396, 865, 13, 51407], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16713960291975635, "compression_ratio": 1.733788395904437, "no_speech_prob": 2.0519215666869872e-12}, {"id": 807, "seek": 275072, "start": 2771.8799999999997, "end": 2772.3599999999997, "text": " What then?", "tokens": [51423, 708, 550, 30, 51447], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16713960291975635, "compression_ratio": 1.733788395904437, "no_speech_prob": 2.0519215666869872e-12}, {"id": 808, "seek": 275072, "start": 2772.4599999999996, "end": 2774.2999999999997, "text": " They aren't perfectly isomorphic.", "tokens": [51452, 814, 3212, 380, 6239, 307, 32702, 299, 13, 51544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16713960291975635, "compression_ratio": 1.733788395904437, "no_speech_prob": 2.0519215666869872e-12}, {"id": 809, "seek": 275072, "start": 2774.4399999999996, "end": 2777.4599999999996, "text": " Does that mean they are completely unrelated entities?", "tokens": [51551, 4402, 300, 914, 436, 366, 2584, 38967, 16667, 30, 51702], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16713960291975635, "compression_ratio": 1.733788395904437, "no_speech_prob": 2.0519215666869872e-12}, {"id": 810, "seek": 277746, "start": 2777.46, "end": 2780.7, "text": " I mean, logically, they are still both fountains.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 914, 11, 38887, 11, 436, 366, 920, 1293, 283, 792, 2315, 13, 50527], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14054892493076013, "compression_ratio": 1.797979797979798, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007657218334749e-12}, {"id": 811, "seek": 277746, "start": 2780.78, "end": 2783.08, "text": " They should be related to each other on some spectrum.", "tokens": [50531, 814, 820, 312, 4077, 281, 1184, 661, 322, 512, 11143, 13, 50646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14054892493076013, "compression_ratio": 1.797979797979798, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007657218334749e-12}, {"id": 812, "seek": 277746, "start": 2783.16, "end": 2786.82, "text": " And they are through the framework of information geometry.", "tokens": [50650, 400, 436, 366, 807, 264, 8388, 295, 1589, 18426, 13, 50833], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14054892493076013, "compression_ratio": 1.797979797979798, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007657218334749e-12}, {"id": 813, "seek": 277746, "start": 2787.02, "end": 2787.94, "text": " Information geometry.", "tokens": [50843, 15357, 18426, 13, 50889], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14054892493076013, "compression_ratio": 1.797979797979798, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007657218334749e-12}, {"id": 814, "seek": 277746, "start": 2788.08, "end": 2794.4, "text": " We cannot compare their raw spatial coordinates directly because they exist in entirely different simulated domains.", "tokens": [50896, 492, 2644, 6794, 641, 8936, 23598, 21056, 3838, 570, 436, 2514, 294, 7696, 819, 41713, 25514, 13, 51212], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14054892493076013, "compression_ratio": 1.797979797979798, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007657218334749e-12}, {"id": 815, "seek": 277746, "start": 2794.52, "end": 2795.62, "text": " There is no shared map.", "tokens": [51218, 821, 307, 572, 5507, 4471, 13, 51273], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14054892493076013, "compression_ratio": 1.797979797979798, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007657218334749e-12}, {"id": 816, "seek": 277746, "start": 2795.8, "end": 2796.0, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51282, 1779, 13, 51292], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14054892493076013, "compression_ratio": 1.797979797979798, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007657218334749e-12}, {"id": 817, "seek": 277746, "start": 2796.08, "end": 2798.44, "text": " My computer doesn't know about your computer's coordinates.", "tokens": [51296, 1222, 3820, 1177, 380, 458, 466, 428, 3820, 311, 21056, 13, 51414], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14054892493076013, "compression_ratio": 1.797979797979798, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007657218334749e-12}, {"id": 818, "seek": 277746, "start": 2798.88, "end": 2802.96, "text": " Instead, information geometry allows us to compare their belief states.", "tokens": [51436, 7156, 11, 1589, 18426, 4045, 505, 281, 6794, 641, 7107, 4368, 13, 51640], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14054892493076013, "compression_ratio": 1.797979797979798, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007657218334749e-12}, {"id": 819, "seek": 277746, "start": 2803.14, "end": 2803.96, "text": " Belief states.", "tokens": [51649, 6248, 2521, 4368, 13, 51690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14054892493076013, "compression_ratio": 1.797979797979798, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007657218334749e-12}, {"id": 820, "seek": 277746, "start": 2803.96, "end": 2807.2, "text": " We look at the entropy distributions of both worlds.", "tokens": [51690, 492, 574, 412, 264, 30867, 37870, 295, 1293, 13401, 13, 51852], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14054892493076013, "compression_ratio": 1.797979797979798, "no_speech_prob": 1.7007657218334749e-12}, {"id": 821, "seek": 280746, "start": 2807.46, "end": 2813.92, "text": " What each individual world mathematically believes about its own live possibilities and uncertainties.", "tokens": [50365, 708, 1184, 2609, 1002, 44003, 12307, 466, 1080, 1065, 1621, 12178, 293, 11308, 6097, 13, 50688], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1491062286052298, "compression_ratio": 1.7518248175182483, "no_speech_prob": 2.514056888017202e-12}, {"id": 822, "seek": 280746, "start": 2814.08, "end": 2819.56, "text": " And we measure the informational distance between those probabilistic beliefs across time.", "tokens": [50696, 400, 321, 3481, 264, 49391, 4560, 1296, 729, 31959, 3142, 13585, 2108, 565, 13, 50970], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1491062286052298, "compression_ratio": 1.7518248175182483, "no_speech_prob": 2.514056888017202e-12}, {"id": 823, "seek": 280746, "start": 2819.56, "end": 2828.42, "text": " So we are essentially measuring how hard it would be to mathematically translate the physics of my fountain until it believes it is actually your fountain.", "tokens": [50970, 407, 321, 366, 4476, 13389, 577, 1152, 309, 576, 312, 281, 44003, 13799, 264, 10649, 295, 452, 29451, 1826, 309, 12307, 309, 307, 767, 428, 29451, 13, 51413], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1491062286052298, "compression_ratio": 1.7518248175182483, "no_speech_prob": 2.514056888017202e-12}, {"id": 824, "seek": 280746, "start": 2828.76, "end": 2829.62, "text": " That is unbelievable.", "tokens": [51430, 663, 307, 16605, 13, 51473], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1491062286052298, "compression_ratio": 1.7518248175182483, "no_speech_prob": 2.514056888017202e-12}, {"id": 825, "seek": 280746, "start": 2829.9, "end": 2833.4, "text": " We have essentially built a theoretical universe that is watertight.", "tokens": [51487, 492, 362, 4476, 3094, 257, 20864, 6445, 300, 307, 1281, 41738, 13, 51662], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1491062286052298, "compression_ratio": 1.7518248175182483, "no_speech_prob": 2.514056888017202e-12}, {"id": 826, "seek": 280746, "start": 2833.88, "end": 2836.2, "text": " But theoretical math is great on paper.", "tokens": [51686, 583, 20864, 5221, 307, 869, 322, 3035, 13, 51802], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1491062286052298, "compression_ratio": 1.7518248175182483, "no_speech_prob": 2.514056888017202e-12}, {"id": 827, "seek": 283620, "start": 2836.2, "end": 2840.96, "text": " To actually make this run on a computer in 2026, we have to engineer it.", "tokens": [50365, 1407, 767, 652, 341, 1190, 322, 257, 3820, 294, 945, 10880, 11, 321, 362, 281, 11403, 309, 13, 50603], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15742360713870027, "compression_ratio": 1.536697247706422, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622784741905262e-12}, {"id": 828, "seek": 283620, "start": 2841.04, "end": 2842.12, "text": " We have to build a database.", "tokens": [50607, 492, 362, 281, 1322, 257, 8149, 13, 50661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15742360713870027, "compression_ratio": 1.536697247706422, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622784741905262e-12}, {"id": 829, "seek": 283620, "start": 2842.3199999999997, "end": 2842.52, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50671, 1779, 13, 50681], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15742360713870027, "compression_ratio": 1.536697247706422, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622784741905262e-12}, {"id": 830, "seek": 283620, "start": 2842.98, "end": 2848.46, "text": " How do you physically build a database that can hold an infinite, continuous semantic field?", "tokens": [50704, 1012, 360, 291, 9762, 1322, 257, 8149, 300, 393, 1797, 364, 13785, 11, 10957, 47982, 2519, 30, 50978], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15742360713870027, "compression_ratio": 1.536697247706422, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622784741905262e-12}, {"id": 831, "seek": 283620, "start": 2849.24, "end": 2855.06, "text": " You cannot literally store data for every microscopic fraction of an inch of infinity.", "tokens": [51017, 509, 2644, 3736, 3531, 1412, 337, 633, 47897, 14135, 295, 364, 7227, 295, 13202, 13, 51308], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15742360713870027, "compression_ratio": 1.536697247706422, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622784741905262e-12}, {"id": 832, "seek": 283620, "start": 2855.2599999999998, "end": 2856.52, "text": " The hard drive just doesn't exist.", "tokens": [51318, 440, 1152, 3332, 445, 1177, 380, 2514, 13, 51381], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15742360713870027, "compression_ratio": 1.536697247706422, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622784741905262e-12}, {"id": 833, "seek": 283620, "start": 2856.66, "end": 2857.16, "text": " You cannot.", "tokens": [51388, 509, 2644, 13, 51413], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15742360713870027, "compression_ratio": 1.536697247706422, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622784741905262e-12}, {"id": 834, "seek": 285716, "start": 2857.16, "end": 2863.54, "text": " A naive array that tried to store a continuous field would explode the capacity of any hard drive instantly.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 29052, 10225, 300, 3031, 281, 3531, 257, 10957, 2519, 576, 21411, 264, 6042, 295, 604, 1152, 3332, 13518, 13, 50684], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17964188754558563, "compression_ratio": 1.2, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191843009271233e-12}, {"id": 835, "seek": 285716, "start": 2863.7799999999997, "end": 2864.54, "text": " So what's the solution?", "tokens": [50696, 407, 437, 311, 264, 3827, 30, 50734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17964188754558563, "compression_ratio": 1.2, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191843009271233e-12}, {"id": 836, "seek": 286454, "start": 2864.54, "end": 2869.58, "text": " So the engineers must design the world database to be sparse by construction.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 264, 11955, 1633, 1715, 264, 1002, 8149, 281, 312, 637, 11668, 538, 6435, 13, 50617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17265249036022068, "compression_ratio": 1.6040816326530611, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482844599098213e-12}, {"id": 837, "seek": 286454, "start": 2869.58, "end": 2870.24, "text": " It's sparse.", "tokens": [50617, 467, 311, 637, 11668, 13, 50650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17265249036022068, "compression_ratio": 1.6040816326530611, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482844599098213e-12}, {"id": 838, "seek": 286454, "start": 2870.24, "end": 2875.96, "text": " They use hierarchical data structures like off-trees, which divide space into progressively smaller cubes.", "tokens": [50650, 814, 764, 35250, 804, 1412, 9227, 411, 766, 12, 3599, 279, 11, 597, 9845, 1901, 666, 46667, 4356, 25415, 13, 50936], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17265249036022068, "compression_ratio": 1.6040816326530611, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482844599098213e-12}, {"id": 839, "seek": 286454, "start": 2876.3, "end": 2879.3, "text": " But the key to making it sparse goes back to the entropy constraint.", "tokens": [50953, 583, 264, 2141, 281, 1455, 309, 637, 11668, 1709, 646, 281, 264, 30867, 25534, 13, 51103], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17265249036022068, "compression_ratio": 1.6040816326530611, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482844599098213e-12}, {"id": 840, "seek": 286454, "start": 2879.7799999999997, "end": 2881.84, "text": " Do you recall the rule about unobserved areas?", "tokens": [51127, 1144, 291, 9901, 264, 4978, 466, 8526, 929, 6913, 3179, 30, 51230], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17265249036022068, "compression_ratio": 1.6040816326530611, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482844599098213e-12}, {"id": 841, "seek": 286454, "start": 2882.08, "end": 2884.42, "text": " Entropy cannot decrease unless it is observed.", "tokens": [51242, 3951, 27514, 2644, 11514, 5969, 309, 307, 13095, 13, 51359], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17265249036022068, "compression_ratio": 1.6040816326530611, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482844599098213e-12}, {"id": 842, "seek": 286454, "start": 2884.84, "end": 2886.48, "text": " The dark corners stay uncertain.", "tokens": [51380, 440, 2877, 12413, 1754, 11308, 13, 51462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17265249036022068, "compression_ratio": 1.6040816326530611, "no_speech_prob": 1.7482844599098213e-12}, {"id": 843, "seek": 288648, "start": 2886.48, "end": 2891.34, "text": " Which means the vast majority of the simulated universe is sitting in a state of high entropy.", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 1355, 264, 8369, 6286, 295, 264, 41713, 6445, 307, 3798, 294, 257, 1785, 295, 1090, 30867, 13, 50608], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15701703523334704, "compression_ratio": 1.579925650557621, "no_speech_prob": 1.890348337932335e-12}, {"id": 844, "seek": 288648, "start": 2892.0, "end": 2895.44, "text": " It is unobserved, generic, unresolved possibility.", "tokens": [50641, 467, 307, 8526, 929, 6913, 11, 19577, 11, 517, 495, 29110, 7959, 13, 50813], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15701703523334704, "compression_ratio": 1.579925650557621, "no_speech_prob": 1.890348337932335e-12}, {"id": 845, "seek": 288648, "start": 2895.8, "end": 2898.22, "text": " And here is the brilliant engineering trick.", "tokens": [50831, 400, 510, 307, 264, 10248, 7043, 4282, 13, 50952], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15701703523334704, "compression_ratio": 1.579925650557621, "no_speech_prob": 1.890348337932335e-12}, {"id": 846, "seek": 288648, "start": 2899.14, "end": 2903.06, "text": " High uncertainty equals low computational storage cost.", "tokens": [50998, 5229, 15697, 6915, 2295, 28270, 6725, 2063, 13, 51194], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15701703523334704, "compression_ratio": 1.579925650557621, "no_speech_prob": 1.890348337932335e-12}, {"id": 847, "seek": 288648, "start": 2903.2400000000002, "end": 2903.36, "text": " Oh.", "tokens": [51203, 876, 13, 51209], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15701703523334704, "compression_ratio": 1.579925650557621, "no_speech_prob": 1.890348337932335e-12}, {"id": 848, "seek": 288648, "start": 2903.78, "end": 2909.34, "text": " The system only allocates dense, heavy memory blocks to regions where entropy has actively decreased,", "tokens": [51230, 440, 1185, 787, 12660, 1024, 18011, 11, 4676, 4675, 8474, 281, 10682, 689, 30867, 575, 13022, 24436, 11, 51508], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15701703523334704, "compression_ratio": 1.579925650557621, "no_speech_prob": 1.890348337932335e-12}, {"id": 849, "seek": 288648, "start": 2909.48, "end": 2913.22, "text": " where observation has forced the world to resolve into specific details.", "tokens": [51515, 689, 14816, 575, 7579, 264, 1002, 281, 14151, 666, 2685, 4365, 13, 51702], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15701703523334704, "compression_ratio": 1.579925650557621, "no_speech_prob": 1.890348337932335e-12}, {"id": 850, "seek": 291322, "start": 2913.22, "end": 2913.7, "text": " No.", "tokens": [50365, 883, 13, 50389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16661924304384174, "compression_ratio": 1.652733118971061, "no_speech_prob": 2.219202903039341e-12}, {"id": 851, "seek": 291322, "start": 2914.48, "end": 2919.54, "text": " So that unobserved, foggy corner of the courtyard costs almost zero bytes to store.", "tokens": [50428, 407, 300, 8526, 929, 6913, 11, 13648, 1480, 4538, 295, 264, 41364, 5497, 1920, 4018, 36088, 281, 3531, 13, 50681], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16661924304384174, "compression_ratio": 1.652733118971061, "no_speech_prob": 2.219202903039341e-12}, {"id": 852, "seek": 291322, "start": 2919.7599999999998, "end": 2920.4599999999996, "text": " Almost zero?", "tokens": [50692, 12627, 4018, 30, 50727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16661924304384174, "compression_ratio": 1.652733118971061, "no_speech_prob": 2.219202903039341e-12}, {"id": 853, "seek": 291322, "start": 2920.72, "end": 2921.8599999999997, "text": " That is so elegant.", "tokens": [50740, 663, 307, 370, 21117, 13, 50797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16661924304384174, "compression_ratio": 1.652733118971061, "no_speech_prob": 2.219202903039341e-12}, {"id": 854, "seek": 291322, "start": 2922.24, "end": 2924.66, "text": " Ignorance is literally computationally cheap.", "tokens": [50816, 24754, 284, 719, 307, 3736, 24903, 379, 7084, 13, 50937], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16661924304384174, "compression_ratio": 1.652733118971061, "no_speech_prob": 2.219202903039341e-12}, {"id": 855, "seek": 291322, "start": 2925.24, "end": 2926.62, "text": " But that solves the size problem.", "tokens": [50966, 583, 300, 39890, 264, 2744, 1154, 13, 51035], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16661924304384174, "compression_ratio": 1.652733118971061, "no_speech_prob": 2.219202903039341e-12}, {"id": 856, "seek": 291322, "start": 2926.8999999999996, "end": 2928.2, "text": " What about the access speed problem?", "tokens": [51049, 708, 466, 264, 2105, 3073, 1154, 30, 51114], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16661924304384174, "compression_ratio": 1.652733118971061, "no_speech_prob": 2.219202903039341e-12}, {"id": 857, "seek": 291322, "start": 2928.24, "end": 2929.08, "text": " Right, finding the data.", "tokens": [51116, 1779, 11, 5006, 264, 1412, 13, 51158], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16661924304384174, "compression_ratio": 1.652733118971061, "no_speech_prob": 2.219202903039341e-12}, {"id": 858, "seek": 291322, "start": 2929.22, "end": 2930.98, "text": " If the virtual world is three-dimensional,", "tokens": [51165, 759, 264, 6374, 1002, 307, 1045, 12, 18759, 11, 51253], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16661924304384174, "compression_ratio": 1.652733118971061, "no_speech_prob": 2.219202903039341e-12}, {"id": 859, "seek": 291322, "start": 2931.4599999999996, "end": 2935.9599999999996, "text": " but my physical hard drive is essentially a one-dimensional linear string of memory addresses,", "tokens": [51277, 457, 452, 4001, 1152, 3332, 307, 4476, 257, 472, 12, 18759, 8213, 6798, 295, 4675, 16862, 11, 51502], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16661924304384174, "compression_ratio": 1.652733118971061, "no_speech_prob": 2.219202903039341e-12}, {"id": 860, "seek": 291322, "start": 2936.4199999999996, "end": 2939.9199999999996, "text": " how does the computer load a complex 3D courtyard quickly", "tokens": [51525, 577, 775, 264, 3820, 3677, 257, 3997, 805, 35, 41364, 2661, 51700], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16661924304384174, "compression_ratio": 1.652733118971061, "no_speech_prob": 2.219202903039341e-12}, {"id": 861, "seek": 291322, "start": 2939.9199999999996, "end": 2942.8199999999997, "text": " without the read head jumping wildly all over the disk?", "tokens": [51700, 1553, 264, 1401, 1378, 11233, 34731, 439, 670, 264, 12355, 30, 51845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16661924304384174, "compression_ratio": 1.652733118971061, "no_speech_prob": 2.219202903039341e-12}, {"id": 862, "seek": 294282, "start": 2942.82, "end": 2946.82, "text": " The text uses a beautiful linguistic analogy here to explain the solution.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2487, 4960, 257, 2238, 43002, 21663, 510, 281, 2903, 264, 3827, 13, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1770882288614909, "compression_ratio": 1.7118055555555556, "no_speech_prob": 2.2986011965347997e-12}, {"id": 863, "seek": 294282, "start": 2947.0, "end": 2952.02, "text": " It compares the mapping of computer memory to the historical ordering of the Arabic script.", "tokens": [50574, 467, 38334, 264, 18350, 295, 3820, 4675, 281, 264, 8584, 21739, 295, 264, 19938, 5755, 13, 50825], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1770882288614909, "compression_ratio": 1.7118055555555556, "no_speech_prob": 2.2986011965347997e-12}, {"id": 864, "seek": 294282, "start": 2952.1400000000003, "end": 2954.06, "text": " Oh, to explain space-soling curves, right.", "tokens": [50831, 876, 11, 281, 2903, 1901, 12, 30926, 278, 19490, 11, 558, 13, 50927], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1770882288614909, "compression_ratio": 1.7118055555555556, "no_speech_prob": 2.2986011965347997e-12}, {"id": 865, "seek": 294282, "start": 2954.1400000000003, "end": 2954.28, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50931, 1079, 13, 50938], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1770882288614909, "compression_ratio": 1.7118055555555556, "no_speech_prob": 2.2986011965347997e-12}, {"id": 866, "seek": 294282, "start": 2954.34, "end": 2955.48, "text": " Specifically Hilbert curves.", "tokens": [50941, 26058, 19914, 4290, 19490, 13, 50998], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1770882288614909, "compression_ratio": 1.7118055555555556, "no_speech_prob": 2.2986011965347997e-12}, {"id": 867, "seek": 294282, "start": 2955.6800000000003, "end": 2955.94, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51008, 1079, 13, 51021], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1770882288614909, "compression_ratio": 1.7118055555555556, "no_speech_prob": 2.2986011965347997e-12}, {"id": 868, "seek": 294282, "start": 2956.04, "end": 2958.5, "text": " I really need you to unpack the Arabic script analogy.", "tokens": [51026, 286, 534, 643, 291, 281, 26699, 264, 19938, 5755, 21663, 13, 51149], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1770882288614909, "compression_ratio": 1.7118055555555556, "no_speech_prob": 2.2986011965347997e-12}, {"id": 869, "seek": 294282, "start": 2959.1400000000003, "end": 2962.1000000000004, "text": " What does linguistics have to do with hard drive seek times?", "tokens": [51181, 708, 775, 21766, 6006, 362, 281, 360, 365, 1152, 3332, 8075, 1413, 30, 51329], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1770882288614909, "compression_ratio": 1.7118055555555556, "no_speech_prob": 2.2986011965347997e-12}, {"id": 870, "seek": 294282, "start": 2962.52, "end": 2965.2200000000003, "text": " The Arabic alphabet consists of 28 letters.", "tokens": [51350, 440, 19938, 23339, 14689, 295, 7562, 7825, 13, 51485], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1770882288614909, "compression_ratio": 1.7118055555555556, "no_speech_prob": 2.2986011965347997e-12}, {"id": 871, "seek": 294282, "start": 2966.04, "end": 2970.42, "text": " Historically, there are two completely distinct ways to order those same 28 letters.", "tokens": [51526, 25108, 984, 11, 456, 366, 732, 2584, 10644, 2098, 281, 1668, 729, 912, 7562, 7825, 13, 51745], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1770882288614909, "compression_ratio": 1.7118055555555556, "no_speech_prob": 2.2986011965347997e-12}, {"id": 872, "seek": 297042, "start": 2970.42, "end": 2973.4, "text": " The ancient sequence is called the Abjad order.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 7832, 8310, 307, 1219, 264, 2847, 73, 345, 1668, 13, 50514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21750663090678093, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 3.658309766230161e-12}, {"id": 873, "seek": 297042, "start": 2973.92, "end": 2979.4, "text": " The Abjad sequence is based on historical inheritance from earlier alphabets and numerical values.", "tokens": [50540, 440, 2847, 73, 345, 8310, 307, 2361, 322, 8584, 32122, 490, 3071, 419, 950, 455, 1385, 293, 29054, 4190, 13, 50814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21750663090678093, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 3.658309766230161e-12}, {"id": 874, "seek": 297042, "start": 2979.92, "end": 2981.98, "text": " It is useful for mathematics and history.", "tokens": [50840, 467, 307, 4420, 337, 18666, 293, 2503, 13, 50943], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21750663090678093, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 3.658309766230161e-12}, {"id": 875, "seek": 297042, "start": 2982.28, "end": 2982.52, "text": " Got it.", "tokens": [50958, 5803, 309, 13, 50970], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21750663090678093, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 3.658309766230161e-12}, {"id": 876, "seek": 297042, "start": 2982.78, "end": 2985.66, "text": " But later on, scholars developed the Hujjah sequence.", "tokens": [50983, 583, 1780, 322, 11, 8553, 4743, 264, 389, 4579, 73, 545, 8310, 13, 51127], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21750663090678093, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 3.658309766230161e-12}, {"id": 877, "seek": 297042, "start": 2986.06, "end": 2989.3, "text": " The Hujjah sequence regroups the exact same 28 letters,", "tokens": [51147, 440, 389, 4579, 73, 545, 8310, 319, 17377, 82, 264, 1900, 912, 7562, 7825, 11, 51309], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21750663090678093, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 3.658309766230161e-12}, {"id": 878, "seek": 297042, "start": 2989.52, "end": 2992.96, "text": " but it orders them purely by their visual, physical shape.", "tokens": [51320, 457, 309, 9470, 552, 17491, 538, 641, 5056, 11, 4001, 3909, 13, 51492], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21750663090678093, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 3.658309766230161e-12}, {"id": 879, "seek": 297042, "start": 2993.06, "end": 2993.44, "text": " By shape.", "tokens": [51497, 3146, 3909, 13, 51516], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21750663090678093, "compression_ratio": 1.6304347826086956, "no_speech_prob": 3.658309766230161e-12}, {"id": 880, "seek": 299344, "start": 2993.44, "end": 2993.8, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50383], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20390301440135541, "compression_ratio": 1.5416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.176095241501752e-12}, {"id": 881, "seek": 299344, "start": 2994.26, "end": 2996.5, "text": " Letters that look similar are placed next to each other.", "tokens": [50406, 961, 1559, 300, 574, 2531, 366, 7074, 958, 281, 1184, 661, 13, 50518], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20390301440135541, "compression_ratio": 1.5416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.176095241501752e-12}, {"id": 882, "seek": 299344, "start": 2997.14, "end": 3000.28, "text": " This was done to make it vastly easier to teach handwriting", "tokens": [50550, 639, 390, 1096, 281, 652, 309, 41426, 3571, 281, 2924, 39179, 50707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20390301440135541, "compression_ratio": 1.5416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.176095241501752e-12}, {"id": 883, "seek": 299344, "start": 3000.28, "end": 3003.5, "text": " and to look things up in a dictionary based on visual form.", "tokens": [50707, 293, 281, 574, 721, 493, 294, 257, 25890, 2361, 322, 5056, 1254, 13, 50868], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20390301440135541, "compression_ratio": 1.5416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.176095241501752e-12}, {"id": 884, "seek": 299344, "start": 3003.6, "end": 3004.2000000000003, "text": " Same data.", "tokens": [50873, 10635, 1412, 13, 50903], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20390301440135541, "compression_ratio": 1.5416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.176095241501752e-12}, {"id": 885, "seek": 299344, "start": 3004.48, "end": 3007.38, "text": " Completely different order for a completely different functional purpose.", "tokens": [50917, 39978, 819, 1668, 337, 257, 2584, 819, 11745, 4334, 13, 51062], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20390301440135541, "compression_ratio": 1.5416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.176095241501752e-12}, {"id": 886, "seek": 299344, "start": 3007.52, "end": 3008.0, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51069, 7587, 13, 51093], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20390301440135541, "compression_ratio": 1.5416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.176095241501752e-12}, {"id": 887, "seek": 299344, "start": 3008.42, "end": 3012.06, "text": " The 3D simulated world has its own natural spatial order,", "tokens": [51114, 440, 805, 35, 41713, 1002, 575, 1080, 1065, 3303, 23598, 1668, 11, 51296], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20390301440135541, "compression_ratio": 1.5416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.176095241501752e-12}, {"id": 888, "seek": 301206, "start": 3012.06, "end": 3017.86, "text": " but to store that 3D space on a 1D linear hard drive for incredibly fast access,", "tokens": [50365, 457, 281, 3531, 300, 805, 35, 1901, 322, 257, 502, 35, 8213, 1152, 3332, 337, 6252, 2370, 2105, 11, 50655], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13088143723351614, "compression_ratio": 1.6159695817490494, "no_speech_prob": 1.832192383921516e-12}, {"id": 889, "seek": 301206, "start": 3018.1, "end": 3020.2, "text": " you need a different purpose-built order.", "tokens": [50667, 291, 643, 257, 819, 4334, 12, 23018, 1668, 13, 50772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13088143723351614, "compression_ratio": 1.6159695817490494, "no_speech_prob": 1.832192383921516e-12}, {"id": 890, "seek": 301206, "start": 3020.4, "end": 3023.44, "text": " Okay, so what's the equivalent of the Hujjah sequence for a hard drive?", "tokens": [50782, 1033, 11, 370, 437, 311, 264, 10344, 295, 264, 389, 4579, 73, 545, 8310, 337, 257, 1152, 3332, 30, 50934], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13088143723351614, "compression_ratio": 1.6159695817490494, "no_speech_prob": 1.832192383921516e-12}, {"id": 891, "seek": 301206, "start": 3023.66, "end": 3029.08, "text": " The database uses a mathematical path called a Hilbert curve to linearize the 3D domain.", "tokens": [50945, 440, 8149, 4960, 257, 18894, 3100, 1219, 257, 19914, 4290, 7605, 281, 8213, 1125, 264, 805, 35, 9274, 13, 51216], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13088143723351614, "compression_ratio": 1.6159695817490494, "no_speech_prob": 1.832192383921516e-12}, {"id": 892, "seek": 301206, "start": 3029.2, "end": 3029.92, "text": " A Hilbert curve.", "tokens": [51222, 316, 19914, 4290, 7605, 13, 51258], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13088143723351614, "compression_ratio": 1.6159695817490494, "no_speech_prob": 1.832192383921516e-12}, {"id": 893, "seek": 301206, "start": 3030.06, "end": 3033.58, "text": " A Hilbert curve winds and folds through the 3D space", "tokens": [51265, 316, 19914, 4290, 7605, 17765, 293, 31341, 807, 264, 805, 35, 1901, 51441], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13088143723351614, "compression_ratio": 1.6159695817490494, "no_speech_prob": 1.832192383921516e-12}, {"id": 894, "seek": 301206, "start": 3033.58, "end": 3038.2799999999997, "text": " in a highly specific fractal pattern that guarantees one crucial thing.", "tokens": [51441, 294, 257, 5405, 2685, 17948, 304, 5102, 300, 32567, 472, 11462, 551, 13, 51676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13088143723351614, "compression_ratio": 1.6159695817490494, "no_speech_prob": 1.832192383921516e-12}, {"id": 895, "seek": 303828, "start": 3038.28, "end": 3041.6600000000003, "text": " Points that are physically close to each other in the 3D courtyard", "tokens": [50365, 44763, 300, 366, 9762, 1998, 281, 1184, 661, 294, 264, 805, 35, 41364, 50534], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1505080375118532, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 2.21036643849315e-12}, {"id": 896, "seek": 303828, "start": 3041.6600000000003, "end": 3045.36, "text": " are placed right next to each other on the 1D line of the hard drive.", "tokens": [50534, 366, 7074, 558, 958, 281, 1184, 661, 322, 264, 502, 35, 1622, 295, 264, 1152, 3332, 13, 50719], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1505080375118532, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 2.21036643849315e-12}, {"id": 897, "seek": 303828, "start": 3045.6200000000003, "end": 3046.34, "text": " Oh, that's brilliant.", "tokens": [50732, 876, 11, 300, 311, 10248, 13, 50768], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1505080375118532, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 2.21036643849315e-12}, {"id": 898, "seek": 303828, "start": 3046.6600000000003, "end": 3048.52, "text": " So when my character walks into the courtyard,", "tokens": [50784, 407, 562, 452, 2517, 12896, 666, 264, 41364, 11, 50877], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1505080375118532, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 2.21036643849315e-12}, {"id": 899, "seek": 303828, "start": 3049.2200000000003, "end": 3053.0800000000004, "text": " the computer doesn't have to hunt for a million tiny fragmented files", "tokens": [50912, 264, 3820, 1177, 380, 362, 281, 12454, 337, 257, 2459, 5870, 9241, 14684, 7098, 51105], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1505080375118532, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 2.21036643849315e-12}, {"id": 900, "seek": 303828, "start": 3053.0800000000004, "end": 3054.36, "text": " scattered across the disk.", "tokens": [51105, 21986, 2108, 264, 12355, 13, 51169], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1505080375118532, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 2.21036643849315e-12}, {"id": 901, "seek": 303828, "start": 3054.44, "end": 3058.02, "text": " No, it just reads one continuous solid chunk of the hard drive.", "tokens": [51173, 883, 11, 309, 445, 15700, 472, 10957, 5100, 16635, 295, 264, 1152, 3332, 13, 51352], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1505080375118532, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 2.21036643849315e-12}, {"id": 902, "seek": 303828, "start": 3058.26, "end": 3061.34, "text": " The Hilbert curve is the Hujjah sequence for data storage.", "tokens": [51364, 440, 19914, 4290, 7605, 307, 264, 389, 4579, 73, 545, 8310, 337, 1412, 6725, 13, 51518], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1505080375118532, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 2.21036643849315e-12}, {"id": 903, "seek": 303828, "start": 3061.5800000000004, "end": 3064.02, "text": " It organizes the data by spatial proximity.", "tokens": [51530, 467, 4645, 279, 264, 1412, 538, 23598, 27632, 13, 51652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1505080375118532, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 2.21036643849315e-12}, {"id": 904, "seek": 303828, "start": 3064.36, "end": 3064.84, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51669, 7587, 13, 51693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1505080375118532, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 2.21036643849315e-12}, {"id": 905, "seek": 303828, "start": 3064.84, "end": 3067.5800000000004, "text": " Now there's one last engineering choice in the text", "tokens": [51693, 823, 456, 311, 472, 1036, 7043, 3922, 294, 264, 2487, 51830], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1505080375118532, "compression_ratio": 1.6510903426791277, "no_speech_prob": 2.21036643849315e-12}, {"id": 906, "seek": 306758, "start": 3067.58, "end": 3070.16, "text": " that completely broke my brain when I read it.", "tokens": [50365, 300, 2584, 6902, 452, 3567, 562, 286, 1401, 309, 13, 50494], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19605643660933883, "compression_ratio": 1.6701030927835052, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013931496306922e-12}, {"id": 907, "seek": 306758, "start": 3070.4, "end": 3070.7999999999997, "text": " The rendering.", "tokens": [50506, 440, 22407, 13, 50526], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19605643660933883, "compression_ratio": 1.6701030927835052, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013931496306922e-12}, {"id": 908, "seek": 306758, "start": 3071.04, "end": 3071.2799999999997, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50538, 1079, 13, 50550], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19605643660933883, "compression_ratio": 1.6701030927835052, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013931496306922e-12}, {"id": 909, "seek": 306758, "start": 3071.92, "end": 3072.88, "text": " It is about rendering.", "tokens": [50582, 467, 307, 466, 22407, 13, 50630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19605643660933883, "compression_ratio": 1.6701030927835052, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013931496306922e-12}, {"id": 910, "seek": 306758, "start": 3073.38, "end": 3075.2999999999997, "text": " In almost every video game ever made,", "tokens": [50655, 682, 1920, 633, 960, 1216, 1562, 1027, 11, 50751], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19605643660933883, "compression_ratio": 1.6701030927835052, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013931496306922e-12}, {"id": 911, "seek": 306758, "start": 3075.58, "end": 3078.96, "text": " the renderer, the graphics engine, is the core of the system.", "tokens": [50765, 264, 15529, 260, 11, 264, 11837, 2848, 11, 307, 264, 4965, 295, 264, 1185, 13, 50934], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19605643660933883, "compression_ratio": 1.6701030927835052, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013931496306922e-12}, {"id": 912, "seek": 306758, "start": 3079.02, "end": 3080.54, "text": " It's the engine driving everything.", "tokens": [50937, 467, 311, 264, 2848, 4840, 1203, 13, 51013], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19605643660933883, "compression_ratio": 1.6701030927835052, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013931496306922e-12}, {"id": 913, "seek": 306758, "start": 3080.86, "end": 3081.86, "text": " But in this architecture,", "tokens": [51029, 583, 294, 341, 9482, 11, 51079], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19605643660933883, "compression_ratio": 1.6701030927835052, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013931496306922e-12}, {"id": 914, "seek": 306758, "start": 3082.48, "end": 3085.52, "text": " renderers are just dumb clients reading a database.", "tokens": [51110, 15529, 433, 366, 445, 10316, 6982, 3760, 257, 8149, 13, 51262], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19605643660933883, "compression_ratio": 1.6701030927835052, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013931496306922e-12}, {"id": 915, "seek": 306758, "start": 3086.12, "end": 3088.54, "text": " And there's a massive twist to how they operate.", "tokens": [51292, 400, 456, 311, 257, 5994, 8203, 281, 577, 436, 9651, 13, 51413], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19605643660933883, "compression_ratio": 1.6701030927835052, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013931496306922e-12}, {"id": 916, "seek": 306758, "start": 3088.7599999999998, "end": 3090.7999999999997, "text": " The twist is what happens mechanically", "tokens": [51424, 440, 8203, 307, 437, 2314, 4236, 984, 51526], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19605643660933883, "compression_ratio": 1.6701030927835052, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013931496306922e-12}, {"id": 917, "seek": 306758, "start": 3090.7999999999997, "end": 3093.12, "text": " when a camera looks at a region of high entropy,", "tokens": [51526, 562, 257, 2799, 1542, 412, 257, 4458, 295, 1090, 30867, 11, 51642], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19605643660933883, "compression_ratio": 1.6701030927835052, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013931496306922e-12}, {"id": 918, "seek": 306758, "start": 3093.12, "end": 3095.04, "text": " a place that hasn't been observed yet.", "tokens": [51642, 257, 1081, 300, 6132, 380, 668, 13095, 1939, 13, 51738], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19605643660933883, "compression_ratio": 1.6701030927835052, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013931496306922e-12}, {"id": 919, "seek": 306758, "start": 3095.4, "end": 3095.52, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51756, 1779, 13, 51762], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19605643660933883, "compression_ratio": 1.6701030927835052, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013931496306922e-12}, {"id": 920, "seek": 309552, "start": 3095.52, "end": 3100.48, "text": " If I turn my in-game camera to look at a dark, unexplored corner of the map,", "tokens": [50365, 759, 286, 1261, 452, 294, 12, 15038, 2799, 281, 574, 412, 257, 2877, 11, 11572, 564, 2769, 4538, 295, 264, 4471, 11, 50613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1626377774958025, "compression_ratio": 1.6074380165289257, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298397093744699e-12}, {"id": 921, "seek": 309552, "start": 3101.2, "end": 3102.7, "text": " what is actually happening in the code?", "tokens": [50649, 437, 307, 767, 2737, 294, 264, 3089, 30, 50724], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1626377774958025, "compression_ratio": 1.6074380165289257, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298397093744699e-12}, {"id": 922, "seek": 309552, "start": 3103.12, "end": 3107.9, "text": " Well, the act of rendering a frame to a screen is normally a pure read operation.", "tokens": [50745, 1042, 11, 264, 605, 295, 22407, 257, 3920, 281, 257, 2568, 307, 5646, 257, 6075, 1401, 6916, 13, 50984], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1626377774958025, "compression_ratio": 1.6074380165289257, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298397093744699e-12}, {"id": 923, "seek": 309552, "start": 3108.32, "end": 3108.5, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51005, 1779, 13, 51014], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1626377774958025, "compression_ratio": 1.6074380165289257, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298397093744699e-12}, {"id": 924, "seek": 309552, "start": 3108.68, "end": 3110.08, "text": " You pull data and display it.", "tokens": [51023, 509, 2235, 1412, 293, 4674, 309, 13, 51093], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1626377774958025, "compression_ratio": 1.6074380165289257, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298397093744699e-12}, {"id": 925, "seek": 309552, "start": 3110.18, "end": 3110.38, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51098, 1779, 13, 51108], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1626377774958025, "compression_ratio": 1.6074380165289257, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298397093744699e-12}, {"id": 926, "seek": 309552, "start": 3110.48, "end": 3113.2599999999998, "text": " But if you look at an unresolved high entropy region,", "tokens": [51113, 583, 498, 291, 574, 412, 364, 517, 495, 29110, 1090, 30867, 4458, 11, 51252], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1626377774958025, "compression_ratio": 1.6074380165289257, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298397093744699e-12}, {"id": 927, "seek": 309552, "start": 3113.74, "end": 3116.58, "text": " the act of rendering becomes a write operation.", "tokens": [51276, 264, 605, 295, 22407, 3643, 257, 2464, 6916, 13, 51418], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1626377774958025, "compression_ratio": 1.6074380165289257, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298397093744699e-12}, {"id": 928, "seek": 309552, "start": 3116.92, "end": 3118.6, "text": " Wait, I want to make sure I'm grasping this.", "tokens": [51435, 3802, 11, 286, 528, 281, 652, 988, 286, 478, 29444, 3381, 341, 13, 51519], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1626377774958025, "compression_ratio": 1.6074380165289257, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298397093744699e-12}, {"id": 929, "seek": 311860, "start": 3118.6, "end": 3124.16, "text": " The physical act of my camera looking at something writes that thing into existence.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 4001, 605, 295, 452, 2799, 1237, 412, 746, 13657, 300, 551, 666, 9123, 13, 50643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19243523244107708, "compression_ratio": 1.5392156862745099, "no_speech_prob": 1.2397426835120129e-12}, {"id": 930, "seek": 311860, "start": 3124.48, "end": 3124.7, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50659, 1079, 13, 50670], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19243523244107708, "compression_ratio": 1.5392156862745099, "no_speech_prob": 1.2397426835120129e-12}, {"id": 931, "seek": 311860, "start": 3125.1, "end": 3126.18, "text": " Follow the chain of events.", "tokens": [50690, 9876, 264, 5021, 295, 3931, 13, 50744], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19243523244107708, "compression_ratio": 1.5392156862745099, "no_speech_prob": 1.2397426835120129e-12}, {"id": 932, "seek": 311860, "start": 3126.3399999999997, "end": 3126.56, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50752, 1033, 13, 50763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19243523244107708, "compression_ratio": 1.5392156862745099, "no_speech_prob": 1.2397426835120129e-12}, {"id": 933, "seek": 311860, "start": 3126.7599999999998, "end": 3128.92, "text": " The camera queries the database for the visual data.", "tokens": [50773, 440, 2799, 24109, 264, 8149, 337, 264, 5056, 1412, 13, 50881], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19243523244107708, "compression_ratio": 1.5392156862745099, "no_speech_prob": 1.2397426835120129e-12}, {"id": 934, "seek": 311860, "start": 3129.2999999999997, "end": 3131.22, "text": " The database checks the coordinate and says,", "tokens": [50900, 440, 8149, 13834, 264, 15670, 293, 1619, 11, 50996], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19243523244107708, "compression_ratio": 1.5392156862745099, "no_speech_prob": 1.2397426835120129e-12}, {"id": 935, "seek": 311860, "start": 3131.3399999999997, "end": 3132.56, "text": " I have high entropy here.", "tokens": [51002, 286, 362, 1090, 30867, 510, 13, 51063], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19243523244107708, "compression_ratio": 1.5392156862745099, "no_speech_prob": 1.2397426835120129e-12}, {"id": 936, "seek": 311860, "start": 3132.64, "end": 3134.08, "text": " I don't know what this looks like yet.", "tokens": [51067, 286, 500, 380, 458, 437, 341, 1542, 411, 1939, 13, 51139], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19243523244107708, "compression_ratio": 1.5392156862745099, "no_speech_prob": 1.2397426835120129e-12}, {"id": 937, "seek": 311860, "start": 3134.22, "end": 3134.46, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51146, 1033, 13, 51158], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19243523244107708, "compression_ratio": 1.5392156862745099, "no_speech_prob": 1.2397426835120129e-12}, {"id": 938, "seek": 311860, "start": 3134.54, "end": 3135.54, "text": " It hits a blank spot.", "tokens": [51162, 467, 8664, 257, 8247, 4008, 13, 51212], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19243523244107708, "compression_ratio": 1.5392156862745099, "no_speech_prob": 1.2397426835120129e-12}, {"id": 939, "seek": 313554, "start": 3135.54, "end": 3139.72, "text": " This triggers a specialized neural network called an invase renderer.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 22827, 257, 19813, 18161, 3209, 1219, 364, 1048, 651, 15529, 260, 13, 50574], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1966346182474276, "compression_ratio": 1.6441441441441442, "no_speech_prob": 1.6356124354216517e-12}, {"id": 940, "seek": 313554, "start": 3140.2599999999998, "end": 3145.66, "text": " The inverse renderer invents a plausible candidate appearance based on the surrounding context.", "tokens": [50601, 440, 17340, 15529, 260, 1048, 791, 257, 39925, 11532, 8967, 2361, 322, 264, 11498, 4319, 13, 50871], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1966346182474276, "compression_ratio": 1.6441441441441442, "no_speech_prob": 1.6356124354216517e-12}, {"id": 941, "seek": 313554, "start": 3146.32, "end": 3147.0, "text": " It makes a guess.", "tokens": [50904, 467, 1669, 257, 2041, 13, 50938], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1966346182474276, "compression_ratio": 1.6441441441441442, "no_speech_prob": 1.6356124354216517e-12}, {"id": 942, "seek": 313554, "start": 3147.22, "end": 3149.6, "text": " It submits that candidate to the constraint projector.", "tokens": [50949, 467, 8286, 1208, 300, 11532, 281, 264, 25534, 39792, 13, 51068], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1966346182474276, "compression_ratio": 1.6441441441441442, "no_speech_prob": 1.6356124354216517e-12}, {"id": 943, "seek": 313554, "start": 3149.92, "end": 3155.52, "text": " The projector checks it against the spatial sheaves, the temporal conservation laws, and the local residue.", "tokens": [51084, 440, 39792, 13834, 309, 1970, 264, 23598, 750, 5423, 11, 264, 30881, 16185, 6064, 11, 293, 264, 2654, 34799, 13, 51364], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1966346182474276, "compression_ratio": 1.6441441441441442, "no_speech_prob": 1.6356124354216517e-12}, {"id": 944, "seek": 313554, "start": 3155.72, "end": 3156.48, "text": " The immune system.", "tokens": [51374, 440, 11992, 1185, 13, 51412], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1966346182474276, "compression_ratio": 1.6441441441441442, "no_speech_prob": 1.6356124354216517e-12}, {"id": 945, "seek": 315648, "start": 3156.48, "end": 3157.04, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50393], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15234690514680382, "compression_ratio": 1.6484375, "no_speech_prob": 1.8542823526646046e-12}, {"id": 946, "seek": 315648, "start": 3157.18, "end": 3161.52, "text": " If it passes, it commits it to the database as hard, unchangeable reality.", "tokens": [50400, 759, 309, 11335, 11, 309, 48311, 309, 281, 264, 8149, 382, 1152, 11, 517, 15431, 712, 4103, 13, 50617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15234690514680382, "compression_ratio": 1.6484375, "no_speech_prob": 1.8542823526646046e-12}, {"id": 947, "seek": 315648, "start": 3161.9, "end": 3162.78, "text": " And then...", "tokens": [50636, 400, 550, 485, 50680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15234690514680382, "compression_ratio": 1.6484375, "no_speech_prob": 1.8542823526646046e-12}, {"id": 948, "seek": 315648, "start": 3162.78, "end": 3169.82, "text": " And then, only after all of that math has settled, does the renderer decode the data and show it to your screen.", "tokens": [50680, 400, 550, 11, 787, 934, 439, 295, 300, 5221, 575, 14819, 11, 775, 264, 15529, 260, 979, 1429, 264, 1412, 293, 855, 309, 281, 428, 2568, 13, 51032], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15234690514680382, "compression_ratio": 1.6484375, "no_speech_prob": 1.8542823526646046e-12}, {"id": 949, "seek": 315648, "start": 3170.04, "end": 3176.16, "text": " So my eyeballs are literally forcing the mathematics to collapse probability into hard drive sectors.", "tokens": [51043, 407, 452, 43758, 366, 3736, 19030, 264, 18666, 281, 15584, 8482, 666, 1152, 3332, 18373, 13, 51349], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15234690514680382, "compression_ratio": 1.6484375, "no_speech_prob": 1.8542823526646046e-12}, {"id": 950, "seek": 315648, "start": 3176.88, "end": 3177.8, "text": " That is wild.", "tokens": [51385, 663, 307, 4868, 13, 51431], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15234690514680382, "compression_ratio": 1.6484375, "no_speech_prob": 1.8542823526646046e-12}, {"id": 951, "seek": 315648, "start": 3178.1, "end": 3182.22, "text": " And it completely changes the philosophy of what level of detail means.", "tokens": [51446, 400, 309, 2584, 2962, 264, 10675, 295, 437, 1496, 295, 2607, 1355, 13, 51652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15234690514680382, "compression_ratio": 1.6484375, "no_speech_prob": 1.8542823526646046e-12}, {"id": 952, "seek": 315648, "start": 3182.28, "end": 3184.14, "text": " It completely redefines it.", "tokens": [51655, 467, 2584, 38818, 1652, 309, 13, 51748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15234690514680382, "compression_ratio": 1.6484375, "no_speech_prob": 1.8542823526646046e-12}, {"id": 953, "seek": 318414, "start": 3184.14, "end": 3193.24, "text": " Because in traditional games, if a mountain is far away, the engine renders it as a blurry, low-polygon shape just to save processing power.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 294, 5164, 2813, 11, 498, 257, 6937, 307, 1400, 1314, 11, 264, 2848, 6125, 433, 309, 382, 257, 37644, 11, 2295, 12, 2259, 356, 10660, 3909, 445, 281, 3155, 9007, 1347, 13, 50820], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09082822718171991, "compression_ratio": 1.7147887323943662, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043251796493685e-12}, {"id": 954, "seek": 318414, "start": 3193.58, "end": 3194.52, "text": " It was a fake trick.", "tokens": [50837, 467, 390, 257, 7592, 4282, 13, 50884], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09082822718171991, "compression_ratio": 1.7147887323943662, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043251796493685e-12}, {"id": 955, "seek": 318414, "start": 3194.64, "end": 3199.46, "text": " But in the semantic engine, a lower level of detail in the distance isn't a performance trick anymore.", "tokens": [50890, 583, 294, 264, 47982, 2848, 11, 257, 3126, 1496, 295, 2607, 294, 264, 4560, 1943, 380, 257, 3389, 4282, 3602, 13, 51131], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09082822718171991, "compression_ratio": 1.7147887323943662, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043251796493685e-12}, {"id": 956, "seek": 318414, "start": 3199.8599999999997, "end": 3202.7599999999998, "text": " It represents honest, mathematical uncertainty.", "tokens": [51151, 467, 8855, 3245, 11, 18894, 15697, 13, 51296], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09082822718171991, "compression_ratio": 1.7147887323943662, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043251796493685e-12}, {"id": 957, "seek": 318414, "start": 3203.22, "end": 3204.8799999999997, "text": " It's just blurry because it's uncertain.", "tokens": [51319, 467, 311, 445, 37644, 570, 309, 311, 11308, 13, 51402], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09082822718171991, "compression_ratio": 1.7147887323943662, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043251796493685e-12}, {"id": 958, "seek": 318414, "start": 3204.8799999999997, "end": 3212.2, "text": " If a distant wall is rendered coarsely with blurry textures, it is because the system genuinely hasn't resolved the fine details yet.", "tokens": [51402, 759, 257, 17275, 2929, 307, 28748, 598, 685, 736, 365, 37644, 24501, 11, 309, 307, 570, 264, 1185, 17839, 6132, 380, 20772, 264, 2489, 4365, 1939, 13, 51768], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09082822718171991, "compression_ratio": 1.7147887323943662, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043251796493685e-12}, {"id": 959, "seek": 321220, "start": 3212.2, "end": 3215.64, "text": " It is an accurate visual reflection of the field's high entropy.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 364, 8559, 5056, 12914, 295, 264, 2519, 311, 1090, 30867, 13, 50537], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1559435286611881, "compression_ratio": 1.4233128834355828, "no_speech_prob": 1.5549665504863142e-12}, {"id": 960, "seek": 321220, "start": 3215.8599999999997, "end": 3215.96, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50548, 3153, 13, 50553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1559435286611881, "compression_ratio": 1.4233128834355828, "no_speech_prob": 1.5549665504863142e-12}, {"id": 961, "seek": 321220, "start": 3216.3599999999997, "end": 3224.7, "text": " If you walk closer, your proximity forces the system to do the computational work of resolving it, committing the moss and the cracks to the database permanently.", "tokens": [50573, 759, 291, 1792, 4966, 11, 428, 27632, 5874, 264, 1185, 281, 360, 264, 28270, 589, 295, 49940, 309, 11, 26659, 264, 36193, 293, 264, 21770, 281, 264, 8149, 24042, 13, 50990], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1559435286611881, "compression_ratio": 1.4233128834355828, "no_speech_prob": 1.5549665504863142e-12}, {"id": 962, "seek": 322470, "start": 3224.7, "end": 3227.2599999999998, "text": " It is not a blurry JPEG to save RAM.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 406, 257, 37644, 508, 5208, 38, 281, 3155, 14561, 13, 50493], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11160391757362767, "compression_ratio": 1.5151515151515151, "no_speech_prob": 1.483759079143332e-12}, {"id": 963, "seek": 322470, "start": 3227.58, "end": 3233.24, "text": " It is a literal cloud of quantum probability waiting for my observation to force a collapse.", "tokens": [50509, 467, 307, 257, 20411, 4588, 295, 13018, 8482, 3806, 337, 452, 14816, 281, 3464, 257, 15584, 13, 50792], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11160391757362767, "compression_ratio": 1.5151515151515151, "no_speech_prob": 1.483759079143332e-12}, {"id": 964, "seek": 322470, "start": 3234.1, "end": 3238.2599999999998, "text": " We have covered an incredible, massive amount of theoretical ground today.", "tokens": [50835, 492, 362, 5343, 364, 4651, 11, 5994, 2372, 295, 20864, 2727, 965, 13, 51043], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11160391757362767, "compression_ratio": 1.5151515151515151, "no_speech_prob": 1.483759079143332e-12}, {"id": 965, "seek": 322470, "start": 3238.62, "end": 3241.6, "text": " Let's just briefly trace the arc of this journey.", "tokens": [51061, 961, 311, 445, 10515, 13508, 264, 10346, 295, 341, 4671, 13, 51210], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11160391757362767, "compression_ratio": 1.5151515151515151, "no_speech_prob": 1.483759079143332e-12}, {"id": 966, "seek": 322470, "start": 3241.68, "end": 3242.72, "text": " It's been a long journey.", "tokens": [51214, 467, 311, 668, 257, 938, 4671, 13, 51266], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11160391757362767, "compression_ratio": 1.5151515151515151, "no_speech_prob": 1.483759079143332e-12}, {"id": 967, "seek": 322470, "start": 3242.9199999999996, "end": 3248.9399999999996, "text": " We started with the problem of shifting AI walls and the fundamental failure of context buffers and document databases.", "tokens": [51276, 492, 1409, 365, 264, 1154, 295, 17573, 7318, 7920, 293, 264, 8088, 7763, 295, 4319, 9204, 433, 293, 4166, 22380, 13, 51577], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11160391757362767, "compression_ratio": 1.5151515151515151, "no_speech_prob": 1.483759079143332e-12}, {"id": 968, "seek": 324894, "start": 3248.94, "end": 3258.52, "text": " We threw out discrete objects and replaced them with continuous semantic fields governed by coherence, flow, entropy, residue, and appearance.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 11918, 484, 27706, 6565, 293, 10772, 552, 365, 10957, 47982, 7909, 35529, 538, 26528, 655, 11, 3095, 11, 30867, 11, 34799, 11, 293, 8967, 13, 50844], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10141486922899882, "compression_ratio": 1.5949820788530467, "no_speech_prob": 1.84654028179132e-12}, {"id": 969, "seek": 324894, "start": 3258.64, "end": 3259.48, "text": " The five components.", "tokens": [50850, 440, 1732, 6677, 13, 50892], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10141486922899882, "compression_ratio": 1.5949820788530467, "no_speech_prob": 1.84654028179132e-12}, {"id": 970, "seek": 324894, "start": 3259.76, "end": 3267.44, "text": " We learned how constraint projection forces AI hallucinations to bend to reality and how no other's conservation laws catch temporal lies.", "tokens": [50906, 492, 3264, 577, 25534, 22743, 5874, 7318, 35212, 10325, 281, 11229, 281, 4103, 293, 577, 572, 661, 311, 16185, 6064, 3745, 30881, 9134, 13, 51290], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10141486922899882, "compression_ratio": 1.5949820788530467, "no_speech_prob": 1.84654028179132e-12}, {"id": 971, "seek": 324894, "start": 3267.54, "end": 3268.34, "text": " The three lies.", "tokens": [51295, 440, 1045, 9134, 13, 51335], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10141486922899882, "compression_ratio": 1.5949820788530467, "no_speech_prob": 1.84654028179132e-12}, {"id": 972, "seek": 324894, "start": 3268.54, "end": 3274.94, "text": " And finally, we saw how octrees, Hilbert curves, and inverse rendering make this world engine computationally possible to run.", "tokens": [51345, 400, 2721, 11, 321, 1866, 577, 13350, 4856, 11, 19914, 4290, 19490, 11, 293, 17340, 22407, 652, 341, 1002, 2848, 24903, 379, 1944, 281, 1190, 13, 51665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10141486922899882, "compression_ratio": 1.5949820788530467, "no_speech_prob": 1.84654028179132e-12}, {"id": 973, "seek": 327494, "start": 3274.94, "end": 3279.88, "text": " We have outlined the blueprint for forcing artificial intelligence to respect physical reality.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 362, 27412, 264, 35868, 337, 19030, 11677, 7599, 281, 3104, 4001, 4103, 13, 50612], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10270388408373761, "compression_ratio": 1.6193771626297577, "no_speech_prob": 1.783201190874717e-12}, {"id": 974, "seek": 327494, "start": 3280.16, "end": 3282.58, "text": " It represents a profound architectural shift.", "tokens": [50626, 467, 8855, 257, 14382, 26621, 5513, 13, 50747], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10270388408373761, "compression_ratio": 1.6193771626297577, "no_speech_prob": 1.783201190874717e-12}, {"id": 975, "seek": 327494, "start": 3283.12, "end": 3291.38, "text": " We are moving away from systems designed to generate plausible, momentary illusions and moving toward systems capable of sustaining persistent, verifiable truths.", "tokens": [50774, 492, 366, 2684, 1314, 490, 3652, 4761, 281, 8460, 39925, 11, 1623, 822, 49836, 293, 2684, 7361, 3652, 8189, 295, 49097, 24315, 11, 1306, 30876, 30079, 13, 51187], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10270388408373761, "compression_ratio": 1.6193771626297577, "no_speech_prob": 1.783201190874717e-12}, {"id": 976, "seek": 327494, "start": 3291.66, "end": 3295.36, "text": " And that leads me to one final, deeply provocative thought for you listening today.", "tokens": [51201, 400, 300, 6689, 385, 281, 472, 2572, 11, 8760, 47663, 1194, 337, 291, 4764, 965, 13, 51386], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10270388408373761, "compression_ratio": 1.6193771626297577, "no_speech_prob": 1.783201190874717e-12}, {"id": 977, "seek": 327494, "start": 3295.94, "end": 3300.2200000000003, "text": " It is an extrapolation based strictly on the final chapters of Fliction's text.", "tokens": [51415, 467, 307, 364, 48224, 399, 2361, 20792, 322, 264, 2572, 20013, 295, 3235, 4105, 311, 2487, 13, 51629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10270388408373761, "compression_ratio": 1.6193771626297577, "no_speech_prob": 1.783201190874717e-12}, {"id": 978, "seek": 330022, "start": 3300.22, "end": 3306.8399999999997, "text": " We spent this entire hour talking about video game walls and courtyards and simulated water fountains.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 4418, 341, 2302, 1773, 1417, 466, 960, 1216, 7920, 293, 1005, 874, 2287, 293, 41713, 1281, 283, 792, 2315, 13, 50696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15807211704743215, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924176020314933e-12}, {"id": 979, "seek": 330022, "start": 3307.0, "end": 3308.22, "text": " The physical spaces.", "tokens": [50704, 440, 4001, 7673, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15807211704743215, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924176020314933e-12}, {"id": 980, "seek": 330022, "start": 3308.5, "end": 3308.68, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50779, 1779, 13, 50788], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15807211704743215, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924176020314933e-12}, {"id": 981, "seek": 330022, "start": 3308.7999999999997, "end": 3316.7, "text": " But the text explicitly outlines using this exact same mathematical architecture for something it calls civilization engines.", "tokens": [50794, 583, 264, 2487, 20803, 40125, 1228, 341, 1900, 912, 18894, 9482, 337, 746, 309, 5498, 18036, 12982, 13, 51189], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15807211704743215, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924176020314933e-12}, {"id": 982, "seek": 330022, "start": 3316.8199999999997, "end": 3317.1, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51195, 1079, 13, 51209], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15807211704743215, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924176020314933e-12}, {"id": 983, "seek": 330022, "start": 3317.3599999999997, "end": 3321.62, "text": " Taking the physics of the courtyard and applying them directly to the dynamics of human societies.", "tokens": [51222, 17837, 264, 10649, 295, 264, 41364, 293, 9275, 552, 3838, 281, 264, 15679, 295, 1952, 19329, 13, 51435], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15807211704743215, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924176020314933e-12}, {"id": 984, "seek": 332162, "start": 3321.62, "end": 3330.5, "text": " If you apply this exact math to a simulation of a society, the text argues that human laws become admissibility constraints on the manifold.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 3079, 341, 1900, 5221, 281, 257, 16575, 295, 257, 4086, 11, 264, 2487, 38218, 300, 1952, 6064, 1813, 5910, 891, 2841, 18491, 322, 264, 47138, 13, 50809], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11066426935884141, "compression_ratio": 1.737037037037037, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420326450083405e-12}, {"id": 985, "seek": 332162, "start": 3330.94, "end": 3332.62, "text": " Just like the bedrock constraints.", "tokens": [50831, 1449, 411, 264, 2901, 17799, 18491, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11066426935884141, "compression_ratio": 1.737037037037037, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420326450083405e-12}, {"id": 986, "seek": 332162, "start": 3332.7599999999998, "end": 3337.8399999999997, "text": " Human institutions, like a court system or a university, become dynamic fixed points.", "tokens": [50922, 10294, 8142, 11, 411, 257, 4753, 1185, 420, 257, 5454, 11, 1813, 8546, 6806, 2793, 13, 51176], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11066426935884141, "compression_ratio": 1.737037037037037, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420326450083405e-12}, {"id": 987, "seek": 332162, "start": 3338.2999999999997, "end": 3348.6, "text": " Just like the stone fountain, these institutions survive the fast clock chaos of daily human proposals by constantly projecting those actions against slow clock structural coherence.", "tokens": [51199, 1449, 411, 264, 7581, 29451, 11, 613, 8142, 7867, 264, 2370, 7830, 14158, 295, 5212, 1952, 20198, 538, 6460, 43001, 729, 5909, 1970, 2964, 7830, 15067, 26528, 655, 13, 51714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11066426935884141, "compression_ratio": 1.737037037037037, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420326450083405e-12}, {"id": 988, "seek": 332162, "start": 3348.66, "end": 3349.66, "text": " It scales up vertically.", "tokens": [51717, 467, 17408, 493, 28450, 13, 51767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11066426935884141, "compression_ratio": 1.737037037037037, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420326450083405e-12}, {"id": 989, "seek": 334966, "start": 3349.66, "end": 3353.2799999999997, "text": " And money in this system becomes conserved semantic residue.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 1460, 294, 341, 1185, 3643, 1014, 6913, 47982, 34799, 13, 50546], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12188814974379265, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.7216142790890676e-12}, {"id": 990, "seek": 334966, "start": 3353.7, "end": 3355.3599999999997, "text": " The mapping is mathematically perfect.", "tokens": [50567, 440, 18350, 307, 44003, 2176, 13, 50650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12188814974379265, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.7216142790890676e-12}, {"id": 991, "seek": 334966, "start": 3356.08, "end": 3368.14, "text": " The exact same variational dynamics and constraint equations that keep a stone wall from mutating into a tree can be used to keep a simulated economic system from violating the conservation of value.", "tokens": [50686, 440, 1900, 912, 3034, 1478, 15679, 293, 25534, 11787, 300, 1066, 257, 7581, 2929, 490, 5839, 990, 666, 257, 4230, 393, 312, 1143, 281, 1066, 257, 41713, 4836, 1185, 490, 42201, 264, 16185, 295, 2158, 13, 51289], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12188814974379265, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.7216142790890676e-12}, {"id": 992, "seek": 334966, "start": 3368.2999999999997, "end": 3372.48, "text": " So here is the thought I want to leave you with to mull over on your own time.", "tokens": [51297, 407, 510, 307, 264, 1194, 286, 528, 281, 1856, 291, 365, 281, 275, 858, 670, 322, 428, 1065, 565, 13, 51506], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12188814974379265, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.7216142790890676e-12}, {"id": 993, "seek": 334966, "start": 3372.6, "end": 3372.8399999999997, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51512, 1033, 13, 51524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12188814974379265, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.7216142790890676e-12}, {"id": 994, "seek": 337284, "start": 3372.84, "end": 3397.88, "text": " If an artificial intelligence can perfectly simulate the physics, the economics, and the institutions of a civilization using these unbreakable rules, if it can flawlessly project our proposals, conserve our historical residue, and maintain our dynamic fixed points with mathematical absolute certainty, at what point does the semantic field stop being a simulation and start being a reality?", "tokens": [50365, 759, 364, 11677, 7599, 393, 6239, 27817, 264, 10649, 11, 264, 14564, 11, 293, 264, 8142, 295, 257, 18036, 1228, 613, 517, 13225, 712, 4474, 11, 498, 309, 393, 13717, 12048, 1716, 527, 20198, 11, 45240, 527, 8584, 34799, 11, 293, 6909, 527, 8546, 6806, 2793, 365, 18894, 8236, 27022, 11, 412, 437, 935, 775, 264, 47982, 2519, 1590, 885, 257, 16575, 293, 722, 885, 257, 4103, 30, 51617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06655825508965386, "compression_ratio": 1.6540084388185654, "no_speech_prob": 1.8835005170109165e-12}, {"id": 995, "seek": 339788, "start": 3397.88, "end": 3405.1600000000003, "text": " Well, if the underlying math holds perfectly and the temporal history is uncompromised, there might not be a functional difference.", "tokens": [50365, 1042, 11, 498, 264, 14217, 5221, 9190, 6239, 293, 264, 30881, 2503, 307, 8585, 28722, 2640, 11, 456, 1062, 406, 312, 257, 11745, 2649, 13, 50729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09349094931759051, "compression_ratio": 1.4948979591836735, "no_speech_prob": 1.5977273757489252e-12}, {"id": 996, "seek": 339788, "start": 3405.58, "end": 3407.26, "text": " Thank you so much for joining us in this deep dive.", "tokens": [50750, 1044, 291, 370, 709, 337, 5549, 505, 294, 341, 2452, 9192, 13, 50834], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09349094931759051, "compression_ratio": 1.4948979591836735, "no_speech_prob": 1.5977273757489252e-12}, {"id": 997, "seek": 339788, "start": 3407.38, "end": 3411.04, "text": " Keep questioning the buffer and keep looking for the dynamic fixed points in your own world.", "tokens": [50840, 5527, 21257, 264, 21762, 293, 1066, 1237, 337, 264, 8546, 6806, 2793, 294, 428, 1065, 1002, 13, 51023], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09349094931759051, "compression_ratio": 1.4948979591836735, "no_speech_prob": 1.5977273757489252e-12}, {"id": 998, "seek": 339788, "start": 3411.58, "end": 3412.28, "text": " Until next time.", "tokens": [51050, 9088, 958, 565, 13, 51085], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09349094931759051, "compression_ratio": 1.4948979591836735, "no_speech_prob": 1.5977273757489252e-12}], "language": "en"}
